WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.347 --> 00:00:04.349
[waves crashing]

2
00:00:33.684 --> 00:00:35.978
[engine revving]

3
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:52.035
[knocking on door]

4
00:00:55.247 --> 00:00:57.124
Hey. Sonny. Five minutes.

5
00:01:02.421 --> 00:01:04.923
["Whole Lotta Love" playing]

6
00:01:13.307 --> 00:01:14.807
<i>♪ You need coolin' ♪</i>

7
00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:16.309
[grunts]

8
00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:17.936
<i>♪ Baby. I'm not foolin' ♪</i>

9
00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:23.483
<i>♪ I'm gonna send ya
Back to schoolin' ♪</i>

10
00:01:25.027 --> 00:01:29.907
<i>♪ Way down inside
Honey. you need it ♪</i>

11
00:01:30.616 --> 00:01:35.494
<i>♪ I'm gonna give you my love
I'm gonna give you my love ♪</i>

12
00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:37.663
[people chattering]

13
00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:41.501
<i>♪ Want a whole lotta love
Want a whole lotta love ♪</i>

14
00:01:42.461 --> 00:01:47.006
Sonny! Hey. BMW guys are over there
bitching about brake trouble.

15
00:01:47.007 --> 00:01:48.466
Thanks. Molly. You're a superstar.

16
00:01:48.467 --> 00:01:49.718
I'll see you out there.

17
00:01:51.136 --> 00:01:55.724
<i>♪ All the good times
Baby. baby. I've been yearning ♪</i>

18
00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:01.063
<i>♪ Way. way down inside
Honey. you need it ♪</i>

19
00:02:02.147 --> 00:02:07.277
<i>♪ I'm gonna give you my love ♪</i>

20
00:02:09.029 --> 00:02:11.489
<i>♪ Want a whole lotta love ♪</i>

21
00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:13.324
Turn my back for one minute.

22
00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:15.452
<i>♪ Want a whole lotta love ♪</i>

23
00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:18.829
It's all gone to shit. Sonny.

24
00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:20.206
Pat had to ease off.

25
00:02:20.207 --> 00:02:21.750
We've dropped down to seventh.

26
00:02:22.251 --> 00:02:26.755
If you can just hold position overnight.
hopeful sunrise catches us a break.

27
00:02:31.426 --> 00:02:35.347
Sonny. watch that high-speed balance.
High-speed balance.

28
00:02:37.933 --> 00:02:39.809
[drills whirring]

29
00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:41.060
How's the gearbox?

30
00:02:41.061 --> 00:02:42.396
It's holding up. but go easy.

31
00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:44.856
[breathing deeply]

32
00:02:46.567 --> 00:02:48.860
[breathing heavily]

33
00:03:02.207 --> 00:03:05.418
[commentator] <i>The crowds may
have gone home. but the racing continues.</i>

34
00:03:05.419 --> 00:03:08.963
<i>Sonny Hayes back in the Porsche
for Peak Geico Chip Hart Racing.</i>

35
00:03:08.964 --> 00:03:10.590
<i>the midnight shift.</i>

36
00:03:10.591 --> 00:03:12.091
<i>We all know Hayes</i>

37
00:03:12.092 --> 00:03:13.301
<i>likes to light up the night.</i>

38
00:03:13.302 --> 00:03:17.389
<i>but with the BMW at the head of this pack.
he's got a massive job ahead of him.</i>

39
00:03:29.735 --> 00:03:32.612
<i>Right out of the gate.
Hayes threads the needle into turn three.</i>

40
00:03:32.613 --> 00:03:33.738
<i>moving up to fourth place.</i>

41
00:03:33.739 --> 00:03:35.948
Sonny. wanna maybe pass on the straights?

42
00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:37.284
Just let me drive. will ya?

43
00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:40.828
[song continues]

44
00:03:40.829 --> 00:03:43.498
[commentator] <i>Look out.
Engine trouble for the number 12.</i>

45
00:03:46.168 --> 00:03:48.253
<i>That moves Hayes up another spot.</i>

46
00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:03.685
<i>♪ You've been coolin'
Baby. I've been droolin' ♪</i>

47
00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:06.772
Sweet baby Jesus. We got ten more hours.

48
00:04:07.356 --> 00:04:09.232
Just let Sonny do his thing.

49
00:04:09.233 --> 00:04:11.776
And if these first few laps
are any indication.

50
00:04:11.777 --> 00:04:15.321
it appears as though Sonny Hayes
may have left his brake pedal at home.

51
00:04:15.322 --> 00:04:17.990
<i>♪ I'm gonna give you
Every inch of my love ♪</i>

52
00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:20.326
<i>Hayes sets his sights on the BMW.</i>

53
00:04:20.327 --> 00:04:22.994
<i>♪ Yeah. all right. let's go ♪</i>

54
00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:24.664
- [grunts]
- [commentator] <i>And he attacks.</i>

55
00:04:24.665 --> 00:04:28.459
<i>♪ Want a whole lotta love
Want a whole lotta love ♪</i>

56
00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:30.670
[commentator]
<i>Here comes Hayes on the outside.</i>

57
00:04:30.671 --> 00:04:31.921
Come on. Sonny.

58
00:04:31.922 --> 00:04:33.924
<i>♪ Want a whole lotta love ♪</i>

59
00:04:36.343 --> 00:04:40.347
<i>♪ Way down inside ♪</i>

60
00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:45.184
[pants]

61
00:04:45.185 --> 00:04:51.441
<i>♪ Love ♪</i>

62
00:04:56.738 --> 00:05:00.533
<i>♪ My. my. my. my
My. my. my. my ♪</i>

63
00:05:00.534 --> 00:05:03.745
[commentator] <i>The BMW late on the brakes.
He's in the grass.</i>

64
00:05:08.458 --> 00:05:09.626
<i>Can Hayes hang on?</i>

65
00:05:11.211 --> 00:05:12.211
<i>And he does.</i>

66
00:05:12.212 --> 00:05:13.630
Goddamn!

67
00:05:14.298 --> 00:05:16.257
See that? That's how you race. boys.

68
00:05:16.258 --> 00:05:19.302
When you get back in that car.
you need to do the same goddamn thing.

69
00:05:19.303 --> 00:05:23.931
<i>♪ Hey. oh. ooh ♪</i>

70
00:05:23.932 --> 00:05:27.393
[commentator] <i>Sonny Hayes brings it
into pit lane after an epic third stint</i>

71
00:05:27.394 --> 00:05:29.771
<i>that puts Chip Hart Racing out in front.</i>

72
00:05:30.272 --> 00:05:33.065
<i>Now. it's up to Cale Kelso
to hang on to that lead.</i>

73
00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:34.818
[Kelso] Thanks for the head start. Chief.

74
00:05:38.113 --> 00:05:40.657
Hey. Lose that lead. I'll kill ya.

75
00:05:43.327 --> 00:05:48.372
<i>♪ Shake for me. girl
I wanna be your backdoor man ♪</i>

76
00:05:48.373 --> 00:05:49.625
[BMW driver] Hayes!

77
00:05:50.209 --> 00:05:51.585
Hey. dirtbag!

78
00:05:53.462 --> 00:05:56.005
- Gonna run me off the track. Hayes?
- [crew member] It's not worth it.

79
00:05:56.006 --> 00:05:59.760
You think I don't know where to find you?
Screw you!

80
00:06:01.261 --> 00:06:02.429
Let go of me!

81
00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:04.847
<i>♪ Oh. oh. oh ♪</i>

82
00:06:04.848 --> 00:06:06.350
Hey. Attaboy. Sonny.

83
00:06:07.392 --> 00:06:09.561
Thanks. Don't wake me if we lose.

84
00:06:10.103 --> 00:06:13.315
[crowd cheering]

85
00:06:13.982 --> 00:06:15.651
[laughs]

86
00:06:17.611 --> 00:06:19.320
[cheers]

87
00:06:19.321 --> 00:06:21.113
<i>♪ Keep it coolin'. baby ♪</i>

88
00:06:21.114 --> 00:06:22.741
[song fades]

89
00:06:24.535 --> 00:06:27.329
Sonny Hayes.
I believe you forgot something.

90
00:06:28.288 --> 00:06:29.414
Bag's full. Chip.

91
00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:31.291
Seriously?

92
00:06:31.959 --> 00:06:34.585
Your first win at Daytona.
Don't you even want to touch it?

93
00:06:34.586 --> 00:06:35.670
- Ooh. bad luck.
- Come on.

94
00:06:35.671 --> 00:06:37.673
- Just touch it.
- [laughing] No. Hey.

95
00:06:38.757 --> 00:06:40.842
I will take that bonus check though.

96
00:06:42.135 --> 00:06:46.306
Sonny. Sonny! Just hear me out.

97
00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:48.516
Look. I wanna bring you on board.

98
00:06:48.517 --> 00:06:50.017
- [laughs]
- You're CHR family now.

99
00:06:50.018 --> 00:06:51.894
Right here. next year. let's run it back.

100
00:06:51.895 --> 00:06:53.854
We did it. man. Deal's a deal.

101
00:06:53.855 --> 00:06:56.108
I-I know what a deal is.

102
00:06:57.651 --> 00:06:59.402
So that's it? One and done?

103
00:06:59.403 --> 00:07:02.071
I appreciate the seat. Chip. I really do.

104
00:07:02.072 --> 00:07:03.657
What kind of way is that to race?

105
00:07:04.157 --> 00:07:06.075
You just spend your whole life
starting over. man.

106
00:07:06.076 --> 00:07:07.160
You take care.

107
00:07:08.328 --> 00:07:10.247
- [engine starts]
- I'll see you down the road.

108
00:07:18.005 --> 00:07:20.131
Hey! Don't you want the watch?

109
00:07:20.132 --> 00:07:21.299
[Sonny] Got one!

110
00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:22.967
["Round and Round" playing on radio]

111
00:07:22.968 --> 00:07:24.802
[radio presenter 1]
<i>WHOG. Ormond-by-the-Sea.</i>

112
00:07:24.803 --> 00:07:26.220
[radio presenter 2]
<i>Proud to be locally owned.</i>

113
00:07:26.221 --> 00:07:27.763
<i>A Southern Stone station.</i>

114
00:07:27.764 --> 00:07:29.181
<i>The world's most famous rock...</i>

115
00:07:29.182 --> 00:07:32.476
[radio presenter 1] <i>...from the world's
most famous beach. we are...</i>

116
00:07:32.477 --> 00:07:34.270
[radio presenter 2]
<i>...Daytona's rock station...</i>

117
00:07:34.271 --> 00:07:36.189
[radio presenter 1]
<i>...ninety-five seven. the Hog.</i>

118
00:07:37.274 --> 00:07:40.902
<i>♪ Out on the streets
That's where we'll meet ♪</i>

119
00:07:40.903 --> 00:07:44.906
<i>♪ You make the night
I always cross the line ♪</i>

120
00:07:44.907 --> 00:07:48.284
<i>♪ Tightened our belts
Abused ourselves ♪</i>

121
00:07:48.285 --> 00:07:49.952
<i>♪ Get in our way
We'll put you on your shelf ♪</i>

122
00:07:49.953 --> 00:07:51.246
[timer buzzes]

123
00:07:52.164 --> 00:07:55.333
Sorry. can I use your phone
for a second. please?

124
00:07:55.334 --> 00:07:56.584
It's not working.

125
00:07:56.585 --> 00:07:58.503
Um. no.

126
00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:04.592
You know. you remind me of this friend
I used to have.

127
00:08:04.593 --> 00:08:05.677
Which friend?

128
00:08:06.178 --> 00:08:07.429
Friend who dressed better.

129
00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:10.056
This is a Gucci suit.

130
00:08:10.057 --> 00:08:11.265
So's this.

131
00:08:11.266 --> 00:08:13.267
Huh. What did your friend do?

132
00:08:13.268 --> 00:08:14.352
Drove cars.

133
00:08:14.353 --> 00:08:16.187
- Was he fast?
- Wasn't slow.

134
00:08:16.188 --> 00:08:19.316
- Did he win?
- [inhales sharply] Yeah. he did.

135
00:08:21.526 --> 00:08:23.861
- Come here. you son of a bitch.
- [laughs]

136
00:08:23.862 --> 00:08:24.946
Oh. God.

137
00:08:24.947 --> 00:08:26.739
[friend] Are you thinking Baja?

138
00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:28.908
[Sonny] Yeah. New day. new challenge.

139
00:08:28.909 --> 00:08:31.285
That's exactly what I said to myself
when I bought Apex GP.

140
00:08:31.286 --> 00:08:33.996
- ["The Stroke" playing on radio]
- [groans]

141
00:08:33.997 --> 00:08:35.541
How deep in the hole are you?

142
00:08:36.708 --> 00:08:39.086
I'll tell you.
but you have to promise not to laugh.

143
00:08:39.919 --> 00:08:40.962
Shoot.

144
00:08:42.713 --> 00:08:44.174
350...

145
00:08:45.676 --> 00:08:47.219
million.

146
00:08:49.638 --> 00:08:50.722
Don't laugh.

147
00:08:52.182 --> 00:08:53.350
Impressive.

148
00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:55.768
Well. been fun?

149
00:08:55.769 --> 00:08:58.020
Oh. yeah. Absolutely.

150
00:08:58.021 --> 00:08:59.272
What's the problem then?

151
00:08:59.273 --> 00:09:02.692
Problem is two seasons and a half.
zero points.

152
00:09:02.693 --> 00:09:04.902
My best driver left for another team.

153
00:09:04.903 --> 00:09:07.238
He said the car was a shitbox.

154
00:09:07.239 --> 00:09:08.322
[laughs]

155
00:09:08.323 --> 00:09:10.074
The team is in last place.

156
00:09:10.075 --> 00:09:11.702
My number two's a rookie.

157
00:09:12.202 --> 00:09:13.661
And the season's half over.

158
00:09:13.662 --> 00:09:15.289
- How many races left?
- Nine.

159
00:09:15.789 --> 00:09:17.748
And if we don't turn it around.
I lose the team.

160
00:09:17.749 --> 00:09:19.333
- What?
- Mmm.

161
00:09:19.334 --> 00:09:20.544
But you own the team.

162
00:09:21.169 --> 00:09:25.257
No race wins in your first three seasons.
the board can force a sale.

163
00:09:26.758 --> 00:09:28.677
Man. sounds like you need a new board.

164
00:09:30.304 --> 00:09:31.513
I need a new driver.

165
00:09:36.935 --> 00:09:39.313
[laughs]

166
00:09:40.272 --> 00:09:41.689
[Sonny] You got F2. You got F3.

167
00:09:41.690 --> 00:09:44.275
You got an entire assembly line of kids
raised on the simulator.

168
00:09:44.276 --> 00:09:47.486
No. I don't have time for some kid
to learn how to come in tenth. I don't.

169
00:09:47.487 --> 00:09:50.239
Well. you don't just walk off the street
and pilot a rocket.

170
00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:52.909
Yes. you can if you've done it before.
That's the whole point.

171
00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:57.038
Louis Chiron was 57 years old
when he won the Monaco Grand Prix.

172
00:09:57.039 --> 00:09:59.457
- Louis who?
- Philippe Étancelin. 56 years old.

173
00:09:59.458 --> 00:10:00.833
You just Googled these names. didn't you?

174
00:10:00.834 --> 00:10:04.545
Some people look at Sonny Hayes.
they see a guy who lives in a van.

175
00:10:04.546 --> 00:10:06.672
a gambling junkie who missed his shot.

176
00:10:06.673 --> 00:10:08.883
Wow. Ruben. you are really selling this.

177
00:10:08.884 --> 00:10:11.093
But I see a guy who makes teams better.

178
00:10:11.094 --> 00:10:13.179
- I see experience. I see know-how.
- Mmm.

179
00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:14.388
[laughs] You're off your meds.

180
00:10:14.389 --> 00:10:18.018
My rookie's a phenomenal talent.
Phenomenal. But he's young.

181
00:10:18.518 --> 00:10:19.978
You know what he lacks? Maturity.

182
00:10:20.729 --> 00:10:22.271
You plus him?

183
00:10:22.272 --> 00:10:24.523
Boom. I got a team.

184
00:10:24.524 --> 00:10:26.609
[Sonny]
All right. Let's say I'm the next Louis...

185
00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:28.528
- Chiron. Mm-hmm.
- Him.

186
00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:32.115
The problem is it's not just the driver.
it's the car.

187
00:10:32.866 --> 00:10:34.617
I've followed your season. Ruben.

188
00:10:34.618 --> 00:10:36.035
"Shitbox" is being kind.

189
00:10:36.036 --> 00:10:37.328
I knew you were watching.

190
00:10:37.329 --> 00:10:40.164
What if I told you
we get an upgrade package this weekend?

191
00:10:40.165 --> 00:10:42.041
- Six months in development--
- Ruben...

192
00:10:42.042 --> 00:10:43.251
No. no. no. Wait.

193
00:10:43.252 --> 00:10:47.464
I just need one of my cars
across the finish line first. One.

194
00:10:48.048 --> 00:10:50.008
I love ya. I'm not going back.

195
00:10:51.385 --> 00:10:52.511
[sighs]

196
00:10:54.137 --> 00:10:55.138
Okay.

197
00:10:58.642 --> 00:11:00.351
What would he want you to do?

198
00:11:00.352 --> 00:11:02.354
[chuckles]

199
00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:03.980
[Sonny] Join a boy band?

200
00:11:03.981 --> 00:11:05.607
Seriously. Come on.

201
00:11:07.776 --> 00:11:09.819
Seriously. I'd ask him
what he's smiling about.

202
00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:10.904
Come on.

203
00:11:11.905 --> 00:11:14.116
He's smiling at the possibility.

204
00:11:16.034 --> 00:11:17.536
We both know how that ended.

205
00:11:19.371 --> 00:11:20.372
Yep.

206
00:11:21.456 --> 00:11:22.457
Okay.

207
00:11:23.125 --> 00:11:26.586
- This is a first-class ticket to London.
- Oh. my God.

208
00:11:26.587 --> 00:11:27.879
First class.

209
00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:31.466
I'm offering you
an open seat in Formula 1.

210
00:11:32.426 --> 00:11:35.094
The only place you could say for one day.

211
00:11:35.095 --> 00:11:40.434
if you win.
you are the absolute best in the world.

212
00:11:50.485 --> 00:11:52.321
- Hey. Ruben.
- Mmm.

213
00:11:52.863 --> 00:11:54.823
- Ever seen a miracle?
- Not yet.

214
00:11:55.449 --> 00:11:56.533
Me neither.

215
00:11:57.576 --> 00:11:58.744
Good to see you. amigo.

216
00:12:00.954 --> 00:12:03.039
- All right. sweetie. here you go.
- Thank you.

217
00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:05.334
- Mm-hmm.
- Hey. let me ask you something.

218
00:12:07.586 --> 00:12:12.173
Close friend of yours made you an offer
that was 100%. positively

219
00:12:12.174 --> 00:12:13.508
too good to be true.

220
00:12:14.468 --> 00:12:15.468
What do you do?

221
00:12:15.469 --> 00:12:18.179
[sighs] Well. how much are we talking?

222
00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:19.640
Not about the money.

223
00:12:21.225 --> 00:12:22.726
So what is it about?

224
00:12:23.852 --> 00:12:24.937
Hmm.

225
00:12:36.198 --> 00:12:37.658
[engine revving]

226
00:12:55.509 --> 00:12:58.095
[driving synth music playing]

227
00:13:06.311 --> 00:13:09.188
[crew member] <i>Tire temps look good.
Eighty-five front. 75 rear.</i>

228
00:13:09.189 --> 00:13:11.567
- <i>You are good to push.</i>
- [driver] Copy.

229
00:13:20.492 --> 00:13:22.326
[crew member] <i>Battery is full.
You're good for strat two.</i>

230
00:13:22.327 --> 00:13:23.412
[driver] <i>Going for a lap.</i>

231
00:13:41.179 --> 00:13:43.390
Purple sector one. Best one yet.

232
00:13:44.057 --> 00:13:45.225
[driver] Car feels good.

233
00:14:20.135 --> 00:14:21.719
[tires squeal]

234
00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:22.846
Damn!

235
00:14:26.934 --> 00:14:28.936
Locked it up. Flat spot. front left.

236
00:14:34.691 --> 00:14:36.318
[sighs]

237
00:14:37.277 --> 00:14:38.361
Bring him in.

238
00:14:38.362 --> 00:14:39.820
Go to strat one.

239
00:14:39.821 --> 00:14:41.657
Uh. box this lap. Box this lap.

240
00:14:54.294 --> 00:14:56.797
- [groans]
- Let's go find those gremlins.

241
00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:16.733
[blows]

242
00:15:19.820 --> 00:15:22.322
[crew chattering]

243
00:15:23.949 --> 00:15:25.409
[groans]

244
00:15:32.541 --> 00:15:33.958
[grunts. gasps]

245
00:15:33.959 --> 00:15:35.294
Sorry. Joshua.

246
00:15:38.255 --> 00:15:40.340
Jodie. try not to kill our driver.

247
00:15:47.222 --> 00:15:48.973
What's the verdict? [sniffs]

248
00:15:48.974 --> 00:15:52.644
[sighs] I don't know what's happening.
I mean. it feels good. I start to push.

249
00:15:53.145 --> 00:15:55.521
Then it understeers in the slow corners
and oversteers the fast.

250
00:15:55.522 --> 00:15:57.148
What? On entries or exits?

251
00:15:57.149 --> 00:15:58.858
Either. Both.

252
00:15:58.859 --> 00:16:00.234
Oh. great. Yeah.

253
00:16:00.235 --> 00:16:03.112
There's 10.000 sensors on this thing
and you can't tell me what's going on.

254
00:16:03.113 --> 00:16:04.989
But I'm not out there. am I?

255
00:16:04.990 --> 00:16:07.993
So. I-I'm gonna need
your help on this. Please.

256
00:16:12.539 --> 00:16:15.292
[speaking German]

257
00:16:16.168 --> 00:16:17.419
[speaking German]

258
00:16:22.633 --> 00:16:24.550
[child giggles]

259
00:16:24.551 --> 00:16:27.221
[in English]
150 million dollar jungle gym.

260
00:16:27.846 --> 00:16:28.847
So cute.

261
00:16:29.473 --> 00:16:32.392
We should let her drive.
Can't be any worse.

262
00:16:33.143 --> 00:16:34.811
[child imitating engine]

263
00:16:35.479 --> 00:16:36.812
Joshua.

264
00:16:36.813 --> 00:16:39.148
- Hi.
- Lisbeth. PR?

265
00:16:39.149 --> 00:16:40.900
- Oh. yeah.
- Doesn't matter.

266
00:16:40.901 --> 00:16:43.611
For the press conference.
we want to steer around tech issues

267
00:16:43.612 --> 00:16:47.156
and focus on the super strong bond
with your new teammate. Luca Cortez.

268
00:16:47.157 --> 00:16:48.991
[laughs] Luca?

269
00:16:48.992 --> 00:16:50.494
Who I've known a week.

270
00:16:51.036 --> 00:16:53.162
Who when he was third banana
on the left at Red Bull.

271
00:16:53.163 --> 00:16:55.749
told the press he thought
Joshua Pearce was overrated.

272
00:16:56.792 --> 00:16:58.209
That Luca Cortez?

273
00:16:58.210 --> 00:16:59.752
Yes.

274
00:16:59.753 --> 00:17:02.964
- [chuckles] Can't wait. Yeah.
- All right. Great. Thank you.

275
00:17:02.965 --> 00:17:04.048
- Yo.
- Yep.

276
00:17:04.049 --> 00:17:06.342
That's a yes? Yeah? Yes? [groans]

277
00:17:06.343 --> 00:17:07.426
[Joshua] What's up?

278
00:17:07.427 --> 00:17:09.137
Yo. you were right. bro.

279
00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:12.139
Ruben's in big trouble.
He might have to sell the team.

280
00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:14.058
- [snaps fingers]
- I knew it.

281
00:17:14.059 --> 00:17:15.309
And what does that mean for me?

282
00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:17.771
New buyers. they're likely to clean house.

283
00:17:18.981 --> 00:17:19.982
Listen.

284
00:17:20.566 --> 00:17:24.653
You need to show these people
who the number one driver really is. man.

285
00:17:25.279 --> 00:17:26.280
Now.

286
00:17:27.948 --> 00:17:29.241
Or you're gonna lose your job.

287
00:17:29.782 --> 00:17:32.451
Yeah. Let that sink in.

288
00:17:32.452 --> 00:17:34.788
[speaking German]

289
00:17:35.581 --> 00:17:37.749
- [in English] Hey.
- [parent. speaking German]

290
00:17:38.959 --> 00:17:40.294
You good?

291
00:17:42.629 --> 00:17:46.883
Okay. let's take
the first half of the season

292
00:17:46.884 --> 00:17:48.968
and erase it from our minds.

293
00:17:48.969 --> 00:17:50.052
[crew cheers]

294
00:17:50.053 --> 00:17:52.347
Someone says.
"Kaspar. what happened this year?"

295
00:17:52.931 --> 00:17:56.976
I swear on the lives of my children.
I do not freaking know.

296
00:17:56.977 --> 00:17:58.394
[laughs]

297
00:17:58.395 --> 00:17:59.730
There's only this car.

298
00:18:00.314 --> 00:18:03.983
And there is only our future.

299
00:18:03.984 --> 00:18:06.862
[crew exclaiming] Yes. Our future.

300
00:18:15.871 --> 00:18:17.455
[Kaspar] Who is that asshole?

301
00:18:17.456 --> 00:18:18.540
He's with me.

302
00:18:19.458 --> 00:18:22.251
Your man thought I was maintenance.
Sent me to the back gate.

303
00:18:22.252 --> 00:18:23.712
[Ruben chuckles]

304
00:18:24.755 --> 00:18:26.172
Brother. you have never let me down.

305
00:18:26.173 --> 00:18:28.341
- [chuckles] Well. there's still time.
- [chuckles]

306
00:18:28.342 --> 00:18:30.009
Apex GP!

307
00:18:30.010 --> 00:18:32.553
Sonny Hayes.
He raced with me back in the day.

308
00:18:32.554 --> 00:18:34.388
- Against you. you mean.
- Yeah.

309
00:18:34.389 --> 00:18:36.933
- Kate McKenna. our technical director.
- Hi.

310
00:18:36.934 --> 00:18:39.936
- Dodge Dauda. our chief mechanic.
- Hi.

311
00:18:39.937 --> 00:18:42.188
And Kaspar Smolinski. team principal.

312
00:18:42.189 --> 00:18:43.814
You may know him by reputation.

313
00:18:43.815 --> 00:18:46.652
Five-time Constructors champion
with Ferrari.

314
00:18:47.194 --> 00:18:48.528
Huh.

315
00:18:49.279 --> 00:18:50.446
As a rear jack man.

316
00:18:50.447 --> 00:18:52.156
So was my pop. Can't win without 'em.

317
00:18:52.157 --> 00:18:55.118
- And our talented rookie. Joshua.
- Why has he got a helmet?

318
00:18:56.203 --> 00:18:58.079
- Uh. safety?
- [chuckles]

319
00:18:58.080 --> 00:19:00.540
Joshua. your seat is safe. Okay?

320
00:19:00.541 --> 00:19:02.543
Sonny is here for the audition.

321
00:19:04.962 --> 00:19:06.379
When was the last time you won a race?

322
00:19:06.380 --> 00:19:08.089
Sunday. Daytona.

323
00:19:08.090 --> 00:19:10.091
Oh. I'm sorry. I-I meant Formula 1.

324
00:19:10.092 --> 00:19:12.426
Oh. I'm sorry. Then same as you.

325
00:19:12.427 --> 00:19:15.513
- [laughs. exclaims] Wow.
- [chuckles]

326
00:19:15.514 --> 00:19:18.307
Never thought I'd say this.
has anyone seen Luca Cortez?

327
00:19:18.308 --> 00:19:20.434
- [chuckles]
- Sidebar <i>bitte</i>. Ruben.

328
00:19:20.435 --> 00:19:23.479
When I interview with you.
many veteran drivers--

329
00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:25.147
Yeah. who all turned you down.

330
00:19:25.148 --> 00:19:26.774
- How many?
- Seven.

331
00:19:26.775 --> 00:19:28.609
- That's a lot.
- I'm number seven?

332
00:19:28.610 --> 00:19:30.111
- Mm-hmm.
- You're eight.

333
00:19:30.112 --> 00:19:31.445
This is a disaster.

334
00:19:31.446 --> 00:19:32.822
Starting to feel more like a nine.

335
00:19:32.823 --> 00:19:34.615
Technically. there is one
who I've not heard from yet.

336
00:19:34.616 --> 00:19:35.825
- [stammers]
- So I am a nine?

337
00:19:35.826 --> 00:19:37.493
You know how numbers work. right?

338
00:19:37.494 --> 00:19:40.496
In business.
my most inspired ideas come late.

339
00:19:40.497 --> 00:19:43.124
Yeah. Best things in life
usually arrive ninth. right?

340
00:19:43.125 --> 00:19:46.627
With respect. Ruben. I cannot condone
we spend our only test day

341
00:19:46.628 --> 00:19:48.838
giving your long-lost teammate
an audition.

342
00:19:48.839 --> 00:19:50.256
Kaspar. you misunderstand.

343
00:19:50.257 --> 00:19:52.676
We're not auditioning him.
He's auditioning us.

344
00:19:54.094 --> 00:19:55.386
That's your new driver.

345
00:19:55.387 --> 00:19:56.555
Good luck.

346
00:19:59.725 --> 00:20:01.142
New wing. new side pods.

347
00:20:01.143 --> 00:20:02.644
Any changes to the floor?

348
00:20:03.812 --> 00:20:06.440
Nothing the eight other drivers
wouldn't have figured out.

349
00:20:07.316 --> 00:20:09.066
That's why they call me Lucky Number Nine.

350
00:20:09.067 --> 00:20:11.944
Listen. it's been a while
since you've driven here. mate. Yeah?

351
00:20:11.945 --> 00:20:14.281
The balance on these cars are tricky.
so be careful turn one and nine.

352
00:20:14.907 --> 00:20:16.158
Wouldn't want to see you get hurt.

353
00:20:17.534 --> 00:20:18.993
How about we set a reasonable target?

354
00:20:18.994 --> 00:20:22.663
Give me the same setup as him. If I can't
post a lap time within a second of JP's.

355
00:20:22.664 --> 00:20:24.416
then I will promptly see myself out

356
00:20:25.083 --> 00:20:27.043
and you're free to take a shot
at lucky number ten.

357
00:20:27.044 --> 00:20:28.837
- Ten?
- Ten.

358
00:20:29.546 --> 00:20:30.547
Ten.

359
00:20:32.758 --> 00:20:33.842
Who's JP?

360
00:20:35.177 --> 00:20:36.720
[rock music playing]

361
00:20:37.846 --> 00:20:40.556
Cross round on Brooklands.
easy on Luffield.

362
00:20:40.557 --> 00:20:42.808
Up to Woodcote. hard out in Copse.

363
00:20:42.809 --> 00:20:44.186
And be careful on the curve.

364
00:20:48.941 --> 00:20:51.902
Default mode. settings one. to two.
back to three.

365
00:20:52.527 --> 00:20:54.278
Differential one through four.

366
00:20:54.279 --> 00:20:55.656
DRS.

367
00:20:59.785 --> 00:21:03.579
<i>♪ I bet you thought
You'd seen the last of me ♪</i>

368
00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:07.124
<i>♪ I can't change the way I am. you see ♪</i>

369
00:21:07.125 --> 00:21:09.043
<i>♪ I think it's my responsibility ♪</i>

370
00:21:09.044 --> 00:21:10.628
[exhales deeply]

371
00:21:10.629 --> 00:21:14.340
<i>♪ To tell you
I'm just as bad as I used to be ♪</i>

372
00:21:14.341 --> 00:21:16.259
[engine starts. revs]

373
00:21:16.260 --> 00:21:19.179
<i>♪ I'm just as bad as I used to be ♪</i>

374
00:21:20.222 --> 00:21:21.598
[breathes deeply]

375
00:21:22.849 --> 00:21:24.935
Okay. Let's see what you got.

376
00:21:32.234 --> 00:21:37.406
If he raced with Ruben.
he raced with Schumacher. With Senna.

377
00:21:39.783 --> 00:21:43.161
<i>♪ I tried changing my reality ♪</i>

378
00:21:43.787 --> 00:21:46.790
<i>♪ But I don't think
It's gonna set me free ♪</i>

379
00:21:47.791 --> 00:21:50.585
<i>♪ There's only one thing I can guarantee ♪</i>

380
00:21:50.586 --> 00:21:55.048
<i>♪ And that's
I'm just as bad as I used to be ♪</i>

381
00:21:55.841 --> 00:21:58.552
<i>♪ I'm just as bad as I used to be ♪</i>

382
00:21:59.261 --> 00:22:02.723
<i>♪ I'm just as bad as I used to be ♪</i>

383
00:22:03.223 --> 00:22:07.393
<i>♪ I'm just as bad as I used to be ♪</i>

384
00:22:07.394 --> 00:22:09.271
All right. pull up Joshua's sector times.

385
00:22:19.072 --> 00:22:20.781
Twenty quid says he stacks it.

386
00:22:20.782 --> 00:22:22.492
Make it a hundred. you're on.

387
00:22:23.410 --> 00:22:24.660
Oh. shit.

388
00:22:24.661 --> 00:22:26.871
- [laughs]
- [laughs]

389
00:22:26.872 --> 00:22:30.124
Sorry. uh. this is Hugh Nickleby.
your race engineer.

390
00:22:30.125 --> 00:22:32.210
Good morning. Hugh.
How are my tire temps looking?

391
00:22:32.211 --> 00:22:35.129
<i>Yep. almost warm. End of the lap.
you should be good to push.</i>

392
00:22:35.130 --> 00:22:36.673
[exhales deeply]

393
00:22:38.133 --> 00:22:39.134
[grunts]

394
00:22:40.219 --> 00:22:41.303
[exhales deeply]

395
00:22:44.598 --> 00:22:46.892
[tires squeal]

396
00:22:50.687 --> 00:22:52.688
[sighs]

397
00:22:52.689 --> 00:22:54.524
Right. Man.

398
00:22:55.567 --> 00:22:57.276
- [Sonny] <i>Hugh?</i>
- Yes. sir?

399
00:22:57.277 --> 00:22:59.320
- You should've taken that bet<i>.</i>
- [chuckles]

400
00:22:59.321 --> 00:23:00.739
- [sighs]
- [Hugh] Copy that.

401
00:23:01.365 --> 00:23:05.035
<i>♪ No one's accusing me of sanity ♪</i>

402
00:23:05.827 --> 00:23:09.414
<i>♪ I ain't everybody's cup of tea ♪</i>

403
00:23:10.082 --> 00:23:11.874
<i>♪ But that's the facts
I'm talkin' factually ♪</i>

404
00:23:11.875 --> 00:23:13.126
Going for a lap.

405
00:23:14.086 --> 00:23:16.504
<i>♪ I'm just as bad as I used to be ♪</i>

406
00:23:16.505 --> 00:23:20.967
<i>♪ Yes. I'm just as bad as I used to be ♪</i>

407
00:23:20.968 --> 00:23:24.888
<i>♪ Whoa. I'm just as bad as I used to be ♪</i>

408
00:23:25.472 --> 00:23:29.643
<i>♪ I'm just as bad as I used to be ♪</i>

409
00:23:31.103 --> 00:23:33.187
Nope. Shit.

410
00:23:33.188 --> 00:23:34.272
He's dead.

411
00:23:34.273 --> 00:23:37.066
Come on. Don't do that.

412
00:23:37.067 --> 00:23:38.776
[all groan]

413
00:23:38.777 --> 00:23:39.861
And buried.

414
00:24:16.982 --> 00:24:18.358
[grunts]

415
00:24:19.526 --> 00:24:20.611
Wait.

416
00:24:22.613 --> 00:24:23.989
Wait.

417
00:24:24.907 --> 00:24:26.200
[inhales sharply]

418
00:24:26.992 --> 00:24:28.409
Now.

419
00:24:28.410 --> 00:24:29.494
[grunts]

420
00:24:31.914 --> 00:24:33.207
The car is there. come on.

421
00:24:37.461 --> 00:24:39.128
He's gaining.

422
00:24:39.129 --> 00:24:40.422
Ah. shit.

423
00:24:41.298 --> 00:24:43.926
- [tires squealing]
- [grunts]

424
00:24:49.223 --> 00:24:51.849
[grunts. groans]

425
00:24:51.850 --> 00:24:52.934
[song ends]

426
00:24:52.935 --> 00:24:54.769
- [grunts]
- You okay?

427
00:24:54.770 --> 00:24:57.396
[groans] Yep. All good.

428
00:24:57.397 --> 00:25:01.025
- [laughs]
- [sirens wailing]

429
00:25:01.026 --> 00:25:03.737
[grunting]

430
00:25:09.910 --> 00:25:12.287
- [groans. sighs]
- [Kaspar] Oh!

431
00:25:13.038 --> 00:25:15.998
- [Kate] Come on.
- [Sonny pants]

432
00:25:15.999 --> 00:25:17.458
Yeah. she's got something.

433
00:25:17.459 --> 00:25:19.002
Yeah. you mean had something.

434
00:25:20.337 --> 00:25:22.630
But definitely snappy
in the high-speed corners.

435
00:25:22.631 --> 00:25:23.966
Unpredictable in the lows.

436
00:25:24.925 --> 00:25:27.009
Had trouble with the rears. turns 14. 16--

437
00:25:27.010 --> 00:25:28.594
And the final turn. maybe?

438
00:25:28.595 --> 00:25:30.889
- No. that's on me.
- What was his lap time?

439
00:25:31.557 --> 00:25:36.311
He passed his entirely self-imposed test
by five hundredths of a second.

440
00:25:38.814 --> 00:25:40.274
[sighs] Huh.

441
00:25:40.857 --> 00:25:41.984
[chuckles]

442
00:25:43.443 --> 00:25:44.486
Well... [sighs]

443
00:25:46.363 --> 00:25:47.572
...it's a start.

444
00:25:47.573 --> 00:25:49.199
[scoffs]

445
00:25:50.534 --> 00:25:52.536
[laid-back music playing]

446
00:25:56.498 --> 00:26:00.210
Bro. we got nine races to catch
the eye of another team. you know.

447
00:26:00.878 --> 00:26:02.712
And as your manager. I have to advise you

448
00:26:02.713 --> 00:26:05.256
that we need to start hitting
these social and sponsor events.

449
00:26:05.257 --> 00:26:06.966
You need more engagement. Josh.
more followers.

450
00:26:06.967 --> 00:26:09.219
- All right. deal.
- All right. cool. I'm just saying. innit?

451
00:26:10.304 --> 00:26:11.430
You eaten? I'm starving.

452
00:26:11.972 --> 00:26:12.973
Nah.

453
00:26:13.473 --> 00:26:14.724
Gotta see someone though.

454
00:26:14.725 --> 00:26:17.518
Yeah? Hey. take a picture. post that shit.

455
00:26:17.519 --> 00:26:19.145
Send it to me. I'll post that shit.

456
00:26:19.146 --> 00:26:20.646
It's my mum.

457
00:26:20.647 --> 00:26:22.315
Don't you dare post that shit.

458
00:26:22.316 --> 00:26:23.482
[laughs]

459
00:26:23.483 --> 00:26:25.527
I knew you was gonna say that.

460
00:26:28.947 --> 00:26:30.406
[music ends]

461
00:26:30.407 --> 00:26:31.741
[music plays softly on radio]

462
00:26:31.742 --> 00:26:33.076
[phone chimes]

463
00:26:36.580 --> 00:26:38.540
- [clicks tongue. sighs]
- Okay. baby?

464
00:26:39.041 --> 00:26:40.709
Yeah. Just tired.

465
00:26:41.543 --> 00:26:43.086
Bad tires or the engine?

466
00:26:44.004 --> 00:26:45.546
Come on. Mum.
You don't know about the cars.

467
00:26:45.547 --> 00:26:47.840
[chuckles] Facety.

468
00:26:47.841 --> 00:26:51.303
All right. I may not know much about cars.
but I know a lot about you.

469
00:26:51.970 --> 00:26:52.971
Go.

470
00:26:54.264 --> 00:26:55.431
[sighs]

471
00:26:55.432 --> 00:26:57.976
I might lose my seat
if the team don't win a race.

472
00:26:58.977 --> 00:26:59.978
Any race.

473
00:27:00.812 --> 00:27:01.896
There are other teams?

474
00:27:01.897 --> 00:27:03.607
Yeah. there's 20 seats.
but they're all filled.

475
00:27:04.691 --> 00:27:06.859
Plus. there's this new guy. and... [sighs]

476
00:27:06.860 --> 00:27:07.944
...he's old.

477
00:27:07.945 --> 00:27:09.195
How old?

478
00:27:09.196 --> 00:27:11.781
Like. really old. Like... 80.

479
00:27:11.782 --> 00:27:13.617
[laughs]

480
00:27:15.285 --> 00:27:17.037
He's such an arsehole. Mum.

481
00:27:17.746 --> 00:27:18.997
He's quick. though.

482
00:27:19.581 --> 00:27:20.957
Don't mind that.

483
00:27:20.958 --> 00:27:22.583
Focus on you.

484
00:27:22.584 --> 00:27:24.877
You can spend your whole life
worrying about other people.

485
00:27:24.878 --> 00:27:27.339
but your time is right now.

486
00:27:29.299 --> 00:27:30.425
You still love it?

487
00:27:31.969 --> 00:27:33.302
Course I still love it.

488
00:27:33.303 --> 00:27:35.597
Then remember what
your father used to say.

489
00:27:36.473 --> 00:27:38.934
"Put your head down and drive."

490
00:27:40.102 --> 00:27:41.102
Yes. ma'am.

491
00:27:41.103 --> 00:27:42.937
- [chuckles]
- [chuckles]

492
00:27:42.938 --> 00:27:44.314
[jaunty music playing]

493
00:27:58.078 --> 00:28:00.289
- [bells ring]
- [cows moo]

494
00:28:03.625 --> 00:28:05.293
[bicycle bell rings]

495
00:28:05.294 --> 00:28:07.962
[herder 1] Come on. then. It's all good.
Come on. Come on. then.

496
00:28:07.963 --> 00:28:09.840
Come on. Come on.

497
00:28:10.465 --> 00:28:12.508
- Come here. Come on. then.
- You're kiddin' me.

498
00:28:12.509 --> 00:28:14.677
[herders clamoring]

499
00:28:14.678 --> 00:28:17.430
[herder 2] Don't park there.
It's just a car. Quieten down.

500
00:28:17.431 --> 00:28:18.765
Come on. eh? Come on.

501
00:28:25.063 --> 00:28:26.398
[music ends]

502
00:28:28.191 --> 00:28:30.569
Thought your job was to build
the fastest car on the planet.

503
00:28:31.194 --> 00:28:33.614
[chuckles] My job is wind.

504
00:28:34.489 --> 00:28:36.491
So. helps to feel it.

505
00:28:37.826 --> 00:28:38.826
Mmm. [sighs]

506
00:28:38.827 --> 00:28:40.328
["Bright Lights" playing]

507
00:28:40.329 --> 00:28:42.788
Mysterious moves at Apex GP.

508
00:28:42.789 --> 00:28:46.542
who have finally announced the driver
who will take their second seat.

509
00:28:46.543 --> 00:28:49.754
<i>And in a bizarre twist.
it's American Sonny Hayes.</i>

510
00:28:49.755 --> 00:28:53.090
<i>who hasn't raced in Formula 1
for over three decades.</i>

511
00:28:53.091 --> 00:28:54.884
<i>Son of an IndyCar mechanic.</i>

512
00:28:54.885 --> 00:28:58.429
<i>Hayes was considered something
of a reckless young phenomenon.</i>

513
00:28:58.430 --> 00:29:00.765
<i>the greatest who never was.</i>

514
00:29:00.766 --> 00:29:03.643
<i>His former career
being brought to an abrupt halt</i>

515
00:29:03.644 --> 00:29:06.521
<i>by a horrific accident
at the Spanish Grand Prix.</i>

516
00:29:07.064 --> 00:29:10.274
<i>He reappeared a decade later
in racing championships</i>

517
00:29:10.275 --> 00:29:13.694
<i>as diverse as Le Mans.
NASCAR. the Dakar Rally.</i>

518
00:29:13.695 --> 00:29:16.656
<i>and even a stint as
a New York taxi driver.</i>

519
00:29:16.657 --> 00:29:18.658
- Oh. no.
- [crowd applauding]

520
00:29:18.659 --> 00:29:20.743
[Will Buxton] <i>But now he's back
racing for a team which has.</i>

521
00:29:20.744 --> 00:29:25.331
<i>in its entire F1 history.
never even finished in the top ten.</i>

522
00:29:25.332 --> 00:29:27.333
<i>None of this will dampen speculation</i>

523
00:29:27.334 --> 00:29:31.754
<i>that majority shareholder Cervantes
Capital are looking to sell the team.</i>

524
00:29:31.755 --> 00:29:34.507
<i>And if they do.
that will likely also bring an end</i>

525
00:29:34.508 --> 00:29:37.301
<i>to the career of F1 rookie Joshua Pearce.</i>

526
00:29:37.302 --> 00:29:39.136
- Can we go now?
<i>- "Desperate times." they say.</i>

527
00:29:39.137 --> 00:29:40.596
<i>"call for desperate measures."</i>

528
00:29:40.597 --> 00:29:43.432
<i>but I honestly cannot recall
a driver signing</i>

529
00:29:43.433 --> 00:29:45.477
- <i>quite as desperate as this.</i>
- Let's go.

530
00:29:46.728 --> 00:29:49.355
Boy. look at my son.

531
00:29:49.356 --> 00:29:51.399
- [Joshua] Huh? [chuckles]
- Hey. [laughs]

532
00:29:51.400 --> 00:29:53.192
- [manager] That's the one.
- [Joshua's mom] Huh.

533
00:29:53.193 --> 00:29:55.486
- [music ends]
- That's the other driver?

534
00:29:55.487 --> 00:29:58.322
Yep. That's him and his stupid face.

535
00:29:58.323 --> 00:30:00.908
But. wait. you said he was old.
He not that old.

536
00:30:00.909 --> 00:30:02.410
[manager] Hey. Josh.

537
00:30:02.411 --> 00:30:03.995
You want a next shot anywhere?

538
00:30:03.996 --> 00:30:06.999
Nine races means nine times
you have to beat Chuck Norris.

539
00:30:09.042 --> 00:30:11.294
For now. start by winning over the press.

540
00:30:11.295 --> 00:30:13.462
- Yeah? You ready?
- Mm-hmm.

541
00:30:13.463 --> 00:30:14.673
Cool. Let's go.

542
00:30:15.215 --> 00:30:16.215
- [sighs]
- Mmm.

543
00:30:16.216 --> 00:30:19.344
That's a handsome man right there.
[chuckles]

544
00:30:21.096 --> 00:30:26.475
[Will Buxton] Joshua. Hey. Um. it's been
an undeniably messy start to your season.

545
00:30:26.476 --> 00:30:32.398
No wins. car problems throughout.
and now you have another new teammate.

546
00:30:32.399 --> 00:30:34.192
How exactly are you finding it?

547
00:30:34.985 --> 00:30:37.945
Messy start doesn't mean
you can't finish neat. All right?

548
00:30:37.946 --> 00:30:41.782
Apex have a fire crew of engineers.
so I'm confident we'll come back fightin'.

549
00:30:41.783 --> 00:30:43.744
In terms of new teammates.

550
00:30:44.536 --> 00:30:47.955
I think it's really wonderful that Apex
are giving second chances to the elderly.

551
00:30:47.956 --> 00:30:50.041
[all laugh]

552
00:30:50.042 --> 00:30:52.836
Ah. yes. Next question.
Thank you. Yes. Don. Yeah.

553
00:30:53.587 --> 00:30:56.505
Mr. Hayes. Hi. Don Cavendish.
Um. welcome back to the UK.

554
00:30:56.506 --> 00:30:57.924
It's been a while. mmm?

555
00:30:57.925 --> 00:30:59.634
I mean. last time
you raced at Silverstone.

556
00:30:59.635 --> 00:31:03.221
Bill Clinton was your president.
and we were all dancing the Macarena.

557
00:31:03.222 --> 00:31:05.933
- So. uh. it must be surreal to be back.
- [reporters laugh]

558
00:31:08.227 --> 00:31:09.269
Yeah.

559
00:31:11.396 --> 00:31:14.023
And. uh. during that decade.
you gave up racing.

560
00:31:14.024 --> 00:31:16.108
and. uh. gambled professionally?

561
00:31:16.109 --> 00:31:17.194
Uh-huh.

562
00:31:17.819 --> 00:31:20.571
Before declaring yourself
personally bankrupt?

563
00:31:20.572 --> 00:31:21.948
Yep.

564
00:31:21.949 --> 00:31:24.951
[Don] You had a marriage annulled
and two more ended in divorce?

565
00:31:24.952 --> 00:31:26.370
Yep.

566
00:31:28.163 --> 00:31:29.873
Anything you wish you'd done differently?

567
00:31:31.667 --> 00:31:32.667
Yeah.

568
00:31:32.668 --> 00:31:34.920
[reporters murmuring]

569
00:31:36.004 --> 00:31:38.506
[chuckles] No more questions.
Thank you. Yes. Thank you.

570
00:31:38.507 --> 00:31:43.010
[reporters clamoring]

571
00:31:43.011 --> 00:31:45.639
[somber orchestral music playing]

572
00:31:51.687 --> 00:31:54.356
[grunts]

573
00:32:01.822 --> 00:32:03.030
[music becomes electronic. dramatic]

574
00:32:03.031 --> 00:32:04.323
[panting]

575
00:32:04.324 --> 00:32:07.660
[breathing heavily]

576
00:32:07.661 --> 00:32:10.037
[grunts]

577
00:32:10.038 --> 00:32:12.207
[grunting]

578
00:32:14.001 --> 00:32:16.169
[sighs]

579
00:32:38.233 --> 00:32:41.361
[people chattering]

580
00:32:57.127 --> 00:32:58.128
[Joshua] Yes. Dodge.

581
00:33:02.007 --> 00:33:03.257
What time was he here?

582
00:33:03.258 --> 00:33:04.384
Before me.

583
00:33:11.183 --> 00:33:13.351
- And before you.
- [Joshua sighs]

584
00:33:13.352 --> 00:33:14.518
[music fades]

585
00:33:14.519 --> 00:33:17.271
[people cheering]

586
00:33:17.272 --> 00:33:19.358
[ball bouncing in distance]

587
00:33:20.567 --> 00:33:21.902
[sighs]

588
00:33:25.113 --> 00:33:27.365
Okay. here he comes. Apologize.

589
00:33:27.366 --> 00:33:29.076
[scoffs] Apologize? I can't do that.

590
00:33:29.576 --> 00:33:32.370
- How you mean? Why not?
- Because it's a sign of weakness.

591
00:33:32.371 --> 00:33:33.496
It's a sign of strength.

592
00:33:33.497 --> 00:33:34.790
Sign of weakness.

593
00:33:35.332 --> 00:33:36.916
You hard ears. just do it.

594
00:33:36.917 --> 00:33:38.251
Mum. I can't.

595
00:33:38.252 --> 00:33:39.920
You can. You will.

596
00:33:40.587 --> 00:33:41.588
[sighs]

597
00:33:44.633 --> 00:33:45.842
[sucks teeth]

598
00:33:48.136 --> 00:33:49.346
[sighs]

599
00:33:52.224 --> 00:33:53.225
Hey. man.

600
00:33:54.726 --> 00:33:57.354
Other day at the press conference.
stuff I said wasn't cool.

601
00:33:58.772 --> 00:34:00.898
[muttering] You say sorry.

602
00:34:00.899 --> 00:34:06.070
So. basically what I'm trying to say is...
I'm sorry.

603
00:34:06.071 --> 00:34:09.116
It's all right. You're just worried I'm
quicker than you. Hi. I'm Sonny.

604
00:34:09.825 --> 00:34:11.827
Oh. Bernadette Pearce. Nice to meet you.

605
00:34:12.411 --> 00:34:14.787
Pleasure.
It's all good. I'll see you out there.

606
00:34:14.788 --> 00:34:16.247
[scoffs]

607
00:34:16.248 --> 00:34:18.250
[ball bouncing]

608
00:34:21.795 --> 00:34:23.796
[pop song playing. muffled]

609
00:34:23.797 --> 00:34:24.882
[sighs]

610
00:34:26.091 --> 00:34:27.383
[sighs] How are you feeling?

611
00:34:27.384 --> 00:34:28.969
- So good.
- Good.

612
00:34:32.222 --> 00:34:33.306
- You good?
- Good.

613
00:34:33.806 --> 00:34:34.808
Good.

614
00:34:35.893 --> 00:34:36.892
No pressure.

615
00:34:36.893 --> 00:34:37.978
None.

616
00:34:39.146 --> 00:34:40.147
[sighs]

617
00:34:43.400 --> 00:34:45.276
- Great.
- Great. [clears throat]

618
00:34:45.277 --> 00:34:46.527
Great.

619
00:34:47.237 --> 00:34:48.946
[Croft] <i>Welcome along to Silverstone.</i>

620
00:34:48.947 --> 00:34:54.619
<i>the circuit where on the 13th of May 1950
the Formula 1 World Championship began.</i>

621
00:34:54.620 --> 00:34:59.332
<i>Today. we kick off the final nine races
of this thrilling championship season</i>

622
00:34:59.333 --> 00:35:02.585
<i>here at the 77th British Grand Prix.</i>

623
00:35:02.586 --> 00:35:05.129
[Brundle] <i>As always.
11 teams will take the grid.</i>

624
00:35:05.130 --> 00:35:07.131
<i>fielding two drivers each.</i>

625
00:35:07.132 --> 00:35:11.010
<i>With race order determined
by the qualifying times set yesterday.</i>

626
00:35:11.011 --> 00:35:13.095
<i>Red Bull will start on pole</i>

627
00:35:13.096 --> 00:35:16.683
<i>followed by the two McLarens
and two Ferraris.</i>

628
00:35:17.893 --> 00:35:20.311
[Croft] <i>Drivers.
two minutes to national anthem.</i>

629
00:35:20.312 --> 00:35:22.981
["God Save the King" playing]

630
00:35:36.954 --> 00:35:38.956
[marching band playing]

631
00:35:45.504 --> 00:35:47.756
["We Will Rock You" playing]

632
00:35:49.216 --> 00:35:50.300
Sonny!

633
00:35:51.218 --> 00:35:53.052
Ah. Ruben.
Don't make me talk to the money.

634
00:35:53.053 --> 00:35:55.388
Come on. give me a moment.
Just smile and shake hands.

635
00:35:55.389 --> 00:35:57.139
He's an important member of the board.

636
00:35:57.140 --> 00:35:58.683
Sonny. this is Peter Banning.

637
00:35:58.684 --> 00:35:59.976
- one of my investors.
- Hi.

638
00:35:59.977 --> 00:36:01.060
Hi.

639
00:36:01.061 --> 00:36:03.104
He knows absolutely nothing about racing...

640
00:36:03.105 --> 00:36:05.731
- Yeah.
- ...but he's my eyes and ears on the board.

641
00:36:05.732 --> 00:36:08.192
And. uh. you're Ruben's Hail Mary.

642
00:36:08.193 --> 00:36:09.944
Now. that is
an American football term. right?

643
00:36:09.945 --> 00:36:11.571
The Hail Mary. the long shot. The--

644
00:36:11.572 --> 00:36:13.072
I believe it's a religious term. originally.

645
00:36:13.073 --> 00:36:14.156
That is true. That is true.

646
00:36:14.157 --> 00:36:15.950
I'm praying to them all.

647
00:36:15.951 --> 00:36:18.286
I'm the one guy on the board
who actually wants to keep the team.

648
00:36:18.287 --> 00:36:20.204
The rest are calling it. you know.
Ruben's Inferno.

649
00:36:20.205 --> 00:36:21.998
But. seriously. man. I'm hooked.

650
00:36:21.999 --> 00:36:24.542
I've binged all of <i>Drive to Survive</i>.

651
00:36:24.543 --> 00:36:27.712
I honestly don't think I've ever known
so much about car tires. It's incredible.

652
00:36:27.713 --> 00:36:28.963
I'm gonna get back to my day job.

653
00:36:28.964 --> 00:36:30.798
- Okay.
- Okay.

654
00:36:30.799 --> 00:36:32.216
["We Will Rock You" continues]

655
00:36:32.217 --> 00:36:34.469
Hey. man.
We're counting on you. Good luck.

656
00:37:33.070 --> 00:37:34.863
What are you doing here. Sonny?

657
00:37:50.837 --> 00:37:53.464
[Croft] <i>And as the clock ticks then
to the top of the hour.</i>

658
00:37:53.465 --> 00:37:56.300
<i>it's time to get things going here
at Silverstone.</i>

659
00:37:56.301 --> 00:37:58.010
<i>It's formation lap first.</i>

660
00:37:58.011 --> 00:38:03.100
<i>One tour of the track and a chance for the
drivers to warm up their tires and brakes.</i>

661
00:38:05.936 --> 00:38:08.521
[Brundle] <i>Oh. no.
There's a problem for Apex.</i>

662
00:38:08.522 --> 00:38:11.857
<i>That's Hayes in P22. His car hasn't moved.</i>

663
00:38:11.858 --> 00:38:14.026
Hang on. I got power trouble.

664
00:38:14.027 --> 00:38:16.529
It's start mode. Sonny.

665
00:38:16.530 --> 00:38:17.947
Start mode on.

666
00:38:17.948 --> 00:38:20.032
[Brundle] <i>Yes.
a lesson for everyone at home.</i>

667
00:38:20.033 --> 00:38:22.159
<i>New car? Do read the manual.</i>

668
00:38:22.160 --> 00:38:24.620
[Croft] <i>It's been a while since he was
out on the track. At this rate...</i>

669
00:38:24.621 --> 00:38:26.789
- <i>Dios mío.</i>
- <i>...he's not even gonna get into the race.</i>

670
00:38:26.790 --> 00:38:27.875
<i>Ay.</i>

671
00:38:29.418 --> 00:38:30.501
- I got it.
- [engine revs]

672
00:38:30.502 --> 00:38:31.587
All good.

673
00:38:33.589 --> 00:38:36.257
[Croft] <i>And he's away at last.
Thank goodness for that.</i>

674
00:38:36.258 --> 00:38:38.718
[Brundle] <i>If he falls too far behind
on the formation lap...</i>

675
00:38:38.719 --> 00:38:39.802
- Drink?
- <i>...he'll be at risk...</i>

676
00:38:39.803 --> 00:38:42.306
- Eh? No.
- <i>...of having to start in the pit lane.</i>

677
00:38:43.473 --> 00:38:46.017
Where's Sonny? He's holding us up.

678
00:38:46.018 --> 00:38:48.437
Yeah. Just checking. Joshua.
Just checking.

679
00:38:49.605 --> 00:38:51.564
- What's wrong with his car?
- What? Nothing.

680
00:38:51.565 --> 00:38:53.065
[Brundle] <i>With a clear track ahead.</i>

681
00:38:53.066 --> 00:38:56.360
<i>Hayes has been able
to push much harder on this formation lap.</i>

682
00:38:56.361 --> 00:38:59.865
<i>He'll turn up at the back of the grid
with warm tires. ready to go.</i>

683
00:39:01.033 --> 00:39:03.577
Cheeky shit. It's on purpose.

684
00:39:08.457 --> 00:39:09.790
What is this guy doing?

685
00:39:09.791 --> 00:39:13.753
[Croft] <i>This is actually now
turning into an advantage for Sonny Hayes.</i>

686
00:39:13.754 --> 00:39:17.966
[Brundle] <i>And he's just made it in time.
Watch out for his start.</i>

687
00:39:26.934 --> 00:39:31.103
[Croft] <i>Five lights ahead of the drivers.
It's lights out and away we go!</i>

688
00:39:31.104 --> 00:39:32.314
[crowd cheering]

689
00:39:44.159 --> 00:39:46.369
<i>Here comes Sonny Hayes.
ladies and gentlemen.</i>

690
00:39:46.370 --> 00:39:50.248
<i>Using those warm tires to carve his way
through the back of the field.</i>

691
00:39:50.249 --> 00:39:53.209
[Brundle] <i>And if you ever need
confidence in your car.</i>

692
00:39:53.210 --> 00:39:54.753
<i>it's here at Silverstone.</i>

693
00:40:11.562 --> 00:40:13.479
<i>Hayes is just sailing past people.</i>

694
00:40:13.480 --> 00:40:16.482
<i>He's moved up seven places
since the start.</i>

695
00:40:16.483 --> 00:40:19.402
- <i>Apex GP has struggled with this car...</i>
- Yes!

696
00:40:19.403 --> 00:40:21.779
<i>...but they've brought an upgrade package
this weekend.</i>

697
00:40:21.780 --> 00:40:25.784
<i>Let's see if it makes a difference
as Hayes attacks Perez in the Red Bull.</i>

698
00:40:29.705 --> 00:40:32.583
Car's bouncing around this dirty air.
I can't position to attack.

699
00:40:33.375 --> 00:40:35.751
[Brundle] <i>Hayes complaining
about his car over the radio.</i>

700
00:40:35.752 --> 00:40:38.588
<i>That's not what the team wants to hear.</i>

701
00:40:38.589 --> 00:40:41.841
Copy. Gap is 0.9 to Perez.
You're within DRS range.

702
00:40:41.842 --> 00:40:44.094
<i>Should be able to take him
on the next straight.</i>

703
00:40:46.763 --> 00:40:50.308
[Croft] <i>Hayes now using
the drag reduction system to get past.</i>

704
00:40:50.309 --> 00:40:51.809
- [cheering]
- Yeah!

705
00:40:51.810 --> 00:40:54.061
Won't be able to hold him off. guys.
I got no grip.

706
00:40:54.062 --> 00:40:56.147
<i>- This is trouble now for Apex GP.
-</i> Oh. come on.

707
00:40:56.148 --> 00:40:57.982
<i>The Red Bull's tires are now warm</i>

708
00:40:57.983 --> 00:41:01.611
<i>and Hayes hasn't got his tire advantage
from the start anymore.</i>

709
00:41:01.612 --> 00:41:05.072
<i>We've seen the attack.
Now it's all about defense.</i>

710
00:41:05.073 --> 00:41:07.867
<i>And Perez on the attack into Vale.</i>

711
00:41:07.868 --> 00:41:11.245
<i>Hayes is in trouble.
This could be the places reversed.</i>

712
00:41:11.246 --> 00:41:13.289
- [crowd cheering]
<i>- And it is.</i>

713
00:41:13.290 --> 00:41:14.373
Damn.

714
00:41:14.374 --> 00:41:16.500
Rear end is loose.
Tell me if you see a fix.

715
00:41:16.501 --> 00:41:19.378
Tell him to pull back the entry
to get a better exit.

716
00:41:19.379 --> 00:41:21.673
He-He thinks it's the setup. It's not.

717
00:41:24.051 --> 00:41:25.176
[Croft] <i>Twenty laps down.</i>

718
00:41:25.177 --> 00:41:29.180
<i>Verstappen leads but Joshua Pearce
is struggling out there at the moment.</i>

719
00:41:29.181 --> 00:41:32.141
Guys. get me off these softs.
I'm going backwards.

720
00:41:32.142 --> 00:41:34.977
Copy that. Lap 20. Box. box.

721
00:41:34.978 --> 00:41:37.480
[Brundle] <i>Stakes couldn't be higher
for rookie Joshua Pearce.</i>

722
00:41:37.481 --> 00:41:41.193
<i>This is not where you want to be.
in last place.</i>

723
00:41:43.612 --> 00:41:45.197
[groans] I'm jammed. Back up!

724
00:41:52.287 --> 00:41:53.663
Hit something. What was that?

725
00:41:53.664 --> 00:41:54.747
[crowd shrieks]

726
00:41:54.748 --> 00:41:57.291
[Croft] <i>Ooh. a seven-second pit stop.</i>

727
00:41:57.292 --> 00:41:59.418
<i>Apex GP won't be happy with that.</i>

728
00:41:59.419 --> 00:42:02.421
<i>That's double the time it should've taken.</i>

729
00:42:02.422 --> 00:42:04.048
Lost the rears. Box. box.

730
00:42:04.049 --> 00:42:06.051
Copy. Go to plan B. Box. box.

731
00:42:06.760 --> 00:42:09.470
[Croft] <i>And here comes Sonny Hayes
for a fresh set of tires.</i>

732
00:42:09.471 --> 00:42:14.308
<i>He'll be hoping these will help him
hold on to his current position of P15.</i>

733
00:42:14.309 --> 00:42:15.309
Front jacks! Front jacks!

734
00:42:15.310 --> 00:42:17.019
[Brundle] <i>The front jack has
not worked properly.</i>

735
00:42:17.020 --> 00:42:20.356
- You're kidding me.
<i>- This is causing absolute pandemonium</i>

736
00:42:20.357 --> 00:42:22.734
<i>in the Apex GP pit lane.</i>

737
00:42:24.570 --> 00:42:27.948
<i>Whatever could go wrong
is going wrong for this team.</i>

738
00:42:31.118 --> 00:42:34.704
[Croft] <i>And coming out of the pit.
Hayes just ahead of his teammate.</i>

739
00:42:34.705 --> 00:42:39.250
<i>As Pearce and Hayes go battling it out
here at Silverstone.</i>

740
00:42:39.251 --> 00:42:40.586
Coming for you. old man.

741
00:42:47.968 --> 00:42:49.760
Got the pace. man.
Tell him to let me pass.

742
00:42:49.761 --> 00:42:51.512
Yeah. Copy. Hold position. Stand by. Kate.

743
00:42:51.513 --> 00:42:54.349
Josh is faster. Sonny is on cold tires.

744
00:42:59.855 --> 00:43:01.481
Yeah. okay. Sonny. no fighting.
Let him through.

745
00:43:07.029 --> 00:43:09.155
Sonny. no fighting.

746
00:43:09.156 --> 00:43:10.698
Who's fighting? I'm racing.

747
00:43:10.699 --> 00:43:13.159
[Croft] <i>Pearce on the inside.
Hayes on the outside.</i>

748
00:43:13.160 --> 00:43:15.578
[Brundle] <i>Hayes trying
to make him eat concrete</i>

749
00:43:15.579 --> 00:43:17.330
<i>up against the old pit wall there.</i>

750
00:43:17.331 --> 00:43:19.582
Joshua. you're gonna
have to fight for position.

751
00:43:19.583 --> 00:43:20.666
<i>You are racing Sonny.</i>

752
00:43:20.667 --> 00:43:21.834
A-ffirm.

753
00:43:21.835 --> 00:43:24.420
[Brundle] <i>They're giving
absolutely no quarter.</i>

754
00:43:24.421 --> 00:43:26.422
<i>No benefit to their teammate at all.</i>

755
00:43:26.423 --> 00:43:29.175
<i>They're pushing as if
they're trying to win a Grand Prix.</i>

756
00:43:29.176 --> 00:43:32.470
[Croft] <i>But this is the battle
for last place. remember?</i>

757
00:43:32.471 --> 00:43:33.721
<i>And what a brawl it is.</i>

758
00:43:33.722 --> 00:43:35.224
Let's go. kid. Bring it.

759
00:43:38.769 --> 00:43:40.519
What is this guy doing? Let me through.

760
00:43:40.520 --> 00:43:42.814
[crowd cheering]

761
00:43:50.739 --> 00:43:51.782
[spectators gasp]

762
00:43:56.954 --> 00:43:58.788
[Croft] <i>Round the final corner.</i>

763
00:43:58.789 --> 00:43:59.997
<i>It's close!</i>

764
00:43:59.998 --> 00:44:01.624
<i>They make contact.</i>

765
00:44:01.625 --> 00:44:05.169
- <i>Both Apex GP cars into the gravel.</i>
- [Sonny grunts]

766
00:44:05.170 --> 00:44:07.255
<i>and Pearce hits the barrier.</i>

767
00:44:07.256 --> 00:44:09.298
[crowd clamoring]

768
00:44:09.299 --> 00:44:10.634
- Ah. no!
- No!

769
00:44:11.343 --> 00:44:12.510
[Brundle] <i>This is mad.</i>

770
00:44:12.511 --> 00:44:14.804
<i>The cardinal sin of motor racing.</i>

771
00:44:14.805 --> 00:44:16.514
- <i>A double DNF.</i>
- [Ruben groans]

772
00:44:16.515 --> 00:44:20.476
<i>Just when it couldn't get any worse
for the black and gold.</i>

773
00:44:20.477 --> 00:44:22.229
- [Peter] That's a tough one. man.
- [mutters. sighing]

774
00:44:27.818 --> 00:44:30.195
[crowd shrieking. booing]

775
00:44:38.579 --> 00:44:39.871
We can't corner.

776
00:44:39.872 --> 00:44:42.540
We're bouncing around the place
like we're on the bloody Tube

777
00:44:42.541 --> 00:44:44.835
and now we think it's cool
to leave wheel guns in the pit box.

778
00:44:45.460 --> 00:44:46.460
Who even was that?

779
00:44:46.461 --> 00:44:48.714
- That was me.
- Of course.

780
00:44:51.341 --> 00:44:52.342
Old man.

781
00:44:55.304 --> 00:44:57.973
You losing your hearing? What was that?

782
00:44:58.974 --> 00:44:59.974
You wanna do this here?

783
00:44:59.975 --> 00:45:02.351
Yeah. I'd love to do this here
in front of the team. right.

784
00:45:02.352 --> 00:45:03.769
The one that you're apparently a part of.

785
00:45:03.770 --> 00:45:06.606
- Okay. You made a mistake. It happens.
- [laughs]

786
00:45:06.607 --> 00:45:08.357
I made a mistake. I love this guy. man.

787
00:45:08.358 --> 00:45:10.818
- Don't worry about it. Jodie.
- Are you even listening to me?

788
00:45:10.819 --> 00:45:12.778
- Not really.
- [Kaspar] No!

789
00:45:12.779 --> 00:45:14.197
Stop.

790
00:45:14.198 --> 00:45:15.698
Joshua is right.

791
00:45:15.699 --> 00:45:17.366
An order is an order.

792
00:45:17.367 --> 00:45:20.287
May I remind you that you report to me?

793
00:45:23.957 --> 00:45:24.958
Cool.

794
00:45:25.751 --> 00:45:27.669
Just don't ask me to give up position.

795
00:45:30.714 --> 00:45:32.633
Sorry. Sorry. guys.

796
00:45:34.760 --> 00:45:36.385
Hold up.

797
00:45:36.386 --> 00:45:38.054
You swan into our garage
like some entitled prick.

798
00:45:38.055 --> 00:45:39.931
- "Swan"?
- Calling us piss poor...

799
00:45:39.932 --> 00:45:41.641
- What's "swan"?
- ...and then you drive like that. Huh?

800
00:45:41.642 --> 00:45:43.601
You said I "swan." What's that mean?

801
00:45:43.602 --> 00:45:46.395
You. You're an arsehole.
You come in like an arsehole. You swan.

802
00:45:46.396 --> 00:45:48.148
So swans are assholes?

803
00:45:50.192 --> 00:45:52.944
You're making the mistake of thinking
that I'm just gonna be some grateful kid

804
00:45:52.945 --> 00:45:54.780
who'll bend a knee to an old-timer.

805
00:45:55.447 --> 00:45:57.658
I climbed a mountain to get here. bro.

806
00:45:58.450 --> 00:45:59.534
Formula 1.

807
00:45:59.535 --> 00:46:02.370
Back home we call that
a participation trophy.

808
00:46:02.371 --> 00:46:04.372
[reporters] Joshua. Joshua! Josh!

809
00:46:04.373 --> 00:46:05.498
[clamoring]

810
00:46:05.499 --> 00:46:07.501
[chuckles] Yeah.

811
00:46:08.835 --> 00:46:11.170
What the hell are you smiling about. man?

812
00:46:11.171 --> 00:46:12.422
Did you win something?

813
00:46:12.965 --> 00:46:15.216
There's 20 other drivers
still out on that track

814
00:46:15.217 --> 00:46:17.301
and you're in here
posing for that nonsense.

815
00:46:17.302 --> 00:46:20.305
Do you think any of them respect us?
Do you?

816
00:46:21.431 --> 00:46:24.767
They need to learn that
no one gets past us without a fight.

817
00:46:24.768 --> 00:46:25.852
No one.

818
00:46:28.855 --> 00:46:31.608
You don't like the way I'm driving?
Beat me. swan.

819
00:46:38.949 --> 00:46:39.950
Hell of a race. huh?

820
00:46:40.492 --> 00:46:41.618
Whoo!

821
00:46:52.421 --> 00:46:55.883
[breathes deeply]

822
00:47:00.012 --> 00:47:03.223
Sorry. I didn't see you. Um... [sighs]

823
00:47:03.974 --> 00:47:05.975
[sighs] You still beating yourself up?

824
00:47:05.976 --> 00:47:07.268
Yeah.

825
00:47:07.269 --> 00:47:09.438
Yeah. I know that one. [chuckles]

826
00:47:11.773 --> 00:47:14.651
Um. thanks for what you said out there.

827
00:47:16.153 --> 00:47:18.906
Just don't do it again. okay?

828
00:47:19.615 --> 00:47:21.200
Makes me look like I need help.

829
00:47:21.909 --> 00:47:24.745
Oh. man. You're right. [sighs] Got it.

830
00:47:25.329 --> 00:47:28.414
Hey. for what it's worth.
don't be shitty to yourself.

831
00:47:28.415 --> 00:47:30.499
There's plenty of people out there
that'll do that for you.

832
00:47:30.500 --> 00:47:31.835
Yeah.

833
00:47:36.715 --> 00:47:37.883
[sighs]

834
00:47:40.302 --> 00:47:44.931
"I'm sorry. Ruben. for demolishing not one
but both of your lovely cars.

835
00:47:44.932 --> 00:47:47.475
For coming back into your life
only to destroy it."

836
00:47:47.476 --> 00:47:48.893
Is this your revenge for Monaco?

837
00:47:48.894 --> 00:47:50.394
Yeah. I waited 30 years

838
00:47:50.395 --> 00:47:53.814
and came all this way
to humiliate myself on global television.

839
00:47:53.815 --> 00:47:57.236
Funny. You think I brought you in
to make my other driver quit?

840
00:47:57.945 --> 00:48:01.405
Listen. he's cocky.
He's arrogant. He's got a lot to learn.

841
00:48:01.406 --> 00:48:03.492
[laughs]

842
00:48:05.035 --> 00:48:07.870
You were cocky. you were arrogant
and you had a lot to learn.

843
00:48:07.871 --> 00:48:10.706
I'm not here to hold anyone's hand.
I'm here to race.

844
00:48:10.707 --> 00:48:13.710
No. you're not. Sonny.
You're here to give me a heart attack.

845
00:48:14.962 --> 00:48:16.588
The board is up my ass

846
00:48:17.965 --> 00:48:20.383
and I have to decide
whether to continue this fiasco

847
00:48:20.384 --> 00:48:23.177
- or pull the plug now.
- You have till the end of the season.

848
00:48:23.178 --> 00:48:26.014
By which time Apex will be worth less
than my shoes!

849
00:48:26.723 --> 00:48:28.475
Sonny! God...

850
00:48:31.186 --> 00:48:32.229
Tell me about Kate.

851
00:48:33.730 --> 00:48:35.398
The car.
I wanna talk to her about the car.

852
00:48:35.399 --> 00:48:37.984
She's the world's first
female tech director of an F1 team.

853
00:48:37.985 --> 00:48:39.527
I mean. that takes balls.

854
00:48:39.528 --> 00:48:41.613
Wow. Is that your line?

855
00:48:42.197 --> 00:48:43.281
She'll see right through it.

856
00:48:43.282 --> 00:48:44.490
It's not a line.

857
00:48:44.491 --> 00:48:46.869
- I'm sorry. Sorry.
- Is she married?

858
00:48:47.452 --> 00:48:50.663
Okay. stay there in that tub of ice
until Budapest.

859
00:48:50.664 --> 00:48:52.207
You don't move.

860
00:48:54.585 --> 00:48:55.752
Hey. Ruben...

861
00:48:57.838 --> 00:48:59.339
We can't get there with this car.

862
00:49:08.390 --> 00:49:09.433
[sighs]

863
00:49:45.761 --> 00:49:47.470
Hey. Hey.

864
00:49:47.471 --> 00:49:48.972
Yeah. sorry. Hi. hi. hi.

865
00:49:49.598 --> 00:49:50.599
What you working on?

866
00:49:51.308 --> 00:49:55.811
I'm working on a new front wing concept.
Trying to pick us up a tenth or so.

867
00:49:55.812 --> 00:49:59.357
Cool. And you can replicate turns?
Lateral airflow?

868
00:49:59.358 --> 00:50:01.234
No. just straight line drag.

869
00:50:01.235 --> 00:50:03.403
But. I mean.
we can calculate it from there.

870
00:50:04.154 --> 00:50:07.406
Okay. what about turbulent air
from a car we're following?

871
00:50:07.407 --> 00:50:09.408
No. not exactly. but--

872
00:50:09.409 --> 00:50:12.286
Track conditions. surface quality.
weather. ambient temps?

873
00:50:12.287 --> 00:50:16.582
[chuckles] I'm sorry. uh. is there
something that you wanted to discuss?

874
00:50:16.583 --> 00:50:19.253
Kate. you read my mind.

875
00:50:23.257 --> 00:50:27.093
So how does one get to be the first female
technical director of an F1 team?

876
00:50:27.094 --> 00:50:28.345
Must take...

877
00:50:31.682 --> 00:50:34.684
dedication and lots of hard work.

878
00:50:34.685 --> 00:50:38.145
- That's your urgent question?
- Hmm? Mm-mmm.

879
00:50:38.146 --> 00:50:42.149
Plenty of people think I don't belong here
and I'm happy to add you to the list

880
00:50:42.150 --> 00:50:44.026
if you're implying
what I... I think you're implying.

881
00:50:44.027 --> 00:50:45.403
As a rule I don't imply stuff.

882
00:50:45.404 --> 00:50:46.904
So you like straight talk?

883
00:50:46.905 --> 00:50:48.740
Straight as an arrow. No sugar.

884
00:50:49.700 --> 00:50:51.534
Everyone thinks Ruben's lost it.

885
00:50:51.535 --> 00:50:52.869
That he is clutching at straws.

886
00:50:52.870 --> 00:50:54.704
They're saying maybe he lost a bet.

887
00:50:54.705 --> 00:50:57.164
- Ran over your dog.
- [chuckles]

888
00:50:57.165 --> 00:51:01.837
They're saying Sonny Hayes
isn't a has-been.

889
00:51:02.337 --> 00:51:03.505
He's a never-was.

890
00:51:07.092 --> 00:51:09.720
Yeah. when I said I like straight talk
I meant me.

891
00:51:10.262 --> 00:51:13.556
From others. I mostly prefer praise.
flattery. hero worship.

892
00:51:13.557 --> 00:51:15.433
at times. straight-up bullshit.

893
00:51:15.434 --> 00:51:17.894
- Is that what Ruben's for?
- [laughs]

894
00:51:17.895 --> 00:51:20.354
Ruben. I love the guy.
Most solid. steadfast--

895
00:51:20.355 --> 00:51:21.814
Said you asked if I was married.

896
00:51:21.815 --> 00:51:25.276
Disloyal. mean. twisted.
bitter. husk of a man.

897
00:51:25.277 --> 00:51:31.657
Mmm. yeah. And he also told me about
a big string of ex-wives and girlfriends.

898
00:51:31.658 --> 00:51:33.326
He said to avoid you like the plague.

899
00:51:33.327 --> 00:51:36.747
Okay... [chuckles] ...let me explain this.

900
00:51:37.789 --> 00:51:40.124
When you're going 200 miles per hour
into Eau Rouge.

901
00:51:40.125 --> 00:51:42.377
it's good to know who's got your back.

902
00:51:43.629 --> 00:51:45.421
And for the record.
in all my years of racing.

903
00:51:45.422 --> 00:51:49.884
I have never ever hit on
the team technical director.

904
00:51:49.885 --> 00:51:54.181
[smacks lips] Well. now that's
a huge weight off my mind.

905
00:51:58.018 --> 00:52:00.269
So what's this urgent question?

906
00:52:00.270 --> 00:52:01.563
Okay.

907
00:52:02.439 --> 00:52:05.816
Red Bull. Ferrari.
Mercedes. Aston. now McLaren

908
00:52:05.817 --> 00:52:07.443
all have us beat on straight line speed.

909
00:52:07.444 --> 00:52:09.987
Our shot is battling in the turns.

910
00:52:09.988 --> 00:52:12.783
I need a way
to chase through the dirty air.

911
00:52:15.244 --> 00:52:19.372
You want me to redesign
so you can follow closer?

912
00:52:19.373 --> 00:52:20.958
We need to build our car for combat.

913
00:52:22.042 --> 00:52:24.335
Uh. how am I supposed to make that safe?

914
00:52:24.336 --> 00:52:25.879
Who said anything about safe?

915
00:52:28.382 --> 00:52:29.715
That's your question?

916
00:52:29.716 --> 00:52:31.008
Yeah.

917
00:52:31.009 --> 00:52:32.302
And here's the straight talk.

918
00:52:33.470 --> 00:52:34.471
It's urgent.

919
00:52:36.974 --> 00:52:38.559
[scoffs]

920
00:52:40.310 --> 00:52:42.895
You know.
I bet when you look in the mirror.

921
00:52:42.896 --> 00:52:49.443
you see this rough-and-tumble.
old school. no bullshit cowboy.

922
00:52:49.444 --> 00:52:52.613
Doesn't take orders.
Goes his own way. Huh?

923
00:52:52.614 --> 00:52:54.116
A lone wolf.

924
00:52:55.117 --> 00:52:56.617
Well. I have news for you.

925
00:52:56.618 --> 00:52:59.620
Formula 1 is a team sport. It always was.

926
00:52:59.621 --> 00:53:02.541
And maybe that's why you failed at it?

927
00:53:03.667 --> 00:53:07.503
The only question here is.
"Why did Sonny Hayes come back to F1?"

928
00:53:07.504 --> 00:53:12.175
Now that question
is extremely fucking urgent.

929
00:53:16.388 --> 00:53:19.808
I'll start listening to you
when you finish a race.

930
00:53:24.313 --> 00:53:25.314
[grumbles]

931
00:53:27.316 --> 00:53:28.817
[electronic pop song playing]

932
00:53:34.573 --> 00:53:36.491
<i>♪ Don't let me down ♪</i>

933
00:53:42.706 --> 00:53:45.667
<i>♪ Don't let me down ♪</i>

934
00:53:48.212 --> 00:53:51.047
<i>♪ Don't let me down ♪</i>

935
00:53:51.048 --> 00:53:52.215
<i>♪ Oh yeah. oh yeah. oh yeah ♪</i>

936
00:53:52.216 --> 00:53:54.800
<i>♪ Don't let me drown ♪</i>

937
00:53:54.801 --> 00:53:56.761
<i>♪ Oh yeah. oh yeah. oh yeah ♪</i>

938
00:53:56.762 --> 00:53:59.347
<i>♪ Don't let me down ♪</i>

939
00:53:59.348 --> 00:54:01.057
<i>♪ Oh yeah. oh yeah. oh yeah ♪</i>

940
00:54:01.058 --> 00:54:05.103
<i>♪ Don't let me drown ♪</i>

941
00:54:09.524 --> 00:54:11.818
[song continues]

942
00:54:12.527 --> 00:54:14.613
<i>♪ Don't let me down ♪</i>

943
00:54:20.953 --> 00:54:23.747
<i>♪ Don't let me drown ♪</i>

944
00:54:26.917 --> 00:54:29.293
<i>♪ Nights like these ♪</i>

945
00:54:29.294 --> 00:54:33.090
<i>♪ There's something mystical
About nights like these ♪</i>

946
00:54:33.882 --> 00:54:36.384
<i>♪ And the concept of time don't matter ♪</i>

947
00:54:36.385 --> 00:54:38.094
[song fades]

948
00:54:38.095 --> 00:54:39.429
[brakes hiss]

949
00:54:40.681 --> 00:54:44.141
[Buxton] <i>At the Spanish Grand Prix.
the American rookie Sonny Hayes</i>

950
00:54:44.142 --> 00:54:48.145
<i>had just signed a new contract.
and his future looked very bright.</i>

951
00:54:48.146 --> 00:54:51.941
<i>He'd earned a reputation
for his aggressive driving style.</i>

952
00:54:51.942 --> 00:54:55.903
<i>Seen by some as reckless.
it nevertheless served him well</i>

953
00:54:55.904 --> 00:54:58.739
<i>as he climbed up the order
over the course of the season.</i>

954
00:54:58.740 --> 00:55:01.827
<i>relentlessly pursuing
his first F1 victory.</i>

955
00:55:03.537 --> 00:55:06.330
<i>Hayes was running well
in the opening laps.</i>

956
00:55:06.331 --> 00:55:09.041
<i>chasing down race leader Ayrton Senna.</i>

957
00:55:09.042 --> 00:55:11.294
<i>However when Hayes made a risky move</i>

958
00:55:11.295 --> 00:55:15.424
<i>and attacked Senna on the outside of
a high-speed right-hand turn.</i>

959
00:55:16.008 --> 00:55:19.385
<i>a frightening scene unfolded
as quick as a flash.</i>

960
00:55:19.386 --> 00:55:22.013
[commentator 1] <i>My goodness!
I just saw him plunge off to the right.</i>

961
00:55:22.014 --> 00:55:23.639
<i>There you can see the debris on the right.</i>

962
00:55:23.640 --> 00:55:26.309
<i>What on earth happened there.
I don't know.</i>

963
00:55:26.310 --> 00:55:27.768
[commentator 2]
<i>Yes. this looks very severe indeed.</i>

964
00:55:27.769 --> 00:55:31.230
<i>I must say. it looks like. uh. he is...
he really needs help.</i>

965
00:55:31.231 --> 00:55:33.149
<i>There is nobody coming to him
at the moment.</i>

966
00:55:33.150 --> 00:55:35.443
<i>The race has been stopped.
The red flag is out.</i>

967
00:55:35.444 --> 00:55:37.362
<i>This looks a little bit like a--</i>

968
00:55:54.630 --> 00:55:58.216
[Kate] Our models predict all teams
are gonna be targeting a one-stop race.

969
00:55:58.217 --> 00:56:02.553
Plan A is to switch from mediums to hards.
between lap 27 and 33.

970
00:56:02.554 --> 00:56:08.851
Plan B will be medium-hard-medium.
first window 16 to 21. second. 45 to 51.

971
00:56:08.852 --> 00:56:10.645
Plan C for softs doesn't make sense.

972
00:56:10.646 --> 00:56:12.940
At this temp.
the tire deg will be too high.

973
00:56:14.691 --> 00:56:15.692
Nothing else?

974
00:56:16.276 --> 00:56:18.110
- Yep.
- Yeah. Joshua?

975
00:56:18.111 --> 00:56:20.321
So. we've just got to
drive our race. all right?

976
00:56:20.322 --> 00:56:21.405
Let's not try and be heroes.

977
00:56:21.406 --> 00:56:23.574
Just make it through
those first turns clean.

978
00:56:23.575 --> 00:56:25.785
Can't win at lap one.
starting at the back.

979
00:56:25.786 --> 00:56:29.038
so we just gotta hope for some
lucky breaks later on. all right?

980
00:56:29.039 --> 00:56:30.289
- [crew member] Yeah.
- Yeah.

981
00:56:30.290 --> 00:56:31.959
Create your own breaks.

982
00:56:33.293 --> 00:56:35.212
Um. hello. hi? I just said that.

983
00:56:36.505 --> 00:56:37.798
Hope is not a strategy.

984
00:56:41.635 --> 00:56:43.053
Anything else. Professor?

985
00:56:43.971 --> 00:56:45.931
Um... [sighs]

986
00:56:46.431 --> 00:56:47.516
Drive fast?

987
00:56:59.820 --> 00:57:03.906
- [crowd cheering]
- [timer beeps]

988
00:57:03.907 --> 00:57:04.991
[timer stops]

989
00:57:04.992 --> 00:57:07.326
[Croft] <i>It's lights out. and away we go.</i>

990
00:57:07.327 --> 00:57:10.079
<i>Great start from Hamilton.
Verstappen battling with him.</i>

991
00:57:10.080 --> 00:57:13.542
<i>Piastri. Zhou. Leclerc...
and here come the two Apex GPs.</i>

992
00:57:14.501 --> 00:57:18.922
<i>But Gasly shuts the door.
leaving them with nowhere to go.</i>

993
00:57:25.304 --> 00:57:28.681
<i>Into turn one.
and there's three cars gone off.</i>

994
00:57:28.682 --> 00:57:31.893
<i>Gasly. Ocon. and the AlphaTauri. Tsunoda.</i>

995
00:57:31.894 --> 00:57:33.269
[Sonny] Hit debris. Check my tires.

996
00:57:33.270 --> 00:57:36.063
Yeah. you've got a puncture. Right rear.
Box. Box this lap.

997
00:57:36.064 --> 00:57:38.233
First goddamn turn. A ruined race.

998
00:57:39.192 --> 00:57:41.737
[Sonny] Oh. shit. shit. shit. Ah. shit.

999
00:57:45.240 --> 00:57:46.742
He's coming in! Let's go.

1000
00:57:47.326 --> 00:57:48.826
[Sonny] Let's go Plan C.

1001
00:57:48.827 --> 00:57:53.289
No. Plan C is for soft tires.
They won't last ten laps in this heat. No.

1002
00:57:53.290 --> 00:57:54.540
That's a negative. Sonny. Plan A.

1003
00:57:54.541 --> 00:57:57.168
[Sonny] Plan A is called Plan A 'cause
it's when everything is going right.

1004
00:57:57.169 --> 00:57:58.253
You see anything going right?

1005
00:57:58.962 --> 00:58:00.630
Plan C. Softs.

1006
00:58:00.631 --> 00:58:03.842
It's not his call.
Tell him A. as in "asshole."

1007
00:58:04.593 --> 00:58:06.260
Okay. let's go! Turn 'em out! Hard tires.

1008
00:58:06.261 --> 00:58:07.846
[Sonny] Softs. goddamn it.

1009
00:58:13.227 --> 00:58:16.187
- What's wrong with the car?
- The guy sitting in it.

1010
00:58:16.188 --> 00:58:20.983
Are you insane? We need hard tires.
Everybody here is at a one-stop race.

1011
00:58:20.984 --> 00:58:23.153
[Sonny] We do what
everybody does. we lose.

1012
00:58:24.863 --> 00:58:26.406
- Make him go!
- How?

1013
00:58:27.157 --> 00:58:30.159
You think I don't know my tires?
I was a mechanic.

1014
00:58:30.160 --> 00:58:33.956
Five championship titles
with my bare freaking hands!

1015
00:58:37.000 --> 00:58:38.001
Give him his tires.

1016
00:58:39.002 --> 00:58:40.920
- [Hugh] Okay. let's go.
- Go. go. change!

1017
00:58:40.921 --> 00:58:42.631
Let's go. let's go! Change quick. now!

1018
00:58:47.970 --> 00:58:48.970
[Sonny] Be ready.

1019
00:58:48.971 --> 00:58:50.681
Ready for what?

1020
00:58:57.980 --> 00:59:01.066
- Where's JP sitting?
- [Hugh] <i>Currently running P14.</i>

1021
00:59:03.360 --> 00:59:04.820
[Sonny] All right. here we go now.

1022
00:59:05.320 --> 00:59:06.612
[Croft] <i>Hayes makes his move.</i>

1023
00:59:06.613 --> 00:59:09.282
<i>chasing Kevin Magnussen.
It's a late lunge!</i>

1024
00:59:09.283 --> 00:59:10.950
[Brundle] <i>He's damaged his front wing.</i>

1025
00:59:10.951 --> 00:59:15.872
<i>Any driver knows Magnussen will shut
the door on a clumsy move like that.</i>

1026
00:59:15.873 --> 00:59:17.707
[Sonny] Aw. dagnabbit.

1027
00:59:17.708 --> 00:59:19.208
Plan C for "chaos."

1028
00:59:19.209 --> 00:59:20.418
[chuckles]

1029
00:59:20.419 --> 00:59:23.796
[Croft] <i>So that will bring out a
safety car. which always shakes up a race.</i>

1030
00:59:23.797 --> 00:59:26.924
<i>Slows down the leaders.
leaves the field bunched up together.</i>

1031
00:59:26.925 --> 00:59:29.343
<i>and gives teams
the chance for a quick pit stop.</i>

1032
00:59:29.344 --> 00:59:31.762
<i>which only costs half the usual time.</i>

1033
00:59:31.763 --> 00:59:33.306
[Joshua] Safety car. We're boxing. right?

1034
00:59:33.307 --> 00:59:34.640
Standby. Kate.

1035
00:59:34.641 --> 00:59:37.101
shouldn't we take advantage
while the safety car window is open?

1036
00:59:37.102 --> 00:59:39.270
It's early. We gain track position
if we stay out.

1037
00:59:39.271 --> 00:59:42.732
[Rico] <i>Stay out. stay out.
Want you out. Push. push. Joshua.</i>

1038
00:59:42.733 --> 00:59:44.901
[Brundle] <i>So. the midfield moves up
for the moment.</i>

1039
00:59:44.902 --> 00:59:47.321
<i>including Joshua Pearce to P12.</i>

1040
00:59:47.988 --> 00:59:50.240
[Joshua] This guy better not
be messing up my race.

1041
00:59:55.746 --> 00:59:56.746
Where's JP now?

1042
00:59:56.747 --> 00:59:58.290
Currently running P12.

1043
01:00:05.005 --> 01:00:06.965
Okay. Plan C. Be ready.

1044
01:00:07.925 --> 01:00:09.343
He's gonna do it again.

1045
01:00:13.013 --> 01:00:15.348
[Croft] <i>Back marker Hayes
is now down a lap.</i>

1046
01:00:15.349 --> 01:00:18.768
<i>He has to let Bottas pass.
or face a five-second penalty.</i>

1047
01:00:18.769 --> 01:00:21.520
[Brundle] <i>Hayes is making it
very difficult for Bottas.</i>

1048
01:00:21.521 --> 01:00:24.774
<i>Under the rules he has to let him through
before passing three blue flags.</i>

1049
01:00:24.775 --> 01:00:26.525
<i>or risk a penalty.</i>

1050
01:00:26.526 --> 01:00:29.821
Hey. I'm just putting it out there.
but. uh. maybe you should drive.

1051
01:00:31.323 --> 01:00:34.076
[Hugh] <i>Sonny. you've gotten the blue flag.
Let Bottas through.</i>

1052
01:00:34.952 --> 01:00:36.703
[Sonny] Come on. now. Little closer.

1053
01:00:38.664 --> 01:00:40.248
[Hugh] <i>Sonny. do you copy?</i>

1054
01:00:40.249 --> 01:00:42.042
[Sonny] I hear ya. Lettin' him through.

1055
01:00:43.544 --> 01:00:44.877
Whoops. my bad.

1056
01:00:44.878 --> 01:00:46.796
[Croft] <i>And that's his front wing again!</i>

1057
01:00:46.797 --> 01:00:49.757
<i>Oh. that's gonna bring out
another safety car.</i>

1058
01:00:49.758 --> 01:00:52.802
<i>Given that each wing
costs more than £200.000.</i>

1059
01:00:52.803 --> 01:00:55.597
<i>I think the team might want
Sonny to start chipping in there.</i>

1060
01:00:56.223 --> 01:00:57.391
[chuckles]

1061
01:01:00.811 --> 01:01:03.062
[Joshua] Guys. it's another free stop.
Please tell me we're boxing.

1062
01:01:03.063 --> 01:01:04.605
[Rico] Uh. we're checking.

1063
01:01:04.606 --> 01:01:07.233
- Keep him out.
- Stay out. Stay out. You are staying out.

1064
01:01:07.234 --> 01:01:09.569
[Croft] <i>More drivers come in
to take fresh tires.</i>

1065
01:01:09.570 --> 01:01:13.907
<i>but still. Joshua Pearce remains on track.
He's moved up to P11.</i>

1066
01:01:16.743 --> 01:01:18.161
Look who's back.

1067
01:01:21.915 --> 01:01:23.625
I know. I know. Be ready.

1068
01:01:27.254 --> 01:01:28.422
What is he doing?

1069
01:01:30.173 --> 01:01:31.508
I think he's trying to score us a point.

1070
01:01:34.011 --> 01:01:36.221
[Sonny] Tell JP to save his tires.

1071
01:01:37.389 --> 01:01:40.057
Joshua. just take care of
your tires. okay?

1072
01:01:40.058 --> 01:01:41.851
You have to make them last.

1073
01:01:41.852 --> 01:01:44.730
[Joshua] Last? No shit. I will be.

1074
01:01:47.858 --> 01:01:50.651
[Brundle] <i>With four laps to go
in this stop-and-go race.</i>

1075
01:01:50.652 --> 01:01:51.903
<i>thanks to Sonny Hayes.</i>

1076
01:01:51.904 --> 01:01:54.739
<i>the driver helped most is his teammate.
now in tenth.</i>

1077
01:01:54.740 --> 01:01:57.743
<i>With a 12-second gap ahead of Stroll.</i>

1078
01:01:58.243 --> 01:02:00.203
Tell JP to maintain that gap.

1079
01:02:00.204 --> 01:02:01.455
<i>Keep pushing.</i>

1080
01:02:02.664 --> 01:02:05.208
[Joshua] My tires are gone. man.
What are you waiting for?

1081
01:02:05.209 --> 01:02:07.084
Copy that. We have to call it.

1082
01:02:07.085 --> 01:02:08.629
He's losing over a second every lap.

1083
01:02:09.338 --> 01:02:10.504
Stand by.

1084
01:02:10.505 --> 01:02:14.342
[Croft] <i>Into turn two. Hayes battles with
the Williams and pushes it wide.</i>

1085
01:02:14.343 --> 01:02:16.303
Seriously. what are we waiting for?

1086
01:02:19.848 --> 01:02:20.890
[Croft] <i>Sonny's off the track.</i>

1087
01:02:20.891 --> 01:02:23.726
<i>He's gone too far over.</i> [groans]

1088
01:02:23.727 --> 01:02:25.186
<i>And that's gonna cause damage.</i>

1089
01:02:25.187 --> 01:02:27.940
- Plan C.
- [laughs]

1090
01:02:28.565 --> 01:02:30.274
Oopsie. Sorry. guys.

1091
01:02:30.275 --> 01:02:34.278
[Croft] <i>That's the third safety car
involving the Apex GP driver.</i>

1092
01:02:34.279 --> 01:02:37.449
<i>bringing the Hungarian Grand Prix
to an absolute crawl.</i>

1093
01:02:37.991 --> 01:02:40.159
A sub three-second stop.
and he'll keep P10.

1094
01:02:40.160 --> 01:02:41.577
Box. Joshua. Box. box. box.

1095
01:02:41.578 --> 01:02:43.205
[Joshua] Copy. Coming in.

1096
01:02:45.624 --> 01:02:46.832
What did you say?

1097
01:02:46.833 --> 01:02:49.377
[Brundle] <i>Joshua Pearce
finally gets to pit.</i>

1098
01:02:49.378 --> 01:02:53.131
[Croft] <i>And with a quick stop here.
he could stay in the top ten.</i>

1099
01:03:01.014 --> 01:03:02.056
[grunts]

1100
01:03:02.057 --> 01:03:04.141
[Brundle] <i>This is critical.</i>

1101
01:03:04.142 --> 01:03:08.564
<i>Pearce must beat Stroll to the
pit exit line to maintain tenth place.</i>

1102
01:03:10.107 --> 01:03:11.399
[Croft] <i>And he's done it!</i>

1103
01:03:11.400 --> 01:03:15.236
<i>With yellow flags out. all the cars
are forced to hold track position.</i>

1104
01:03:15.237 --> 01:03:17.446
- <i>meaning that thanks to Sonny Hayes...</i>
- [Joshua] Let's go!

1105
01:03:17.447 --> 01:03:19.740
- <i>...the race ends under a safety car.</i>
- Yeah!

1106
01:03:19.741 --> 01:03:21.660
- Vegas!
- What? Whoa!

1107
01:03:22.619 --> 01:03:24.913
Hey. yeah. Fuck you. [laughs]

1108
01:03:26.999 --> 01:03:29.333
Yeah! [laughs. grunts]

1109
01:03:29.334 --> 01:03:30.751
Yes. baby!

1110
01:03:30.752 --> 01:03:33.839
[crowd cheering]

1111
01:03:41.763 --> 01:03:43.431
[Joshua chuckles] You're crazy. bro.

1112
01:03:43.432 --> 01:03:46.059
[Sonny] It's just tenth.
What are you smiling about?

1113
01:03:48.395 --> 01:03:50.229
[Croft] <i>And behind our podium placings.</i>

1114
01:03:50.230 --> 01:03:52.899
<i>Hamilton and Piastri
complete the top five.</i>

1115
01:03:52.900 --> 01:03:54.775
- <i>and Joshua Pearce in tenth...</i>
- Wow.

1116
01:03:54.776 --> 01:03:57.486
- <i>...scoring Expensify Apex GP...</i>
- Yeah. baby.

1117
01:03:57.487 --> 01:03:59.156
<i>...their first ever point.</i>

1118
01:04:01.408 --> 01:04:04.035
Did you see me? Crazy. right?

1119
01:04:04.036 --> 01:04:06.954
- [Sonny] A deal's a deal. I finished.
- Yeah. in last place.

1120
01:04:06.955 --> 01:04:08.999
Sounds great when you say it.

1121
01:04:15.172 --> 01:04:17.131
[interviewer] I know you have to go
see the stewards later.

1122
01:04:17.132 --> 01:04:18.799
what do you think they're
gonna make of your race today?

1123
01:04:18.800 --> 01:04:20.968
Well. I have to admit.
you guys got this one right.

1124
01:04:20.969 --> 01:04:23.805
- I'm. like... Thank you. Thank you.
- Good job. Yeah.

1125
01:04:24.348 --> 01:04:27.391
I'm still a bit rusty and. you know.
finding my way with this car.

1126
01:04:27.392 --> 01:04:28.893
but I'm confident we'll get there.

1127
01:04:28.894 --> 01:04:32.855
A rope-a-dope at Silverstone.
a demolition derby here in Hungary...

1128
01:04:32.856 --> 01:04:34.232
You've been banned from casinos.

1129
01:04:34.233 --> 01:04:36.692
Are you trying to get banned from F1?
Take the whole team down with you?

1130
01:04:36.693 --> 01:04:39.070
Tell you what. Don.
what do you say we make a bet?

1131
01:04:39.071 --> 01:04:41.322
Your £10 against my 10 grand.

1132
01:04:41.323 --> 01:04:44.242
We place at Monza. I win your 10.
We don't. you win mine.

1133
01:04:44.243 --> 01:04:45.910
- [scoffs]
- Let's do this. man.

1134
01:04:45.911 --> 01:04:47.287
Put your money where your mouth is.

1135
01:04:48.830 --> 01:04:50.414
What the hell? I'll take that.

1136
01:04:50.415 --> 01:04:52.250
- Thank you.
- Thank you so much.

1137
01:04:52.251 --> 01:04:54.919
Hey. No more press.

1138
01:04:54.920 --> 01:04:57.171
No. Sonny. you don't wanna make
the media your enemy.

1139
01:04:57.172 --> 01:04:58.506
And you'll be fined.

1140
01:04:58.507 --> 01:04:59.716
Take it out of my paycheck.

1141
01:05:00.300 --> 01:05:01.677
We don't pay you enough.

1142
01:05:02.803 --> 01:05:04.263
You know. I have to say.

1143
01:05:05.764 --> 01:05:06.807
I kinda like it.

1144
01:05:08.183 --> 01:05:11.519
It's very sort of punk rock for the brand.

1145
01:05:11.520 --> 01:05:12.854
[Peter sighs]

1146
01:05:14.606 --> 01:05:15.607
[Ruben] Hmm.

1147
01:05:24.408 --> 01:05:25.659
Let's run it again.

1148
01:05:34.126 --> 01:05:35.460
How long's he been in there?

1149
01:05:36.044 --> 01:05:39.631
All day. Playing with different
tire pressures. ride heights.

1150
01:05:40.966 --> 01:05:42.217
What were his times?

1151
01:05:42.718 --> 01:05:43.802
He found half a second.

1152
01:05:49.433 --> 01:05:50.767
Give me the same setup as him.

1153
01:05:51.476 --> 01:05:53.645
[typing]

1154
01:06:12.331 --> 01:06:14.290
It must be late. I'm seeing double.

1155
01:06:14.291 --> 01:06:15.375
[Kate chuckles]

1156
01:06:16.418 --> 01:06:18.879
A deal's a deal.
I'm building her for combat.

1157
01:06:20.422 --> 01:06:21.505
At the Dutch Grand Prix.

1158
01:06:21.506 --> 01:06:25.968
you'll be entering the Tarzan Corner
at 322 kilometers per hour.

1159
01:06:25.969 --> 01:06:28.221
Yeah. Too late to change my mind?

1160
01:06:28.222 --> 01:06:29.932
- Yeah.
- [chuckles]

1161
01:06:36.355 --> 01:06:38.147
To answer your question.

1162
01:06:38.148 --> 01:06:41.902
I was in aerospace at Lockheed
when Ruben came in and...

1163
01:06:42.903 --> 01:06:44.987
He liked my work. liked my attitude.

1164
01:06:44.988 --> 01:06:49.201
and he sold me on the thrill of fighting
to the death for a tenth of a second.

1165
01:06:50.410 --> 01:06:53.747
Traveling the world. the roar of a crowd...

1166
01:06:54.331 --> 01:06:57.376
So. I ran the idea past my husband.

1167
01:06:59.962 --> 01:07:02.756
Who swiftly became my ex-husband.

1168
01:07:05.175 --> 01:07:06.176
Good night.

1169
01:07:07.135 --> 01:07:08.136
Good night.

1170
01:07:30.826 --> 01:07:33.160
[line ringing]

1171
01:07:33.161 --> 01:07:34.746
[Ruben] <i>Do you know what time it is?</i>

1172
01:07:35.581 --> 01:07:36.873
All right.

1173
01:07:36.874 --> 01:07:38.458
Tell me about the kid.

1174
01:07:45.299 --> 01:07:47.174
Okay. here's another one my dad would say.

1175
01:07:47.175 --> 01:07:49.386
"Slow is smooth. smooth is fast."

1176
01:07:50.304 --> 01:07:52.680
For what it's worth. One more time around?

1177
01:07:52.681 --> 01:07:55.850
- Just one? Come on. Is that all?
- [Sonny chuckles]

1178
01:07:55.851 --> 01:07:57.435
- [grunts]
- I'd never live with myself.

1179
01:07:57.436 --> 01:07:59.937
if I can't keep up with you. Mr. 1990s.

1180
01:07:59.938 --> 01:08:01.565
- [chuckles]
- Let's go!

1181
01:08:02.107 --> 01:08:04.442
Joining us today.
we have Kaspar Smolinski.

1182
01:08:04.443 --> 01:08:06.652
Zak Brown and Fred Vasseur.

1183
01:08:06.653 --> 01:08:10.156
Now. Kaspar. can we start with you.
after what was a fantastic result

1184
01:08:10.157 --> 01:08:12.575
- for the team in Hungary last time out...
- Thank you.

1185
01:08:12.576 --> 01:08:17.872
...but Sonny has got you skirting the line
of penalties and violations.

1186
01:08:17.873 --> 01:08:20.166
Is this your only strategy.

1187
01:08:20.167 --> 01:08:23.168
and have you got any spare parts left
in the factory?

1188
01:08:23.169 --> 01:08:24.753
[audience chuckling]

1189
01:08:24.754 --> 01:08:26.213
We compete like everybody else.

1190
01:08:26.214 --> 01:08:27.632
Race models change.

1191
01:08:27.633 --> 01:08:29.301
We must adapt. huh?

1192
01:08:29.885 --> 01:08:31.427
Well. Zak. can we bring you in on this?

1193
01:08:31.428 --> 01:08:36.642
Because you've faced Hayes before.
you know the gray areas in which he works.

1194
01:08:37.392 --> 01:08:40.603
Certainly do. Uh. first of all.
he's a lot grayer now.

1195
01:08:40.604 --> 01:08:42.688
- [audience chuckles]
- And. uh. we keep tabs on him.

1196
01:08:42.689 --> 01:08:44.065
you know. back there behind us.

1197
01:08:44.066 --> 01:08:47.235
- [audience chuckles]
- And Fred. any concerns from Ferrari?

1198
01:08:47.236 --> 01:08:49.404
What does Ferrari think of Apex?

1199
01:08:50.155 --> 01:08:53.199
- We don't.
- [audience chuckling]

1200
01:08:53.200 --> 01:08:55.202
["Hold Me" playing]

1201
01:09:07.214 --> 01:09:12.135
[fans clamoring] Sonny! You're the best!

1202
01:09:14.137 --> 01:09:16.972
[Kate] A better qualifying yesterday
gets us in the thick of things.

1203
01:09:16.973 --> 01:09:19.516
P10. P15. [inhales sharply]

1204
01:09:19.517 --> 01:09:21.310
So we're gonna go for a two stop.

1205
01:09:21.311 --> 01:09:26.190
Medium-hard-medium. that's plan A.
Final stint. we go hards for plan B.

1206
01:09:26.191 --> 01:09:28.568
So. on this.
do you have any track concerns?

1207
01:09:28.569 --> 01:09:30.654
Don't look at me. Look at him.

1208
01:09:32.446 --> 01:09:33.699
It's good for JP.

1209
01:09:34.241 --> 01:09:35.241
Start me on hards.

1210
01:09:36.118 --> 01:09:38.828
Nah. the track's cooled down.
You won't have any grip.

1211
01:09:38.829 --> 01:09:40.205
That's right.

1212
01:09:40.873 --> 01:09:43.624
For three weeks.
all the talk's been how reckless I am.

1213
01:09:44.209 --> 01:09:46.793
Everyone's wondering
if I'm gonna drive 'em off track.

1214
01:09:46.794 --> 01:09:49.339
which means no one's
gonna be watching out for him.

1215
01:09:51.466 --> 01:09:55.012
Today. you win us this race.

1216
01:10:02.311 --> 01:10:05.646
[Croft] <i>Twenty laps down here at Monza.
and the pack have been split.</i>

1217
01:10:05.647 --> 01:10:08.441
<i>The leaders are pulling away.
led by Max Verstappen.</i>

1218
01:10:08.442 --> 01:10:10.985
<i>with Joshua Pearce back in P10.</i>

1219
01:10:10.986 --> 01:10:13.779
[Brundle] <i>Meanwhile. Sonny Hayes
is holding up the rest of the pack.</i>

1220
01:10:13.780 --> 01:10:16.200
<i>stuck behind him in a DRS train.</i>

1221
01:10:17.159 --> 01:10:20.828
[Croft] <i>Pearce looks to be in
a great position to finish in the top ten.</i>

1222
01:10:20.829 --> 01:10:23.832
<i>and maybe even a run to the podium.</i>

1223
01:10:25.918 --> 01:10:28.085
[Brundle] <i>But there's still a long way
to go in this race.</i>

1224
01:10:28.086 --> 01:10:32.132
<i>and with rain potentially forecast.
anything can happen.</i>

1225
01:10:32.716 --> 01:10:34.091
Tires are gone. Coming in.

1226
01:10:34.092 --> 01:10:35.510
Yeah. copy. Box. Box.

1227
01:10:36.094 --> 01:10:38.596
[Croft] <i>Apex GP is prepping
a fresh set of tires for Hayes.</i>

1228
01:10:38.597 --> 01:10:42.433
<i>That's gonna bring in
all the other teams to avoid the undercut.</i>

1229
01:10:42.434 --> 01:10:44.101
Uh. changed my mind.

1230
01:10:44.102 --> 01:10:47.730
[Croft] <i>But. no! He's staying out.
with the cars behind him all scrambling</i>

1231
01:10:47.731 --> 01:10:52.276
<i>to get on fresh tires that apparently
he doesn't think he needs anymore.</i>

1232
01:10:52.277 --> 01:10:54.862
Should we just do the opposite
of what he tells us to do?

1233
01:10:54.863 --> 01:10:56.907
Stand by till I lose my tires.

1234
01:10:57.950 --> 01:11:01.036
- I thought he had lost his tires.
- [stammers] I think he means literally.

1235
01:11:03.997 --> 01:11:05.998
Puncture. left rear. Coming in.

1236
01:11:05.999 --> 01:11:08.042
[Croft] <i>And there goes Hayes's tires.</i>

1237
01:11:08.043 --> 01:11:10.545
[Brundle] <i>That's quite a mess.
gravel on the track.</i>

1238
01:11:10.546 --> 01:11:14.006
<i>That will bring out the virtual safety car
for a quick sweep.</i>

1239
01:11:14.007 --> 01:11:15.550
[Croft] <i>So the race gets neutralized.</i>

1240
01:11:15.551 --> 01:11:19.345
<i>Everyone slows down
to 40% of their racing speed.</i>

1241
01:11:19.346 --> 01:11:21.430
<i>and all the race strategies
will get a reset.</i>

1242
01:11:21.431 --> 01:11:24.559
[Brundle] <i>And that is why this is
the perfect time to take a pit stop.</i>

1243
01:11:24.560 --> 01:11:26.018
<i>While you're in the pit lane.</i>

1244
01:11:26.019 --> 01:11:29.146
<i>your opponents
are restricted to a much slower pace</i>

1245
01:11:29.147 --> 01:11:31.941
<i>and you're not going to lose
as much track position when you rejoin.</i>

1246
01:11:31.942 --> 01:11:35.278
- I take it I'm staying out. right?
- Copy. Joshua. stay out. Stay out.

1247
01:11:35.279 --> 01:11:38.030
- <i>We want you out to gain track position.</i>
- Copy.

1248
01:11:38.031 --> 01:11:40.117
Up is down. down is up.

1249
01:11:47.082 --> 01:11:50.334
[Croft] <i>Sonny Hayes hesitated
before he left his pit box.</i>

1250
01:11:50.335 --> 01:11:53.254
<i>and he's come out just in front
of Max Verstappen.</i>

1251
01:11:53.255 --> 01:11:54.589
[Max] That was naughty.

1252
01:11:54.590 --> 01:11:56.883
[Brundle] <i>Hayes has slowed a bit
in the pit lane.</i>

1253
01:11:56.884 --> 01:12:00.928
<i>which will cost the Red Bull
and the two Ferraris precious time.</i>

1254
01:12:00.929 --> 01:12:02.221
Push. Joshua. Push.

1255
01:12:02.222 --> 01:12:03.848
<i>You are now P4. P4.</i>

1256
01:12:03.849 --> 01:12:08.227
[Croft] <i>Who's coming up from behind?
Here he is. Joshua Pearce.</i>

1257
01:12:08.228 --> 01:12:10.104
- Let's see! Let's go!
- Yes!

1258
01:12:10.105 --> 01:12:11.814
- <i>This is all playing into his hands...</i>
- Wow.

1259
01:12:11.815 --> 01:12:14.275
<i>...at the moment.
Could be a dream afternoon.</i>

1260
01:12:14.276 --> 01:12:17.236
<i>But can Hayes hold Verstappen
for a little bit longer?</i>

1261
01:12:17.237 --> 01:12:20.364
<i>Verstappen tries into turn one.
nothing doing there.</i>

1262
01:12:20.365 --> 01:12:23.242
<i>Gets the better exit.
Through the Curva Grande we go.</i>

1263
01:12:23.243 --> 01:12:25.578
- Damn. he's good.
- <i>Verstappen's trying to get past.</i>

1264
01:12:25.579 --> 01:12:27.622
[Brundle] <i>Sonny Hayes
looking carefully in his mirrors.</i>

1265
01:12:27.623 --> 01:12:29.957
<i>He must let Max Verstappen through.</i>

1266
01:12:29.958 --> 01:12:31.667
Yeah. I deserved that.

1267
01:12:31.668 --> 01:12:34.045
[Brundle] <i>And Max shows his disapproval.</i>

1268
01:12:34.046 --> 01:12:37.798
<i>and I don't blame him. as they head down
towards the second chicane.</i>

1269
01:12:37.799 --> 01:12:40.509
[Croft]
<i>And through goes Joshua Pearce in P4.</i>

1270
01:12:40.510 --> 01:12:43.221
<i>now much closer to the front of the pack.</i>

1271
01:12:43.222 --> 01:12:44.306
[thunder rumbles]

1272
01:12:46.141 --> 01:12:48.935
[Brundle] <i>Just seven laps to go.
and here comes the rain.</i>

1273
01:12:48.936 --> 01:12:52.146
[Croft] <i>Let's see who plays it safe
with a switch to the intermediate tire.</i>

1274
01:12:52.147 --> 01:12:54.775
<i>and who might gamble
to stay out on slicks.</i>

1275
01:13:01.198 --> 01:13:02.990
It's getting tricky out here. guys.
What's the plan?

1276
01:13:02.991 --> 01:13:06.994
You're running P4. We think P2 and P3
are switching to inters for safety.

1277
01:13:06.995 --> 01:13:08.788
<i>and it looks like P1 is staying out.</i>

1278
01:13:08.789 --> 01:13:10.666
- <i>What do you wanna do?</i>
- What's Sonny gonna do?

1279
01:13:11.500 --> 01:13:12.917
Take a wild guess.

1280
01:13:12.918 --> 01:13:14.461
- [Joshua] <i>I'm staying out.</i>
- Copy that.

1281
01:13:15.629 --> 01:13:19.006
[Brundle] <i>And the two Ferraris
come in for intermediate tires.</i>

1282
01:13:19.007 --> 01:13:21.467
<i>Let's see who else
decides to play it safe.</i>

1283
01:13:21.468 --> 01:13:25.513
[Croft] <i>And as George Russell pits.
Joshua Pearce moves into P2.</i>

1284
01:13:25.514 --> 01:13:27.139
[cheering]

1285
01:13:27.140 --> 01:13:29.684
Sonny. Joshua is staying out on slicks.
If he can hold on and find a dry line.

1286
01:13:29.685 --> 01:13:30.851
he's gonna finish second.

1287
01:13:30.852 --> 01:13:31.979
Second's not enough.

1288
01:13:33.355 --> 01:13:34.481
Damn it.

1289
01:13:35.023 --> 01:13:36.732
Okay. coming in for inters.

1290
01:13:36.733 --> 01:13:39.444
- Inters. inters.
- Let's go! He's coming in!

1291
01:13:45.951 --> 01:13:48.328
- How far behind me are they?
- Thirty seconds.

1292
01:13:48.871 --> 01:13:50.746
Oh. my God.
He's gonna take out Verstappen.

1293
01:13:50.747 --> 01:13:52.582
Let me know
when they hit the main straight.

1294
01:13:52.583 --> 01:13:56.085
Don't tell him! They penalize both cars.
They will take the win away.

1295
01:13:56.086 --> 01:13:57.170
Just trust me. will ya?

1296
01:13:59.673 --> 01:14:01.674
I'm pushing but I can't catch him.

1297
01:14:01.675 --> 01:14:03.759
[Brundle] <i>As the race leaders
approach the main straight.</i>

1298
01:14:03.760 --> 01:14:07.138
<i>Sonny Hayes is in another standoff
over team strategy.</i>

1299
01:14:07.139 --> 01:14:08.724
- Now.
- No!

1300
01:14:09.975 --> 01:14:12.602
[Croft] <i>Finally.
Hayes back out onto the track.</i>

1301
01:14:12.603 --> 01:14:14.437
<i>and just in front of Verstappen.</i>

1302
01:14:14.438 --> 01:14:17.565
<i>Now he'll get a blue flag here
so Verstappen can get past.</i>

1303
01:14:17.566 --> 01:14:22.069
<i>but until then. the Dutch driver
is caught up in Hayes's dirty air.</i>

1304
01:14:22.070 --> 01:14:24.071
[Brundle] <i>With every turn he hangs on.</i>

1305
01:14:24.072 --> 01:14:26.657
<i>he slows Verstappen
a fraction of a second.</i>

1306
01:14:26.658 --> 01:14:30.161
<i>providing Joshua Pearce
one last chance to catch up.</i>

1307
01:14:30.162 --> 01:14:31.455
I can see him. I'm almost there.

1308
01:14:33.373 --> 01:14:34.373
Tell JP to follow me.

1309
01:14:34.374 --> 01:14:38.462
- Copy. Uh. Joshua. Sonny is your tow.
- I'm right behind him.

1310
01:14:39.630 --> 01:14:41.255
[Croft] <i>Verstappen pulls away then.</i>

1311
01:14:41.256 --> 01:14:44.133
<i>But now. onto the rear wing
of his teammate's car</i>

1312
01:14:44.134 --> 01:14:45.551
<i>comes Joshua Pearce.</i>

1313
01:14:45.552 --> 01:14:48.054
[Brundle] <i>Pearce picks up
the slipstream from Hayes.</i>

1314
01:14:48.055 --> 01:14:51.225
<i>gaining time.
but driving blind in the spray.</i>

1315
01:14:53.894 --> 01:14:56.021
Come on. Stay with me. Stay with me now.

1316
01:15:02.611 --> 01:15:03.778
Pass. Pass.

1317
01:15:03.779 --> 01:15:05.321
- Overtake him. Overtake.
- Copy.

1318
01:15:05.322 --> 01:15:10.159
[Croft] <i>He's been gaining. and boom!
Joshua Pearce slingshots past Sonny Hayes.</i>

1319
01:15:10.160 --> 01:15:13.329
- <i>and now is in striking distance of P1.</i>
- [cheering]

1320
01:15:13.330 --> 01:15:15.873
Tell JP to wait for the straight
into turn one.

1321
01:15:15.874 --> 01:15:17.333
Be patient.

1322
01:15:17.334 --> 01:15:19.544
- <i>Straight at turn one.</i>
- [crew member] Copy.

1323
01:15:19.545 --> 01:15:23.882
Joshua. Sonny says wait for the straight.
The straight into turn one.

1324
01:15:25.384 --> 01:15:27.176
[Joshua] I'm right there.

1325
01:15:27.177 --> 01:15:28.470
I've got him.

1326
01:15:29.346 --> 01:15:31.764
[Brundle] <i>Pearce is right on the gearbox
of Verstappen.</i>

1327
01:15:31.765 --> 01:15:34.684
<i>down the back straight
at over 200 miles an hour.</i>

1328
01:15:34.685 --> 01:15:36.186
I see an opening. Going for it.

1329
01:15:36.812 --> 01:15:38.897
[Brundle] <i>The rookie attacks in 11.</i>

1330
01:15:39.398 --> 01:15:40.399
No. no!

1331
01:15:41.858 --> 01:15:43.568
[Croft]
<i>Pearce pulls alongside the Red Bull.</i>

1332
01:15:43.569 --> 01:15:46.362
<i>he's wheels ahead.
for the first time ever...</i>

1333
01:15:46.363 --> 01:15:49.365
<i>Apex GP... Oh. no!</i>

1334
01:15:49.366 --> 01:15:50.826
<i>No!</i>

1335
01:16:09.636 --> 01:16:12.097
- [sad music playing]
- [no audible dialogue]

1336
01:17:05.234 --> 01:17:10.030
[monitor beeping]

1337
01:17:18.330 --> 01:17:20.666
[reporter speaking Italian on television]

1338
01:17:23.794 --> 01:17:24.836
[sighs]

1339
01:17:26.755 --> 01:17:28.674
[sighs. in English] For God's sake.

1340
01:17:37.975 --> 01:17:40.601
- [Ruben] Bernadette. how's he doing?
- [Bernadette grunts]

1341
01:17:40.602 --> 01:17:41.936
He's stable.

1342
01:17:41.937 --> 01:17:43.689
He's resting now.

1343
01:17:44.690 --> 01:17:46.441
[exhales heavily. mutters]

1344
01:17:47.067 --> 01:17:48.651
Very happy to hear it.

1345
01:17:48.652 --> 01:17:51.237
I'm so sorry for what happened.
It was clearly--

1346
01:17:51.238 --> 01:17:53.490
Sonny. over here. please.

1347
01:18:00.080 --> 01:18:01.540
[sighing]

1348
01:18:08.005 --> 01:18:10.840
Um. I just wanna say I've been--

1349
01:18:10.841 --> 01:18:12.509
Joshua says you're an asshole.

1350
01:18:15.137 --> 01:18:16.637
Yeah. that tracks.

1351
01:18:16.638 --> 01:18:19.099
I think you're a dangerous asshole.

1352
01:18:21.059 --> 01:18:23.686
- Ms. Pearce--
- You're part of the same team. right?

1353
01:18:23.687 --> 01:18:24.979
Looking out for each other.

1354
01:18:24.980 --> 01:18:27.773
Except you had him
doing something so dangerous

1355
01:18:27.774 --> 01:18:30.027
it almost got him killed.

1356
01:18:31.486 --> 01:18:34.531
- Okay. listen--
- No. you listen to me.

1357
01:18:35.365 --> 01:18:37.284
This is my son.

1358
01:18:38.410 --> 01:18:40.661
And if anything...
anything else happens to him.

1359
01:18:40.662 --> 01:18:42.079
I'm coming after you.

1360
01:18:42.080 --> 01:18:44.749
And you better pray I don't put you
in a bed next to Joshua

1361
01:18:44.750 --> 01:18:46.877
for a very. very long time.

1362
01:18:47.628 --> 01:18:48.629
Clear?

1363
01:18:51.089 --> 01:18:52.424
Sure.

1364
01:18:56.428 --> 01:18:57.930
[sighs]

1365
01:19:06.230 --> 01:19:09.024
[reporters murmuring. clamoring]

1366
01:19:09.858 --> 01:19:10.983
Sonny. Sonny.

1367
01:19:10.984 --> 01:19:13.946
Do you think Joshua blames you
for what happened in Monza?

1368
01:19:17.658 --> 01:19:20.618
- [reporters clamoring]
- [reporter] Sonny. come on.

1369
01:19:20.619 --> 01:19:22.995
It was clear
that you were running his race.

1370
01:19:22.996 --> 01:19:26.624
Look. you kept him out on slick tires.
in dangerous conditions.

1371
01:19:26.625 --> 01:19:30.378
that even if you told him not to pass.
wasn't the accident inevitable?

1372
01:19:30.379 --> 01:19:32.505
- If I may. If I may.
- [reporters clamoring]

1373
01:19:32.506 --> 01:19:34.632
Joshua's back home. recovering.

1374
01:19:34.633 --> 01:19:36.884
We are expecting his return
in a few weeks.

1375
01:19:36.885 --> 01:19:42.807
Until that moment. our reserve driver.
Luca Cortez right there. will drive and...

1376
01:19:42.808 --> 01:19:45.477
- Next man up.
- [clamoring] Answer the question!

1377
01:19:47.854 --> 01:19:50.940
[Buxton] <i>A chaotic week
for Expensify Apex GP.</i>

1378
01:19:50.941 --> 01:19:53.901
<i>and again. it's Sonny Hayes at the center.</i>

1379
01:19:53.902 --> 01:19:57.655
<i>Many are blaming him for his teammate's
horrific accident at Monza.</i>

1380
01:19:57.656 --> 01:20:02.243
<i>His high-stakes. gambling style of racing
has the whole grid on edge.</i>

1381
01:20:02.244 --> 01:20:06.163
<i>and while the controversy continues
over who was to blame.</i>

1382
01:20:06.164 --> 01:20:09.750
<i>doctors have said that Pearce
will miss the next three races.</i>

1383
01:20:09.751 --> 01:20:14.172
<i>due to the burns suffered on his hands
as he begins his road to recovery.</i>

1384
01:20:21.680 --> 01:20:24.057
[Kate] <i>Today. we're going
with our combat upgrade.</i>

1385
01:20:24.725 --> 01:20:28.144
<i>The revised shapes will improve
the flow field under the floor.</i>

1386
01:20:28.145 --> 01:20:32.106
<i>allowing us to run in dirty air
with minimal loss of performance.</i>

1387
01:20:32.107 --> 01:20:34.902
Means we have to keep the field close
at all times.

1388
01:20:35.402 --> 01:20:38.739
and as for this week's plan C...

1389
01:20:44.786 --> 01:20:48.497
They've docked us to the back of the grid
'cause they don't like the way we drive.

1390
01:20:48.498 --> 01:20:50.542
Fine. Fuck 'em.

1391
01:20:51.460 --> 01:20:54.670
'Cause if we can pick up
a tenth of a second from you.

1392
01:20:54.671 --> 01:20:58.424
and from you. and you. and me...

1393
01:20:58.425 --> 01:21:01.219
If everyone in this room
can make one critical contribution.

1394
01:21:01.220 --> 01:21:02.596
that's a second every lap.

1395
01:21:03.305 --> 01:21:07.851
And after 72 laps. that's the difference
between last and first.

1396
01:21:09.895 --> 01:21:11.021
Plan C...

1397
01:21:12.648 --> 01:21:14.316
Plan C's for combat.

1398
01:21:16.818 --> 01:21:21.656
Combat. combat. combat.

1399
01:21:21.657 --> 01:21:27.453
[crew chanting] Combat. combat.
combat. combat.

1400
01:21:27.454 --> 01:21:29.163
[chanting continues]

1401
01:21:29.164 --> 01:21:30.414
[driving electronic song playing]

1402
01:21:30.415 --> 01:21:34.502
<i>♪ I don't wanna lose my mind
I don't wanna lose myself ♪</i>

1403
01:21:34.503 --> 01:21:38.881
<i>♪ Tell me if I crossed a line
I ain't trying to hurt myself ♪</i>

1404
01:21:38.882 --> 01:21:44.095
<i>♪ Didn't want to call your name
Only got myself to blame ♪</i>

1405
01:21:44.096 --> 01:21:45.846
<i>♪ Oh. yeah ♪</i>

1406
01:21:45.847 --> 01:21:48.099
<i>♪ In my world. in my mind
Always running out of time ♪</i>

1407
01:21:48.100 --> 01:21:49.267
[crowd cheering]

1408
01:21:49.268 --> 01:21:51.435
[Croft] <i>And that's Hayes
in the upgraded Apex.</i>

1409
01:21:51.436 --> 01:21:54.855
<i>Now the team were penalized
back to last place after Monza.</i>

1410
01:21:54.856 --> 01:21:59.193
<i>but here he is. coming from the cellar.
passing his new teammate. Luca Cortez.</i>

1411
01:21:59.194 --> 01:22:01.654
<i>♪ ...still I wait for you ♪</i>

1412
01:22:01.655 --> 01:22:03.239
[vocalizes]

1413
01:22:03.240 --> 01:22:04.782
<i>♪ Yeah. it feels... ♪</i>

1414
01:22:04.783 --> 01:22:07.743
[Croft] <i>Round the banking.
Hayes has got past Ocon.</i>

1415
01:22:07.744 --> 01:22:11.581
<i>This is brilliant last lap drama.
What a fantastic finish.</i>

1416
01:22:11.582 --> 01:22:13.166
[laughs]

1417
01:22:14.960 --> 01:22:16.502
[exclaims. chuckles]

1418
01:22:16.503 --> 01:22:21.507
<i>♪ Ain't no way to tell
Which way it's gonna go ♪</i>

1419
01:22:21.508 --> 01:22:25.052
<i>♪ But it feels ♪</i>

1420
01:22:25.053 --> 01:22:29.015
<i>♪ So good I might just lose my mind ♪</i>

1421
01:22:29.016 --> 01:22:33.270
<i>♪ No question if it's wrong or right ♪</i>

1422
01:22:33.854 --> 01:22:37.524
<i>♪ And now it's too late
No way to take it slow ♪</i>

1423
01:22:48.076 --> 01:22:50.536
[Brundle] <i>Another fearless attack
from Hayes.</i>

1424
01:22:50.537 --> 01:22:53.456
<i>And here's where the Apex GP
has found strength.</i>

1425
01:22:53.457 --> 01:22:56.710
<i>Three-tenths gained every lap.
and in the corners alone.</i>

1426
01:22:57.377 --> 01:23:00.713
<i>♪ I don't wanna lose my mind
I don't wanna lose myself ♪</i>

1427
01:23:00.714 --> 01:23:02.590
[Croft] <i>Scrapping away on the last lap.</i>

1428
01:23:02.591 --> 01:23:05.927
<i>Sonny Hayes gets the inside line.
but he can't quite get past.</i>

1429
01:23:05.928 --> 01:23:08.638
<i>George Russell will hang on here
for sixth place.</i>

1430
01:23:08.639 --> 01:23:12.016
<i>but this is Apex GP's best ever finish.</i>

1431
01:23:12.017 --> 01:23:15.478
- <i>It's a valiant seventh.</i>
- Combat. I love it!

1432
01:23:15.479 --> 01:23:18.522
[crowd cheering]

1433
01:23:18.523 --> 01:23:20.317
[manager] Every race you miss.
fans just forget you.

1434
01:23:21.068 --> 01:23:23.320
Sonny always seems to be one step ahead.

1435
01:23:24.738 --> 01:23:28.366
You never know.
Sonny may be a saboteur. Josh.

1436
01:23:28.367 --> 01:23:29.534
<i>He may be a saboteur.</i>

1437
01:23:29.535 --> 01:23:31.327
- [crowd cheering]
- [song continues]

1438
01:23:31.328 --> 01:23:34.497
<i>♪ Yeah it feels ♪</i>

1439
01:23:34.498 --> 01:23:38.876
<i>♪ So good I might just lose my mind ♪</i>

1440
01:23:38.877 --> 01:23:41.546
<i>♪ No question if it's wrong or right ♪</i>

1441
01:23:41.547 --> 01:23:44.131
[Croft] <i>...and they go wheel to wheel.
Verstappen and Leclerc.</i>

1442
01:23:44.132 --> 01:23:47.426
<i>Verstappen will have the inside.
Perez goes round the outside.</i>

1443
01:23:47.427 --> 01:23:49.845
<i>Perez makes contact with Charles Leclerc</i>

1444
01:23:49.846 --> 01:23:54.393
<i>as Sonny Hayes threads that Apex GP car
through the midfield.</i>

1445
01:24:05.445 --> 01:24:06.737
<i>♪ Yeah ♪</i>

1446
01:24:06.738 --> 01:24:08.656
<i>♪ Bounce back
When the bottles is on me ♪</i>

1447
01:24:08.657 --> 01:24:11.033
<i>♪ I'm pushin' a new pen
Rewriting the story ♪</i>

1448
01:24:11.034 --> 01:24:13.119
<i>♪ Hello to my old ways
Goodbye to the nosebleeds ♪</i>

1449
01:24:13.120 --> 01:24:15.913
<i>♪ You fighting to stay here
You probably OD'ing ♪</i>

1450
01:24:15.914 --> 01:24:18.082
<i>♪ Ain't finna pop for no reason ♪</i>

1451
01:24:18.083 --> 01:24:20.001
<i>♪ I don't throw shots. I run legions ♪</i>

1452
01:24:20.002 --> 01:24:21.711
<i>♪ I been goin' over the top
Where no queen been ♪</i>

1453
01:24:21.712 --> 01:24:23.713
<i>♪ Die with with no regrets
This is my season ♪</i>

1454
01:24:23.714 --> 01:24:25.464
[Croft] <i>Talk about leaving it late.</i>

1455
01:24:25.465 --> 01:24:29.427
<i>Hayes squeezes through on the inside.
and with a run to the line now.</i>

1456
01:24:29.428 --> 01:24:32.430
<i>for their best position ever. P5.</i>

1457
01:24:32.431 --> 01:24:34.432
[Brundle] <i>Give the design team a bonus.</i>

1458
01:24:34.433 --> 01:24:37.184
<i>because the upgrade
has completely changed this car.</i>

1459
01:24:37.185 --> 01:24:39.437
[Croft] <i>And if Joshua Pearce is watching.</i>

1460
01:24:39.438 --> 01:24:42.440
<i>well. he must be thinking.
"What might have been?"</i>

1461
01:24:42.441 --> 01:24:44.400
<i>♪ Yeah. it feels ♪</i>

1462
01:24:44.401 --> 01:24:47.945
<i>♪ So good I might just lose my mind ♪</i>

1463
01:24:47.946 --> 01:24:50.072
He's treating you like a pawn. Josh.

1464
01:24:50.073 --> 01:24:53.827
- Be a knight! Be a knight! Be a knight!
- [bicycle bell ringing]

1465
01:24:57.831 --> 01:24:59.707
[Croft]
<i>Who would have believed this weeks ago?</i>

1466
01:24:59.708 --> 01:25:03.753
<i>Expensify Apex GP
has the racing world on notice.</i>

1467
01:25:03.754 --> 01:25:06.756
[crowd chanting] Apex! Apex! Apex!

1468
01:25:06.757 --> 01:25:09.259
[chanting continues]

1469
01:25:11.428 --> 01:25:16.933
[Brundle] <i>Someone call the 1990s.
Sonny Hayes. if you missed him. he's back.</i>

1470
01:25:16.934 --> 01:25:19.186
[song ends]

1471
01:25:24.066 --> 01:25:26.652
Last one up buys breakfast. [chuckles]

1472
01:25:27.361 --> 01:25:29.905
[indistinct chattering]

1473
01:25:34.701 --> 01:25:35.786
Look who's back.

1474
01:25:36.662 --> 01:25:40.916
[crew cheering. applauding]

1475
01:25:42.376 --> 01:25:43.418
Hello.

1476
01:25:50.467 --> 01:25:52.135
Good to have you back. JP. We missed you.

1477
01:25:53.345 --> 01:25:55.347
[dramatic rap song playing]

1478
01:26:03.605 --> 01:26:08.067
<i>♪ This for the underdogs
This for the underdogs. underdogs ♪</i>

1479
01:26:08.068 --> 01:26:11.946
<i>♪ Slide out the garage
I got a hundred cars ♪</i>

1480
01:26:11.947 --> 01:26:14.115
<i>♪ This for the underdogs ♪</i>

1481
01:26:14.116 --> 01:26:16.200
<i>♪ The teller just ask me
How I want the cashy ♪</i>

1482
01:26:16.201 --> 01:26:17.785
[crowd chanting] Apex! Apex! Apex! Apex!

1483
01:26:17.786 --> 01:26:19.412
<i>♪ I told 'em a hundred large ♪</i>

1484
01:26:19.413 --> 01:26:22.207
<i>♪ I want them gold wraps
Put it up double R ♪</i>

1485
01:26:23.333 --> 01:26:26.794
<i>♪ Tell 'em get out the way
4x4 big Phantom. supe ♪</i>

1486
01:26:26.795 --> 01:26:30.299
<i>♪ They thought I was canceled
I piped up and flipped the channel ♪</i>

1487
01:26:36.972 --> 01:26:39.640
[Croft] <i>It's lights out and away we go!</i>

1488
01:26:39.641 --> 01:26:41.225
<i>And it's a decent start.</i>

1489
01:26:41.226 --> 01:26:44.270
<i>and everyone keeping it clean
as into La Source we go.</i>

1490
01:26:44.271 --> 01:26:45.855
<i>Ferrari ahead of Red Bull.</i>

1491
01:26:45.856 --> 01:26:51.444
<i>but here the two Apex GP cars
looking to work together as a team.</i>

1492
01:26:51.445 --> 01:26:54.655
<i>It's a welcome back to the track
for Joshua Pearce.</i>

1493
01:26:54.656 --> 01:26:56.365
<i>and Sonny Hayes glad to see him.</i>

1494
01:26:56.366 --> 01:27:00.077
<i>as they slice their way
through positions four and five.</i>

1495
01:27:00.078 --> 01:27:02.122
<i>And onto the Kemmel Straight we go.</i>

1496
01:27:02.831 --> 01:27:07.293
<i>Now approaching top speed.
Sonny Hayes ahead of Joshua Pearce.</i>

1497
01:27:07.294 --> 01:27:10.880
<i>He's showing no ill effects
from that time off after the crash.</i>

1498
01:27:10.881 --> 01:27:14.508
<i>The car's working beautifully.
They're working as a team.</i>

1499
01:27:14.509 --> 01:27:18.429
<i>But hang on. Pearce right on his tail.
using the slipstream.</i>

1500
01:27:18.430 --> 01:27:20.848
<i>Is he about to try and overtake?</i>

1501
01:27:20.849 --> 01:27:23.684
<i>Into the chicane we go
and they touch wheels!</i>

1502
01:27:23.685 --> 01:27:25.686
- <i>This is disaster for Apex...</i>
- [exclaiming]

1503
01:27:25.687 --> 01:27:29.524
<i>...as out goes Sonny Hayes
and into the gravel!</i>

1504
01:27:30.984 --> 01:27:32.277
Assholes! [grunts]

1505
01:27:32.861 --> 01:27:35.404
[Brundle]
<i>What is happening with this team?</i>

1506
01:27:35.405 --> 01:27:39.743
<i>Their first race back together.
and they've run into each other.</i>

1507
01:27:41.870 --> 01:27:42.912
- You did great. Joshua.
- Well done. mate.

1508
01:27:42.913 --> 01:27:44.413
[laughs]

1509
01:27:44.414 --> 01:27:45.749
Whoo! [grunts]

1510
01:27:46.291 --> 01:27:48.584
You pull that shit again.
I will knock your teeth out.

1511
01:27:48.585 --> 01:27:50.419
Oh. no one gets past us
without a fight. right?

1512
01:27:50.420 --> 01:27:52.588
Oh. is this funny?
You think you got a seat next year?

1513
01:27:52.589 --> 01:27:54.715
'Cause you just cut your chances in half.

1514
01:27:54.716 --> 01:27:57.176
- That's how dumb you are.
- You failed. You failed!

1515
01:27:57.177 --> 01:27:58.971
- Why should I listen to you anyway. man?
- Hey.

1516
01:27:59.972 --> 01:28:01.097
[exhales heavily]

1517
01:28:01.098 --> 01:28:03.808
Look. man.
I don't give two shits about you.

1518
01:28:03.809 --> 01:28:06.143
You wanna sabotage your career.
you go right ahead.

1519
01:28:06.144 --> 01:28:08.563
I've seen hundreds of guys
with your talent come and go.

1520
01:28:08.564 --> 01:28:10.107
No one cares!

1521
01:28:10.983 --> 01:28:14.653
But you sabotage Ruben. who backed you?
You sabotage his team?

1522
01:28:16.071 --> 01:28:17.239
I won't let you do it.

1523
01:28:22.452 --> 01:28:25.955
- Thanks. coach. [laughs]
- Get your shit together!

1524
01:28:25.956 --> 01:28:28.709
So stupid! God...

1525
01:28:36.842 --> 01:28:38.301
[interviewer]
How would you sum up your race today?

1526
01:28:38.302 --> 01:28:41.262
Ooh. Um. it was good.

1527
01:28:41.263 --> 01:28:44.516
You know. the car feels great.
I think the team's done an amazing job.

1528
01:28:45.225 --> 01:28:47.311
It's just a shame
about the contact with Sonny.

1529
01:28:48.395 --> 01:28:49.688
You hate to see that happen.

1530
01:28:59.615 --> 01:29:01.241
[pants]

1531
01:29:12.753 --> 01:29:13.921
[sighs]

1532
01:29:17.257 --> 01:29:19.008
- [Joshua] Hey. how are you doing?
- [host] Hi. how are you?

1533
01:29:19.009 --> 01:29:20.552
Good. Sensational.

1534
01:29:22.930 --> 01:29:24.973
- Where's the team?
- Right this way. gentlemen.

1535
01:29:25.599 --> 01:29:26.850
[sighs]

1536
01:29:35.734 --> 01:29:38.654
Brilliant. you made it. Come on. Sit down.

1537
01:29:40.822 --> 01:29:42.573
Sonny. you know Joshua.

1538
01:29:42.574 --> 01:29:44.493
Joshua. Sonny.

1539
01:29:45.077 --> 01:29:46.994
So I'm sure you both
have heard the rumors. [sighs]

1540
01:29:46.995 --> 01:29:50.039
We all lose our jobs
if you can't pull off a miracle.

1541
01:29:50.040 --> 01:29:52.166
and that's starting with
staying on the bloody track.

1542
01:29:52.167 --> 01:29:54.293
Well. we were doing just fine
while JP was out.

1543
01:29:54.294 --> 01:29:55.711
I was out because I was listening to you.

1544
01:29:55.712 --> 01:29:57.213
- Ish.
- And please don't call me JP.

1545
01:29:57.214 --> 01:29:58.839
It's a nickname. You don't get to choose.

1546
01:29:58.840 --> 01:30:01.259
And your name doesn't even make sense.
Is it Sonny. is it Hayesie?

1547
01:30:01.260 --> 01:30:02.426
- We don't know. do we. Kate?
- [scoffs]

1548
01:30:02.427 --> 01:30:03.512
- [chuckles]
- [Kate] Lads.

1549
01:30:04.012 --> 01:30:05.347
Have I not delivered you a car?

1550
01:30:08.517 --> 01:30:10.476
So you can do one thing for me.

1551
01:30:10.477 --> 01:30:11.770
Cards.

1552
01:30:12.437 --> 01:30:14.273
Come on. I know you have 'em with ya.

1553
01:30:15.315 --> 01:30:17.233
It's my team meeting.
we're gonna do it my way.

1554
01:30:17.234 --> 01:30:19.193
- We're playing poker.
- [Joshua scoffs] Come on.

1555
01:30:19.194 --> 01:30:21.988
Yeah. Whoever wins gets to be
our number one driver tomorrow.

1556
01:30:21.989 --> 01:30:24.032
and if I win. I get to choose.

1557
01:30:26.118 --> 01:30:28.035
- Didn't he gamble for a living?
- Mm-hmm. yeah.

1558
01:30:28.036 --> 01:30:29.495
Now he's living in a van.

1559
01:30:29.496 --> 01:30:30.831
[chuckles]

1560
01:30:31.540 --> 01:30:32.541
Texas Hold'em?

1561
01:30:35.294 --> 01:30:36.879
["Just Cool" playing]

1562
01:30:41.174 --> 01:30:43.260
[Sonny speaks indistinctly]

1563
01:30:46.930 --> 01:30:49.223
So. Sonny here likes straight talk.

1564
01:30:49.224 --> 01:30:50.892
- [chuckles]
- Isn't that right. Sonny?

1565
01:30:50.893 --> 01:30:53.227
- [Sonny] Yeah. that's what I hear.
- [Kate] So. let's talk.

1566
01:30:53.228 --> 01:30:54.395
Who wants to go first?

1567
01:30:54.396 --> 01:30:56.188
- I'll go first.
- I'll go first.

1568
01:30:56.189 --> 01:30:57.857
No. I'll go first.

1569
01:30:57.858 --> 01:31:01.277
What's the difference between
Joshua Pearce and Sonny Hayes?

1570
01:31:01.278 --> 01:31:02.361
A lot of decades.

1571
01:31:02.362 --> 01:31:04.739
- Hard-won experience.
- Of living in a van?

1572
01:31:04.740 --> 01:31:06.032
Total freedom.

1573
01:31:06.033 --> 01:31:07.159
Total failure.

1574
01:31:07.868 --> 01:31:09.535
Says the guy who still lives with his mom.

1575
01:31:09.536 --> 01:31:11.037
Says the guy with two pair.

1576
01:31:11.038 --> 01:31:14.041
- Says the guy with trips.
- Says the guy with a full house.

1577
01:31:16.293 --> 01:31:18.085
- Girl.
- [Joshua scoffs]

1578
01:31:18.086 --> 01:31:19.921
Wait. I don't even live with my mum.

1579
01:31:19.922 --> 01:31:21.006
Okay.

1580
01:31:21.590 --> 01:31:23.090
She just cooks for me sometimes.

1581
01:31:23.091 --> 01:31:24.426
Mm-hmm.

1582
01:31:26.345 --> 01:31:29.096
If you'd any constructive criticism
for each other. what would it be?

1583
01:31:29.097 --> 01:31:30.891
- Don't be such an arsehole.
- Don't be such a dickhead.

1584
01:31:32.976 --> 01:31:33.976
That was constructive.

1585
01:31:33.977 --> 01:31:35.270
[scoffs]

1586
01:31:36.897 --> 01:31:39.358
You have a deficient frontal cortex.

1587
01:31:41.068 --> 01:31:42.944
- A what?
- You can't analyze risk.

1588
01:31:42.945 --> 01:31:46.405
It's not all your fault.
It's not fully formed yet at your age.

1589
01:31:46.406 --> 01:31:48.074
But come the day you learn patience.

1590
01:31:48.075 --> 01:31:50.244
- and stop being so immature. thinking--
- Patience.

1591
01:31:50.827 --> 01:31:52.329
- Patience is good.
- [Sonny] Patience.

1592
01:31:53.330 --> 01:31:54.581
Joshua.

1593
01:31:55.832 --> 01:31:58.209
He doesn't care about
what anyone else has to say but himself.

1594
01:31:58.210 --> 01:32:01.629
He just comes in and imposes his will
on all of us with no discussion.

1595
01:32:01.630 --> 01:32:04.340
He doesn't listen.
I'm trying. but he doesn't listen.

1596
01:32:04.341 --> 01:32:05.467
Mmm.

1597
01:32:06.051 --> 01:32:08.427
- Sonny?
- What?

1598
01:32:08.428 --> 01:32:09.972
[Joshua scoffs]

1599
01:32:10.806 --> 01:32:13.558
[sighs] Wow. [scoffs]

1600
01:32:13.559 --> 01:32:15.560
[sighs]

1601
01:32:15.561 --> 01:32:18.354
<i>♪ Why they lie to the people?
Why the world is so evil? ♪</i>

1602
01:32:18.355 --> 01:32:19.564
[no audible dialogue]

1603
01:32:19.565 --> 01:32:23.402
<i>♪ Why cant just cool?
Just let me cool ♪</i>

1604
01:32:23.986 --> 01:32:26.737
<i>♪ Walking explosives
Stressing all of the time ♪</i>

1605
01:32:26.738 --> 01:32:28.114
Who taught you how to play?

1606
01:32:28.115 --> 01:32:30.033
My dad liked to gamble.

1607
01:32:30.617 --> 01:32:33.035
- He make big bets too?
- Put a big one on me.

1608
01:32:33.036 --> 01:32:34.955
How old were you when your fathers died?

1609
01:32:39.501 --> 01:32:40.501
Sorry.

1610
01:32:40.502 --> 01:32:41.837
- Thirteen.
- Thirteen.

1611
01:32:44.548 --> 01:32:46.049
Huh.

1612
01:32:47.092 --> 01:32:48.301
Why do you race?

1613
01:32:48.302 --> 01:32:52.346
Money... [sighs]
...fame and free clothes. [chuckles]

1614
01:32:52.347 --> 01:32:54.640
Oh. my God. with the phone.
Put the thing down. will ya?

1615
01:32:54.641 --> 01:32:56.517
What do you care what they say?

1616
01:32:56.518 --> 01:32:58.394
Easy for you to say. They all love you.

1617
01:32:58.395 --> 01:32:59.730
It's just noise. man.

1618
01:33:01.273 --> 01:33:02.815
Drive the car.

1619
01:33:02.816 --> 01:33:04.192
You're really good at it.

1620
01:33:07.154 --> 01:33:08.447
You might be great.

1621
01:33:25.631 --> 01:33:28.841
<i>♪ Hyperbolic catastrophic scatterbrain ♪</i>

1622
01:33:28.842 --> 01:33:32.970
<i>♪ This is one diabolic catatonic parade ♪</i>

1623
01:33:32.971 --> 01:33:35.514
<i>♪ Everyone just go away
There's nothing new to celebrate ♪</i>

1624
01:33:35.515 --> 01:33:36.807
[Kate exhales heavily]

1625
01:33:36.808 --> 01:33:38.935
<i>♪ There's nowhere left to run away ♪</i>

1626
01:33:38.936 --> 01:33:42.939
<i>♪ They're closing off the open seas
They're locking off the runways ♪</i>

1627
01:33:42.940 --> 01:33:47.318
<i>♪ They keep telling me the one thing
So far from everything I see ♪</i>

1628
01:33:47.319 --> 01:33:48.736
<i>♪ Just go away ♪</i>

1629
01:33:48.737 --> 01:33:51.113
[groans] Yeah. [chuckles]

1630
01:33:51.114 --> 01:33:54.325
Look at that. huh?
Number one driver tomorrow.

1631
01:33:54.326 --> 01:33:55.910
- Bonding?
- [Joshua] Ooh.

1632
01:33:55.911 --> 01:33:56.994
Well. this is nice.

1633
01:33:56.995 --> 01:33:59.080
We gotta go. mate. Sponsor party at OMNIA.

1634
01:33:59.081 --> 01:34:00.332
Gotta steal ya.

1635
01:34:00.916 --> 01:34:02.833
Uh. Uncle Sonny.
you're welcome to come with--

1636
01:34:02.834 --> 01:34:04.503
Thank you. I'm good.
I have a race tomorrow.

1637
01:34:05.212 --> 01:34:08.173
- Cool. Kate?
- No. thank you.

1638
01:34:08.757 --> 01:34:10.466
- [manager] Come on.
- Thanks for this. Kate.

1639
01:34:10.467 --> 01:34:13.636
[manager] Come on. boy.
Uh... Uh. girls. you might have to...

1640
01:34:13.637 --> 01:34:15.680
We're gonna go dancing.
Should we go dancing?

1641
01:34:15.681 --> 01:34:17.641
- Yeah!
- [all clamoring]

1642
01:34:21.436 --> 01:34:23.397
[romantic pop song playing on speakers]

1643
01:34:29.736 --> 01:34:30.988
Listen.

1644
01:34:31.655 --> 01:34:33.240
let's get this straight. okay?

1645
01:34:33.991 --> 01:34:37.410
I don't mess around during the season.
and never with a member of my team.

1646
01:34:37.411 --> 01:34:39.204
and what I'm attracted to is winning.

1647
01:34:39.955 --> 01:34:41.707
And you just lost to a pair of fives.

1648
01:34:54.553 --> 01:34:59.849
<i>♪ So. baby. let's get messy
Let's get all the way undone ♪</i>

1649
01:34:59.850 --> 01:35:04.812
<i>♪ Come over. undress me
Just like I've never been touched ♪</i>

1650
01:35:04.813 --> 01:35:08.733
<i>♪ Baby. I'm obsessed with you
And there's no replica ♪</i>

1651
01:35:08.734 --> 01:35:11.944
<i>♪ Baby. let's get messy
Let's get all the way undone ♪</i>

1652
01:35:11.945 --> 01:35:13.530
[song continues as club remix]

1653
01:35:27.044 --> 01:35:29.046
[energetic pop song plays]

1654
01:35:30.839 --> 01:35:34.759
<i>♪ I wanna let my hair down
While I'm staring down your face ♪</i>

1655
01:35:34.760 --> 01:35:38.262
<i>♪ Wanna go till lights out
Take you right back to my place ♪</i>

1656
01:35:38.263 --> 01:35:41.641
<i>♪ You out your mind
If you don't know what this is ♪</i>

1657
01:35:41.642 --> 01:35:42.726
Hey.

1658
01:35:43.936 --> 01:35:45.395
You're a driver. aren't you?

1659
01:35:46.313 --> 01:35:47.855
- Yeah.
- Which team?

1660
01:35:47.856 --> 01:35:49.190
Apex GP.

1661
01:35:49.191 --> 01:35:51.818
Can you introduce me to Carlos Sainz?

1662
01:35:53.362 --> 01:35:54.487
I'll go get him.

1663
01:35:54.488 --> 01:35:55.571
<i>♪ Move from the back ♪</i>

1664
01:35:55.572 --> 01:35:57.573
<i>♪ Eyes on me
How you like that ♪</i>

1665
01:35:57.574 --> 01:35:59.368
<i>♪ Just like this
Here for the night ♪</i>

1666
01:36:00.327 --> 01:36:02.161
Oh. hey. Hey.

1667
01:36:02.162 --> 01:36:05.122
Oi. why do they say this place is weird?
I like this. bruv.

1668
01:36:05.123 --> 01:36:07.500
Glad you're having fun. man.
Be safe. I'm gonna leave. yeah?

1669
01:36:07.501 --> 01:36:08.834
- Huh?
- I said I'm gonna cut.

1670
01:36:08.835 --> 01:36:11.587
- Oh. wait. no. no. no. You just got here!
- I just... I'm not feeling it.

1671
01:36:11.588 --> 01:36:14.383
What do you mean?
We just got here. bruv. Josh!

1672
01:36:16.176 --> 01:36:17.886
<i>♪ Just keep watching ♪</i>

1673
01:36:18.929 --> 01:36:21.306
[car engine whirring]

1674
01:36:37.489 --> 01:36:40.284
- [tires screech]
- [thuds]

1675
01:36:42.369 --> 01:36:43.578
[screaming]

1676
01:36:43.579 --> 01:36:46.832
[gasps. panting]

1677
01:36:48.876 --> 01:36:49.877
[sighs]

1678
01:37:11.982 --> 01:37:13.191
Hey.

1679
01:37:15.319 --> 01:37:17.237
- [chuckles]
- [groans]

1680
01:37:17.738 --> 01:37:19.239
I shouldn't drink tequila.

1681
01:37:23.785 --> 01:37:25.203
Last night was Ruben's idea?

1682
01:37:25.204 --> 01:37:26.955
[stammers] Yeah. the first part.

1683
01:37:27.539 --> 01:37:30.626
- Well... [stammers. chuckles]
- Not the second! [chuckles]

1684
01:37:41.053 --> 01:37:42.095
Come on.

1685
01:37:43.263 --> 01:37:45.265
Why are you here. Sonny. huh?

1686
01:37:48.518 --> 01:37:50.437
Not much of a story.

1687
01:37:56.151 --> 01:37:57.236
Okay.

1688
01:37:59.071 --> 01:38:00.989
I'm here to prove everyone wrong.

1689
01:38:02.908 --> 01:38:05.577
My ex. my old boss.

1690
01:38:07.287 --> 01:38:09.288
my first-year uni physics professor--

1691
01:38:09.289 --> 01:38:10.915
- That bastard.
- Yeah.

1692
01:38:10.916 --> 01:38:12.000
[chuckles]

1693
01:38:13.210 --> 01:38:15.504
And until we win. I haven't.

1694
01:38:16.713 --> 01:38:20.967
So. unfortunately. I now rely on you.

1695
01:38:20.968 --> 01:38:22.094
Mmm.

1696
01:38:27.849 --> 01:38:29.476
I was gonna be world champion.

1697
01:38:31.103 --> 01:38:32.604
The best there ever was.

1698
01:38:34.064 --> 01:38:36.482
I'm just a kid and I'm on the track
with my idols.

1699
01:38:36.483 --> 01:38:38.776
Senna. Mansell. Prost.

1700
01:38:38.777 --> 01:38:40.445
And I am quick.

1701
01:38:41.864 --> 01:38:43.323
I'm fearless.

1702
01:38:45.158 --> 01:38:46.451
I was next.

1703
01:38:49.454 --> 01:38:50.455
And then...

1704
01:38:51.957 --> 01:38:52.958
[clicks fingers]

1705
01:38:53.876 --> 01:38:55.419
...it was all taken away.

1706
01:38:57.754 --> 01:38:59.131
The crash. huh?

1707
01:39:00.716 --> 01:39:04.511
So I lost my seat. my money.
my sanity. my...

1708
01:39:05.470 --> 01:39:06.763
myself. really.

1709
01:39:07.723 --> 01:39:12.810
Just became this angry.
resentful shithead.

1710
01:39:12.811 --> 01:39:16.565
[chuckles]
Not someone I'm particularly proud of.

1711
01:39:20.944 --> 01:39:23.237
Till one day.
I realized what I had really lost.

1712
01:39:23.238 --> 01:39:28.367
and it wasn't the titles.
or the trophies. or the records.

1713
01:39:28.368 --> 01:39:31.788
It was my love for racing.

1714
01:39:34.416 --> 01:39:36.126
So I started driving.

1715
01:39:37.127 --> 01:39:40.671
Didn't matter the car. the circuit.
didn't need anyone to watch.

1716
01:39:40.672 --> 01:39:44.635
Just as long as I was behind the wheel.
I was good.

1717
01:39:47.804 --> 01:39:49.264
Sometimes...

1718
01:39:55.729 --> 01:39:57.231
[sighs]

1719
01:39:58.565 --> 01:40:01.443
What? Come on.

1720
01:40:04.821 --> 01:40:10.284
It's rare. but sometimes.
there's this moment in the car

1721
01:40:10.285 --> 01:40:12.996
where everything goes quiet.

1722
01:40:13.872 --> 01:40:15.499
my heartbeat slows.

1723
01:40:16.917 --> 01:40:18.377
it's peaceful.

1724
01:40:19.044 --> 01:40:22.089
and I can see everything. and no one...

1725
01:40:22.631 --> 01:40:24.258
no one can touch me.

1726
01:40:27.302 --> 01:40:30.264
And I am chasing that moment
every time I get in the car.

1727
01:40:33.350 --> 01:40:37.980
I don't know when I'll find it again.
but. man. I want to.

1728
01:40:38.772 --> 01:40:40.232
[chuckles] I want to.

1729
01:40:41.733 --> 01:40:44.945
'Cause in that moment. I'm flying.

1730
01:40:56.456 --> 01:40:59.710
[doorbell rings]

1731
01:41:07.050 --> 01:41:08.051
Kate.

1732
01:41:08.594 --> 01:41:10.428
- Ruben.
- Where is he?

1733
01:41:10.429 --> 01:41:11.638
Where's who?

1734
01:41:12.472 --> 01:41:13.974
What are you talking about?

1735
01:41:15.726 --> 01:41:17.144
Ruben. seriously?

1736
01:41:18.103 --> 01:41:20.605
[scoffs] One. how dare you?

1737
01:41:20.606 --> 01:41:23.358
Two. I respect professional boundaries.

1738
01:41:24.151 --> 01:41:25.152
And three...

1739
01:41:27.529 --> 01:41:29.113
Three. yeah. he's on... he's on the balcony.

1740
01:41:29.114 --> 01:41:30.199
[grunts]

1741
01:41:32.367 --> 01:41:34.076
- Well. you're up early.
- [Ruben] Get dressed.

1742
01:41:34.077 --> 01:41:36.413
- Yeah. what's going on?
- They're coming for our car.

1743
01:41:40.000 --> 01:41:43.044
[race director] It's my duty to inform you
that we've received an anonymous tip

1744
01:41:43.045 --> 01:41:45.296
that your upgraded floor is in violation.

1745
01:41:45.297 --> 01:41:46.589
[Ruben] From who?

1746
01:41:46.590 --> 01:41:48.341
- I can't say.
- Ah. [chuckles]

1747
01:41:48.342 --> 01:41:51.177
Sir. we submitted the drawings long ago.

1748
01:41:51.178 --> 01:41:52.261
- Right?
- Mm-hmm.

1749
01:41:52.262 --> 01:41:53.512
And you approved them all.

1750
01:41:53.513 --> 01:41:58.142
It's whether the parts you're racing with
were developed outside of your facility.

1751
01:41:58.143 --> 01:41:59.560
What? That's insane.

1752
01:41:59.561 --> 01:42:02.313
Based on the paperwork we've received.
there are concerns.

1753
01:42:02.314 --> 01:42:04.857
Hang on. where'd you get these?
These are internal documents.

1754
01:42:04.858 --> 01:42:07.443
[Ruben] This team
doesn't break any rules. sir. No. no.

1755
01:42:07.444 --> 01:42:10.488
- I'll take that with a pinch of salt.
- Someone can fabricate documents.

1756
01:42:10.489 --> 01:42:11.864
Your car's under review.

1757
01:42:11.865 --> 01:42:13.032
- You know the procedure.
- What?

1758
01:42:13.033 --> 01:42:17.495
You cannot race unless you substitute
the previously approved components.

1759
01:42:17.496 --> 01:42:19.705
- No!
- Do you mean our old design?

1760
01:42:19.706 --> 01:42:20.915
A shit box!

1761
01:42:20.916 --> 01:42:22.208
[in Spanish] <i>No lo puedo creer.</i>

1762
01:42:22.209 --> 01:42:24.293
[in English] Where were you
the last two years? Why now?

1763
01:42:24.294 --> 01:42:26.754
Because we might actually win a race?
Is that it?

1764
01:42:26.755 --> 01:42:29.799
This is not car racing. sir.
this is like corporate espionage!

1765
01:42:29.800 --> 01:42:31.926
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. Come... Come here.

1766
01:42:31.927 --> 01:42:33.844
I'm talking to you! Sir!

1767
01:42:33.845 --> 01:42:35.764
Without the upgrade. we're screwed.

1768
01:43:02.374 --> 01:43:05.793
[Kaspar] <i>Sonny. let it go.
Focus on a clean start.</i>

1769
01:43:05.794 --> 01:43:07.671
We'll never win clean.

1770
01:43:08.255 --> 01:43:09.755
Can we just not break any rules?

1771
01:43:09.756 --> 01:43:12.426
Yeah. the rules are always
against us though. aren't they?

1772
01:43:15.929 --> 01:43:18.222
Get them safe through lap one. [sighs]

1773
01:43:18.223 --> 01:43:21.225
[Hugh] <i>Sonny. we just need
to keep it in one piece. Okay?</i>

1774
01:43:21.226 --> 01:43:24.061
[Sonny breathing shakily]

1775
01:43:24.062 --> 01:43:26.606
[tense music playing]

1776
01:43:26.607 --> 01:43:27.941
<i>Sonny?</i>

1777
01:43:46.627 --> 01:43:47.920
[tires squeal]

1778
01:43:52.424 --> 01:43:55.134
- Oi. what the hell?
- I don't know!

1779
01:43:55.135 --> 01:43:56.260
[Joshua] <i>What's wrong with Sonny?</i>

1780
01:43:56.261 --> 01:43:58.638
Joshua. yep. Keep focused.
You're still good.

1781
01:43:58.639 --> 01:43:59.765
What's he doing?

1782
01:44:06.271 --> 01:44:07.648
He's driving angry.

1783
01:44:08.315 --> 01:44:09.650
Not good. It's not good.

1784
01:44:16.823 --> 01:44:18.658
Sonny. we need to make these tires last.

1785
01:44:18.659 --> 01:44:20.160
<i>Take it easy.</i>

1786
01:44:27.042 --> 01:44:29.293
No. he's put the car in qualifying mode.

1787
01:44:29.294 --> 01:44:31.587
He's gonna run the battery down.
Tell him to put it back.

1788
01:44:31.588 --> 01:44:33.507
[Hugh] <i>Sonny. you're in qualifying mode.
What's going on?</i>

1789
01:44:34.841 --> 01:44:35.842
Sonny. what's happening?

1790
01:44:45.936 --> 01:44:50.356
[Croft] <i>...blasting along
Las Vegas Boulevard. 210 miles an hour.</i>

1791
01:44:50.357 --> 01:44:52.900
<i>Hard on the brakes now.
and into the chicane.</i>

1792
01:44:52.901 --> 01:44:57.488
<i>Sergio Perez. ahead of Sonny Hayes.
but that's a mega exit from Hayes.</i>

1793
01:44:57.489 --> 01:45:00.700
<i>He's gotta gain on Sergio Perez.
and he's closing.</i>

1794
01:45:00.701 --> 01:45:03.494
<i>Meter by meter. Inch by inch.</i>

1795
01:45:03.495 --> 01:45:08.292
<i>Is this the place to take a gamble?
Hayes attacks round the outside.</i>

1796
01:45:13.964 --> 01:45:15.966
[crowd gasping. clamoring]

1797
01:45:16.466 --> 01:45:17.509
No! No!

1798
01:45:27.686 --> 01:45:30.147
[somber orchestral music playing]

1799
01:45:42.910 --> 01:45:45.370
Why do we do this?

1800
01:45:45.996 --> 01:45:48.789
What's wrong with tennis. huh?

1801
01:45:48.790 --> 01:45:50.458
- Or golf.
- [chuckles]

1802
01:45:50.459 --> 01:45:52.211
[chuckles] Right?

1803
01:45:53.170 --> 01:45:54.713
[exhales heavily]

1804
01:45:55.547 --> 01:45:56.548
Christ.

1805
01:45:58.508 --> 01:46:00.010
We are totally insane.

1806
01:46:02.054 --> 01:46:03.055
[sighs]

1807
01:46:05.015 --> 01:46:07.226
"C5 neck fracture.

1808
01:46:08.560 --> 01:46:10.020
Spinal contusion.

1809
01:46:10.562 --> 01:46:12.564
Compressed thoracic vertebrae.

1810
01:46:13.148 --> 01:46:17.401
Further blunt force impact trauma
likely to result in vision loss.

1811
01:46:17.402 --> 01:46:19.279
paralysis. death."

1812
01:46:22.533 --> 01:46:24.326
Really lead with the good news.
don't they?

1813
01:46:24.993 --> 01:46:26.787
This is a report from 30 years ago.

1814
01:46:28.497 --> 01:46:29.873
Why didn't you tell me?

1815
01:46:32.709 --> 01:46:35.170
You never should have raced again. Sonny.

1816
01:46:36.338 --> 01:46:38.882
How... How do you think I'd feel
if you die on the track?

1817
01:46:41.009 --> 01:46:42.134
Revenge for Monaco.

1818
01:46:42.135 --> 01:46:43.762
[stammers] It's not a joke!

1819
01:46:46.974 --> 01:46:48.934
It's me who's liable. Sonny.

1820
01:46:49.726 --> 01:46:52.603
And don't think there's some
bullshit loophole to get you out of this.

1821
01:46:52.604 --> 01:46:54.146
- No.
- Ruben. we're drivers.

1822
01:46:54.147 --> 01:46:56.942
We are not drivers. not anymore.
I'm sorry. We're not.

1823
01:46:58.944 --> 01:47:00.237
We're losers.

1824
01:47:01.947 --> 01:47:03.323
We're a pair of dumb.

1825
01:47:03.949 --> 01:47:05.325
sentimental.

1826
01:47:06.785 --> 01:47:07.995
broke losers.

1827
01:47:11.874 --> 01:47:12.958
[sighs]

1828
01:47:13.750 --> 01:47:15.168
Okay. You're off the team.

1829
01:47:20.090 --> 01:47:23.844
[sighs] Your van is in the garage
with all your stuff in it. and...

1830
01:47:28.390 --> 01:47:29.516
[chuckles]

1831
01:47:30.392 --> 01:47:32.895
I never should have pulled you
into this. Sonny.

1832
01:47:34.187 --> 01:47:35.397
I'm sorry.

1833
01:47:37.983 --> 01:47:39.151
Ruben. wait!

1834
01:47:40.652 --> 01:47:41.820
[sighs]

1835
01:47:44.865 --> 01:47:45.991
I need this.

1836
01:47:47.201 --> 01:47:48.202
[sighs]

1837
01:47:48.952 --> 01:47:53.332
No one drives forever. Sonny.
Not even you.

1838
01:48:07.888 --> 01:48:13.810
Pippa. load up Monza.
Just like it happened. In the rain.

1839
01:48:15.020 --> 01:48:17.355
[crew member] <i>Joshua.
Sonny says wait for the straight.</i>

1840
01:48:17.356 --> 01:48:19.399
<i>the straight into turn one.</i>

1841
01:48:27.241 --> 01:48:28.492
Run it again. please.

1842
01:48:32.996 --> 01:48:35.958
[crew member] <i>...wait for the straight.
the straight into turn one.</i>

1843
01:48:38.585 --> 01:48:40.420
Run it again. please.

1844
01:48:50.138 --> 01:48:52.140
[crew member] <i>The straight into turn one.</i>

1845
01:48:58.605 --> 01:49:02.568
[exclaims] Whoo! [chuckles]

1846
01:49:19.585 --> 01:49:20.878
[Peter] Sonny.

1847
01:49:22.129 --> 01:49:23.171
Sonny.

1848
01:49:24.423 --> 01:49:26.340
Hey. You're not in Abu Dhabi?

1849
01:49:26.341 --> 01:49:28.885
I fly out tonight. I. uh...

1850
01:49:28.886 --> 01:49:30.262
Yeah. I wanted to catch you.

1851
01:49:31.805 --> 01:49:33.097
So. listen. [sighs]

1852
01:49:33.098 --> 01:49:37.060
We both know that the board's
wanted to unload Apex from the start.

1853
01:49:37.728 --> 01:49:40.730
but. yeah. then you rode into town.

1854
01:49:40.731 --> 01:49:43.399
raised our whole profile.
and now I've. uh...

1855
01:49:43.400 --> 01:49:45.944
Yeah. I've got... I've got buyers lining up.

1856
01:49:47.863 --> 01:49:49.697
- Uh-huh.
- Gotta be honest with you. man.

1857
01:49:49.698 --> 01:49:52.701
I thought you were gonna be the...
the final nail in the coffin.

1858
01:49:53.285 --> 01:49:54.869
But now I see the play.

1859
01:49:54.870 --> 01:49:58.582
And I want you as part of the package.

1860
01:50:01.919 --> 01:50:03.462
What sort of package?

1861
01:50:04.129 --> 01:50:06.881
I've set up a sale where I run the team.

1862
01:50:06.882 --> 01:50:08.550
and keep you on for strategy.

1863
01:50:09.343 --> 01:50:10.677
maybe even team principal.

1864
01:50:12.012 --> 01:50:15.849
With the money from that deal.
I can make you a very rich man.

1865
01:50:16.892 --> 01:50:18.267
Here's the thing.

1866
01:50:18.268 --> 01:50:20.478
With the... the changing regulations.

1867
01:50:20.479 --> 01:50:23.899
new Mercedes power unit.
Kate's aero. two new drivers...

1868
01:50:25.275 --> 01:50:27.361
we've got a real shot
at the championship next year.

1869
01:50:28.654 --> 01:50:29.862
What about Ruben?

1870
01:50:29.863 --> 01:50:30.948
Don't worry.

1871
01:50:31.698 --> 01:50:32.990
You know.

1872
01:50:32.991 --> 01:50:34.201
We won't embarrass him.

1873
01:50:34.868 --> 01:50:37.746
We'll keep him on with a... with a title.
or brand ambassador...

1874
01:50:38.372 --> 01:50:39.456
You know. something.

1875
01:50:43.544 --> 01:50:44.794
And I get final say?

1876
01:50:44.795 --> 01:50:46.087
Don't change a thing.

1877
01:50:46.088 --> 01:50:47.339
Do what you do. man.

1878
01:50:48.382 --> 01:50:49.840
And that's the irony here.

1879
01:50:49.841 --> 01:50:52.760
You know. the board
originally approved your hire

1880
01:50:52.761 --> 01:50:54.388
because we thought you'd help us lose.

1881
01:50:55.264 --> 01:50:56.598
- Sorry to make you sweat.
- Hey.

1882
01:50:58.308 --> 01:50:59.433
That's my number.

1883
01:50:59.434 --> 01:51:00.769
Talk to your people.

1884
01:51:01.311 --> 01:51:07.234
But. uh... [chuckles] ...right after the race.
I. uh... I wanna lock down the deal. okay?

1885
01:51:07.734 --> 01:51:09.695
- So. by Sunday?
- Perfect.

1886
01:51:10.863 --> 01:51:13.740
Listen. this thing can be your legacy.
you know?

1887
01:51:15.868 --> 01:51:17.077
An F1 champion.

1888
01:51:18.328 --> 01:51:19.746
What you always wanted. right?

1889
01:51:23.292 --> 01:51:26.794
It was you who forged those documents.
wasn't it?

1890
01:51:26.795 --> 01:51:27.880
Huh.

1891
01:51:30.549 --> 01:51:32.384
[chuckles]

1892
01:51:33.218 --> 01:51:36.054
- You're a killer. man. aren't you?
- Hey. I'm a winner.

1893
01:51:37.681 --> 01:51:40.183
- Aren't you. huh?
- [sighs]

1894
01:51:42.311 --> 01:51:43.312
Okay.

1895
01:51:46.315 --> 01:51:48.650
Oh. hey. How's the back?

1896
01:51:49.651 --> 01:51:50.776
Better.

1897
01:51:50.777 --> 01:51:53.447
I've got an amazing guy.
I'll. uh... I'll hook you up.

1898
01:51:54.740 --> 01:51:55.741
Hail Mary.

1899
01:52:23.352 --> 01:52:24.478
You good?

1900
01:52:29.191 --> 01:52:33.070
[sighs] Listen. Mum.
I've gotta tell you something.

1901
01:52:36.949 --> 01:52:41.995
In Monza. right before the crash.
it was my decision to make the move.

1902
01:52:43.413 --> 01:52:45.165
Sonny actually told me to wait.

1903
01:52:47.167 --> 01:52:50.295
[breathes deeply]

1904
01:52:52.881 --> 01:52:53.965
[knocks on door]

1905
01:52:53.966 --> 01:52:55.174
Family.

1906
01:52:55.175 --> 01:52:57.677
I've been working the phones with IndyCar.

1907
01:52:57.678 --> 01:52:59.554
and I think I can get you
a test drive. bruv.

1908
01:52:59.555 --> 01:53:00.847
- Hello. Auntie. [kisses]
- Hi.

1909
01:53:02.099 --> 01:53:04.559
They're trying to pull in
a new demographic. obviously.

1910
01:53:04.560 --> 01:53:07.354
And the ladies love that smile.

1911
01:53:07.938 --> 01:53:10.648
And we can throw in some incentives.
like flights and cars.

1912
01:53:10.649 --> 01:53:12.776
Listen. Cash. you can go.
I don't need you today.

1913
01:53:13.860 --> 01:53:15.361
Nah. mate. You got media next.

1914
01:53:15.362 --> 01:53:18.031
[chuckles] I don't care. They can fine me.

1915
01:53:18.824 --> 01:53:19.825
Besides.

1916
01:53:21.326 --> 01:53:22.953
that's not why I'm doing it. right?

1917
01:53:23.871 --> 01:53:25.956
Josh. starting tomorrow.
we're not "doing it" anywhere.

1918
01:53:27.666 --> 01:53:29.126
It's all just noise.

1919
01:53:30.043 --> 01:53:32.212
Media. engagement. followers.

1920
01:53:32.921 --> 01:53:36.091
Listen. I've gotta focus on the race.

1921
01:53:37.926 --> 01:53:39.595
[Cash] Auntie. please.

1922
01:53:41.221 --> 01:53:42.556
Well. you heard the man.

1923
01:53:51.607 --> 01:53:54.151
- Deal.
- Deal. [chuckles]

1924
01:53:57.112 --> 01:53:59.155
- Yo.
- Hey.

1925
01:53:59.156 --> 01:54:00.741
- Hi.
- Hey.

1926
01:54:03.702 --> 01:54:05.745
Guys. what's happening?

1927
01:54:05.746 --> 01:54:08.998
<i>Parc fermé</i>.
Waiting for FIA to cut the seals.

1928
01:54:08.999 --> 01:54:11.126
Oh. good. [sighs]

1929
01:54:11.710 --> 01:54:14.171
- We got time then.
- For what?

1930
01:54:15.130 --> 01:54:16.340
For...

1931
01:54:17.841 --> 01:54:19.425
[chuckles]

1932
01:54:19.426 --> 01:54:21.678
No. no. no.

1933
01:54:26.266 --> 01:54:29.560
Welcome to the Paddock Club.
for our most valued guests.

1934
01:54:29.561 --> 01:54:33.564
Please. uh. grab a drink.
make yourselves at home.

1935
01:54:33.565 --> 01:54:37.945
and. uh. enjoy the very best view
there is of. uh... of Formula 1.

1936
01:54:39.988 --> 01:54:41.490
Okay? Okay.

1937
01:54:45.202 --> 01:54:46.370
[clears throat]

1938
01:54:59.258 --> 01:55:01.426
Hey. guys. don't stop! Keep going!

1939
01:55:04.346 --> 01:55:07.516
[chuckles]

1940
01:55:11.478 --> 01:55:14.314
[sighing]

1941
01:55:15.732 --> 01:55:16.817
[groans]

1942
01:55:31.748 --> 01:55:34.126
[stirring orchestral music playing]

1943
01:55:37.129 --> 01:55:40.048
No way. [chuckles]

1944
01:55:43.886 --> 01:55:45.053
[sighs]

1945
01:55:47.514 --> 01:55:50.434
<i>Jesús</i>. it's like a morgue around here.

1946
01:55:52.769 --> 01:55:54.270
[stammers] How'd you get here?

1947
01:55:54.271 --> 01:55:55.731
Premium economy.

1948
01:55:56.565 --> 01:55:58.150
[Ruben scoffs]

1949
01:55:59.985 --> 01:56:01.861
What? What is this?

1950
01:56:01.862 --> 01:56:03.529
Well. that's my bullshit loophole.

1951
01:56:03.530 --> 01:56:05.740
Oh. no. forget it.
I'm not even going to read that.

1952
01:56:05.741 --> 01:56:08.367
That is a real legal document
from a real Tijuana lawyer...

1953
01:56:08.368 --> 01:56:10.203
- [chuckles]
- ...waiving all liability to you

1954
01:56:10.204 --> 01:56:12.831
and your company vis-à-vis this race.
myself. and me.

1955
01:56:13.916 --> 01:56:15.167
- And...
- [inhales sharply]

1956
01:56:17.753 --> 01:56:21.173
...since you owe me my last paycheck.
technically I'm still on this team.

1957
01:56:26.428 --> 01:56:27.930
Kate. where's the shitbox?

1958
01:56:28.597 --> 01:56:31.015
The FIA confirmed that
the documents were forged.

1959
01:56:31.016 --> 01:56:33.143
and they were sent by someone from Apex.

1960
01:56:33.977 --> 01:56:35.062
Huh.

1961
01:56:35.687 --> 01:56:38.648
Okay. I don't care about your loophole.
I don't.

1962
01:56:38.649 --> 01:56:40.775
That is my car. You are not racing it.

1963
01:56:40.776 --> 01:56:41.984
- Ruben.
- No. Sonny.

1964
01:56:41.985 --> 01:56:43.362
Listen.

1965
01:56:44.613 --> 01:56:46.405
I can't let you do that.

1966
01:56:46.406 --> 01:56:47.490
I can't.

1967
01:56:47.491 --> 01:56:48.699
Okay?

1968
01:56:48.700 --> 01:56:49.785
[stammers]

1969
01:56:50.452 --> 01:56:54.081
If the last thing I do is drive that car.
I will take that life. man.

1970
01:56:57.960 --> 01:56:59.378
A thousand times.

1971
01:57:01.338 --> 01:57:03.048
[sighs]

1972
01:57:04.132 --> 01:57:05.384
We can't win.

1973
01:57:07.219 --> 01:57:08.637
We can't if we don't try.

1974
01:57:15.060 --> 01:57:16.061
[sighs]

1975
01:57:19.648 --> 01:57:20.857
[sighs]

1976
01:57:28.365 --> 01:57:30.158
[laughing]

1977
01:57:31.827 --> 01:57:33.537
[laughs]

1978
01:57:44.464 --> 01:57:46.758
[groaning]

1979
01:57:47.968 --> 01:57:48.969
[knocks on door]

1980
01:57:54.933 --> 01:57:56.434
How come you never look at the card?

1981
01:57:56.435 --> 01:57:57.685
[Sonny] What card?

1982
01:57:57.686 --> 01:57:58.770
[chuckles]

1983
01:57:59.980 --> 01:58:02.441
[crowd cheering]

1984
01:58:38.894 --> 01:58:41.312
Welcome to the very final spots
on the grid.

1985
01:58:41.313 --> 01:58:45.775
And as ever. we'll go from last to first.
And breaking news here in P22.

1986
01:58:45.776 --> 01:58:47.443
<i>because we're hearing
the Apex GP team have made...</i>

1987
01:58:47.444 --> 01:58:49.238
- Hey. Peter.
- Yeah?

1988
01:58:49.821 --> 01:58:51.072
That's your guy. Isn't it?

1989
01:58:51.073 --> 01:58:55.159
<i>...being replaced by Sonny Hayes. who
didn't even make the trip to Abu Dhabi...</i>

1990
01:58:55.160 --> 01:58:57.787
Uh. will you excuse me for one second?
I'm really sorry.

1991
01:58:57.788 --> 01:59:00.666
<i>Now. the rules require that
he has to start at the back of the pack.</i>

1992
01:59:01.333 --> 01:59:03.627
Excuse me. What the hell?

1993
01:59:04.378 --> 01:59:05.587
What?

1994
01:59:09.758 --> 01:59:10.842
You still got my phone?

1995
01:59:14.680 --> 01:59:15.681
[phone buzzes]

1996
01:59:29.820 --> 01:59:31.362
- Good luck today.
- You too. James.

1997
01:59:31.363 --> 01:59:32.572
Excuse me. Hey. Sonny. Sonny!

1998
01:59:32.573 --> 01:59:34.198
Hey. look.
I know we've had our differences.

1999
01:59:34.199 --> 01:59:36.492
- but look. this is your last F1 race.
- Chaz! This guy.

2000
01:59:36.493 --> 01:59:37.870
Any thought...

2001
01:59:40.038 --> 01:59:41.039
What's that?

2002
01:59:42.332 --> 01:59:44.126
[crowd cheering]

2003
01:59:45.168 --> 01:59:46.461
Bloody hell.

2004
01:59:48.380 --> 01:59:49.631
Bloody hell!

2005
01:59:50.132 --> 01:59:51.674
[laughs]

2006
01:59:51.675 --> 01:59:54.177
[UAE national anthem playing]

2007
02:00:10.319 --> 02:00:11.320
Elbows out?

2008
02:00:11.987 --> 02:00:12.988
Elbows out.

2009
02:00:14.781 --> 02:00:20.328
[Croft] <i>All set for our season finale
here in Abu Dhabi where it's lights out.</i>

2010
02:00:20.329 --> 02:00:23.956
<i>And away we go.
Good start there for Joshua Pearce.</i>

2011
02:00:23.957 --> 02:00:26.209
<i>Drivers jockeying for position</i>

2012
02:00:26.210 --> 02:00:30.922
<i>as we head full-throttle
down the main straight and into turn one.</i>

2013
02:00:30.923 --> 02:00:35.843
<i>Tricky first corner. and going wide.
the Aston Martin and the AlphaTauri</i>

2014
02:00:35.844 --> 02:00:38.095
- [laughs]
<i>- as Pearce picks up two places.</i>

2015
02:00:38.096 --> 02:00:40.556
[Brundle] <i>Yes. Pearce showing
some real maturity there.</i>

2016
02:00:40.557 --> 02:00:44.728
<i>He saw a bad situation before it happened
and he's off to a great start.</i>

2017
02:01:03.288 --> 02:01:04.665
Don't even think about it.

2018
02:01:20.639 --> 02:01:23.559
[Croft] <i>Here comes the Alpine
down the inside. Contact!</i>

2019
02:01:24.810 --> 02:01:27.938
<i>And three days out of hospital.
Hayes will feel that.</i>

2020
02:01:37.781 --> 02:01:39.824
Gained places. guys. We're alive.

2021
02:01:39.825 --> 02:01:41.492
[Brundle]
<i>I hope he hasn't damaged the car.</i>

2022
02:01:41.493 --> 02:01:44.453
<i>but despite everything.
it's still a great first lap.</i>

2023
02:01:44.454 --> 02:01:46.539
[Croft] <i>It is! Hayes in P16.</i>

2024
02:01:46.540 --> 02:01:49.167
<i>Pearce. his teammate. up to P9.</i>

2025
02:01:51.128 --> 02:01:54.463
<i>Red Bull. Mercedes and Ferrari
holding on to the lead.</i>

2026
02:01:54.464 --> 02:01:56.257
<i>Apex in the midfield.</i>

2027
02:01:56.258 --> 02:01:59.260
<i>Let's see if they can do anything
to shake up this race.</i>

2028
02:01:59.261 --> 02:02:00.428
Gap to leader?

2029
02:02:00.429 --> 02:02:01.555
[Hugh] <i>Fifteen seconds.</i>

2030
02:02:02.764 --> 02:02:05.309
Keep JP plus 20 seconds. Plus 20.

2031
02:02:05.893 --> 02:02:07.728
- Length of a pit stop.
- You know why.

2032
02:02:09.229 --> 02:02:11.105
[Croft] <i>It's a busy race for Sonny Hayes.</i>

2033
02:02:11.106 --> 02:02:14.275
<i>and now here comes Kevin Magnussen
looking to make a move.</i>

2034
02:02:14.276 --> 02:02:16.068
<i>And this could spell trouble.</i>

2035
02:02:16.069 --> 02:02:17.778
[Brundle]
<i>There's history between these two.</i>

2036
02:02:17.779 --> 02:02:21.199
<i>Often. the irresistible force
meets the immovable object.</i>

2037
02:02:21.200 --> 02:02:23.201
<i>And Magnussen. looking down the inside.</i>

2038
02:02:23.202 --> 02:02:26.829
- <i>locks up and hits Hayes.</i>
- Box. box. Box. box. box.

2039
02:02:26.830 --> 02:02:28.290
Copy. coming in for hards.

2040
02:02:29.875 --> 02:02:31.126
Damn.

2041
02:02:32.628 --> 02:02:35.839
Slow is smooth. Smooth is fast.
Here we go. boys.

2042
02:02:43.138 --> 02:02:44.347
[Croft] <i>Hayes exit the pits.</i>

2043
02:02:44.348 --> 02:02:47.225
<i>He had to come in
because of that damage to his tire.</i>

2044
02:02:47.226 --> 02:02:51.355
<i>But what of Joshua Pearce?
Where do Apex GP go with him?</i>

2045
02:02:53.065 --> 02:02:54.982
[Joshua] Guys. am I boxing?
What's the plan?

2046
02:02:54.983 --> 02:02:57.485
<i>Plan C. Plan C. Stay out. Stay out.</i>

2047
02:02:57.486 --> 02:03:00.238
- [laughs] Chaos.
- Copy that.

2048
02:03:00.239 --> 02:03:03.825
Joshua slows down the leaders for Sonny.
Sonny does the same for him.

2049
02:03:05.244 --> 02:03:06.786
[Brundle] <i>Pearce stays out.</i>

2050
02:03:06.787 --> 02:03:09.872
<i>It's a strategy that Apex have used
before this season.</i>

2051
02:03:09.873 --> 02:03:13.961
<i>It helps them with track position for now.
but they gotta keep these tires alive.</i>

2052
02:03:17.506 --> 02:03:19.174
It's the only way we keep this close.

2053
02:03:19.758 --> 02:03:20.800
And then we need luck.

2054
02:03:20.801 --> 02:03:22.177
I'm way ahead of ya.

2055
02:03:23.762 --> 02:03:24.721
[Rico chuckles]

2056
02:03:25.472 --> 02:03:29.058
[Croft] <i>Lap 25. and every driver
so far has pitted. bar one.</i>

2057
02:03:29.059 --> 02:03:30.893
<i>And he leads the race.</i>

2058
02:03:30.894 --> 02:03:33.896
<i>Joshua Pearce controlling the pace
out in front.</i>

2059
02:03:33.897 --> 02:03:35.690
[Brundle] <i>And that gives
his teammate. Hayes.</i>

2060
02:03:35.691 --> 02:03:38.150
<i>a chance to maintain
his position in the midfield</i>

2061
02:03:38.151 --> 02:03:41.445
<i>despite the contact.
puncture and pit stop.</i>

2062
02:03:41.446 --> 02:03:43.156
<i>They're working really well together.</i>

2063
02:03:44.950 --> 02:03:46.117
How's JP doing up there?

2064
02:03:46.118 --> 02:03:49.412
He's keeping the leaders at bay.
DRS active next straight. Sonny.

2065
02:03:49.413 --> 02:03:50.789
Got it.

2066
02:03:51.623 --> 02:03:55.167
[Croft] <i>Onto the back straight.
He's enjoying this new upgrade.</i>

2067
02:03:55.168 --> 02:03:58.421
<i>and he's got DRS.
and he's got Pierre Gasly.</i>

2068
02:03:58.422 --> 02:04:00.591
<i>Sonny Hayes up into P15.</i>

2069
02:04:01.717 --> 02:04:04.094
[Hugh] <i>Sonny. you have got the pace.
Keep pushing.</i>

2070
02:04:04.678 --> 02:04:06.637
[Brundle] <i>Pearce has been doing
a great job out front</i>

2071
02:04:06.638 --> 02:04:10.308
<i>despite the used tires.
but that moment is nearly over now.</i>

2072
02:04:10.309 --> 02:04:13.227
<i>Verstappen up the inside and he's through.</i>

2073
02:04:13.228 --> 02:04:15.813
[Croft] <i>Fabulous first stint
from Joshua Pearce.</i>

2074
02:04:15.814 --> 02:04:18.275
<i>Max has passed.
and his troubles don't end there.</i>

2075
02:04:19.610 --> 02:04:21.485
<i>Here comes Charles Leclerc.</i>

2076
02:04:21.486 --> 02:04:25.823
<i>It's another overtake.
Pearce lost the lead and drops now to P3.</i>

2077
02:04:25.824 --> 02:04:28.367
Sorry. guys. My rear tires are shot.

2078
02:04:28.368 --> 02:04:30.245
Copy that. Box. JP. Box. box.

2079
02:04:31.830 --> 02:04:33.998
[Brundle] <i>Pearce stretching those tires
to the limit.</i>

2080
02:04:33.999 --> 02:04:37.002
<i>Short-term pain for long-term gain.</i>

2081
02:04:45.219 --> 02:04:48.179
<i>And he exits the pit.
He'll have fresher tires.</i>

2082
02:04:48.180 --> 02:04:51.391
<i>He can now attack
in the second half of the race.</i>

2083
02:04:51.975 --> 02:04:53.809
Sonny. the three leaders
are still on hards.

2084
02:04:53.810 --> 02:04:55.811
They're gonna have to stop again.
This is their pit window.

2085
02:04:55.812 --> 02:04:58.899
One of the leaders is gonna undercut.
I need to be there when they do.

2086
02:05:00.317 --> 02:05:02.611
P3 Ferrari. Pippa. can he beat it to one?

2087
02:05:05.155 --> 02:05:06.239
[Pippa] Depends on their stop.

2088
02:05:06.240 --> 02:05:08.074
[Croft] <i>Will the undercut
work for Ferrari?</i>

2089
02:05:08.075 --> 02:05:10.452
Five point eight.
He needs to pick up half a second.

2090
02:05:12.663 --> 02:05:15.039
Sonny. you need half a second.
Go. go. go. go. go.

2091
02:05:15.040 --> 02:05:16.541
[Croft] <i>And Sonny Hayes is on the charge.</i>

2092
02:05:16.542 --> 02:05:19.043
<i>Under the track goes the Ferrari.</i>

2093
02:05:19.044 --> 02:05:21.045
<i>Through the first corner goes Sonny Hayes.</i>

2094
02:05:21.046 --> 02:05:23.798
<i>It's neck and neck. It's really tight.</i>

2095
02:05:23.799 --> 02:05:27.385
<i>Sonny Hayes is just ahead of Carlos Sainz.</i>

2096
02:05:27.386 --> 02:05:29.720
- Yes! Come on!
- [Croft] <i>It's worked so far for Apex GP.</i>

2097
02:05:29.721 --> 02:05:31.597
<i>But their trouble's not over.</i>

2098
02:05:31.598 --> 02:05:35.893
<i>Down the inside. there's a chance
for Carlos Sainz. and he takes it.</i>

2099
02:05:35.894 --> 02:05:37.186
<i>But he locks up.</i>

2100
02:05:37.187 --> 02:05:39.981
<i>The Ferrari goes wide
and Sonny Hayes says.</i>

2101
02:05:39.982 --> 02:05:42.734
<i>"Thank you very much indeed."</i>

2102
02:05:44.361 --> 02:05:46.445
How are they staying so close to the lead?

2103
02:05:46.446 --> 02:05:49.700
Uh. they're. um... They're working together.

2104
02:05:50.367 --> 02:05:53.871
[Brundle] <i>Two Apex cars in the top 10.
but still a long way to go.</i>

2105
02:05:55.539 --> 02:05:59.375
[Croft] <i>Twenty laps remaining. and Apex
has worked their way up the order.</i>

2106
02:05:59.376 --> 02:06:01.752
<i>We're now at the final pit stop window.</i>

2107
02:06:01.753 --> 02:06:04.422
This is our chance for P1.
Make sure JP beats them out.

2108
02:06:04.423 --> 02:06:09.177
[Croft] <i>Hamilton and Leclerc
come into the pits. but Pearce stays out.</i>

2109
02:06:10.220 --> 02:06:12.972
- [Joshua] Talk to me. Can I catch 'em?
- Yep. They're just coming out.

2110
02:06:12.973 --> 02:06:14.849
<i>Push now. Push now. Push. push.</i>

2111
02:06:14.850 --> 02:06:16.226
Copy. Pushing.

2112
02:06:16.810 --> 02:06:18.394
[Croft] <i>Oh. this is gonna be close.</i>

2113
02:06:18.395 --> 02:06:21.439
<i>Joshua Pearce inching ahead.
Staying ahead.</i>

2114
02:06:21.440 --> 02:06:24.317
<i>For the second time in this race.
he leads.</i>

2115
02:06:24.318 --> 02:06:25.401
[laughs] Let's go!

2116
02:06:25.402 --> 02:06:26.986
- [grunts]
- [grunts] Yes.

2117
02:06:26.987 --> 02:06:30.072
<i>You are P1. Joshua.</i> [laughs]

2118
02:06:30.073 --> 02:06:32.533
[Brundle] <i>But Pearce will have
a hard time holding them off</i>

2119
02:06:32.534 --> 02:06:35.537
<i>with Hamilton and Leclerc on fresh tires.</i>

2120
02:06:44.755 --> 02:06:47.131
[Croft] <i>Four laps to go.
Sonny Hayes is in P4.</i>

2121
02:06:47.132 --> 02:06:49.133
<i>He's five seconds behind his teammate.</i>

2122
02:06:49.134 --> 02:06:50.927
<i>but both are on old tires.</i>

2123
02:06:50.928 --> 02:06:53.639
<i>There's little chance
they'll gain any places now.</i>

2124
02:06:55.891 --> 02:06:59.852
<i>And here's Hamilton
attacking Pearce into turn five.</i>

2125
02:06:59.853 --> 02:07:01.187
<i>And he's through.</i>

2126
02:07:01.188 --> 02:07:05.108
Nobody has to stop again
and our tires are nine laps older.

2127
02:07:06.860 --> 02:07:09.403
[Brundle] <i>And Leclerc attacks and passes.</i>

2128
02:07:09.404 --> 02:07:13.909
<i>Pearce's tires are absolutely finished.
There was nothing he could do about that.</i>

2129
02:07:14.660 --> 02:07:17.745
I'm sorry. guys. I've got nothing left.

2130
02:07:17.746 --> 02:07:21.290
[Croft] <i>It's been the Apex GP story
all year long.</i>

2131
02:07:21.291 --> 02:07:22.375
<i>Plenty of risks.</i>

2132
02:07:22.376 --> 02:07:24.085
<i>A great underdog story.</i>

2133
02:07:24.086 --> 02:07:26.170
<i>but we know. Martin.
only talent crowns a champion.</i>

2134
02:07:26.171 --> 02:07:27.755
[Sonny] <i>Losing grip. Tires are gone.</i>

2135
02:07:27.756 --> 02:07:30.466
[Brundle] <i>Yeah. Sadly. the deck's
been stacked against them</i>

2136
02:07:30.467 --> 02:07:32.426
<i>and now they're out of cards to play.</i>

2137
02:07:32.427 --> 02:07:33.594
It ain't over. right?

2138
02:07:33.595 --> 02:07:36.974
No. but nothing can change.
It's the worst feeling in the world.

2139
02:07:41.603 --> 02:07:43.396
<i>George Russell on the attack.</i>

2140
02:07:43.397 --> 02:07:46.315
<i>Hayes looking to defend.
through the left-hander they go...</i>

2141
02:07:46.316 --> 02:07:47.817
<i>And there's contact!</i>

2142
02:07:47.818 --> 02:07:50.653
<i>Hayes is spun round and into the barrier.</i>

2143
02:07:50.654 --> 02:07:52.446
<i>That's a big one.</i>

2144
02:07:52.447 --> 02:07:53.532
[gasping]

2145
02:07:54.157 --> 02:07:56.493
- Fucking yes. yes. yes.
- Oh. no.

2146
02:07:57.703 --> 02:07:58.703
Yeah. no. Ooh.

2147
02:07:58.704 --> 02:08:00.454
[Brundle] <i>There's debris
all over the race track</i>

2148
02:08:00.455 --> 02:08:02.957
<i>and substantial damage to the barriers.</i>

2149
02:08:02.958 --> 02:08:06.210
<i>The stewards have no choice
but to red flag this race.</i>

2150
02:08:06.211 --> 02:08:07.295
Miracle.

2151
02:08:07.296 --> 02:08:09.130
[Croft] <i>And speaking of damage. Martin.</i>

2152
02:08:09.131 --> 02:08:11.757
<i>Hayes will only be allowed
to continue in this race</i>

2153
02:08:11.758 --> 02:08:15.052
<i>if he can get his car
all the way around the circuit</i>

2154
02:08:15.053 --> 02:08:16.513
<i>and back to the pit lane.</i>

2155
02:08:17.097 --> 02:08:19.348
[Hugh] <i>Sonny. Sonny. can you get it back?</i>

2156
02:08:19.349 --> 02:08:22.144
<i>I'll get it back. I'll get it back
if I have to push it back.</i>

2157
02:08:22.728 --> 02:08:27.148
Come on. Sonny. Nice and easy.

2158
02:08:27.149 --> 02:08:29.734
[grunting]

2159
02:08:29.735 --> 02:08:32.528
He's still going.
[chuckling] He's still going.

2160
02:08:32.529 --> 02:08:34.030
[crew member] JP. red flag.

2161
02:08:34.031 --> 02:08:35.323
<i>Red flag. Come in.</i>

2162
02:08:35.324 --> 02:08:39.744
We are still alive. <i>hermano</i>. [laughs]

2163
02:08:39.745 --> 02:08:41.454
Red flag!

2164
02:08:41.455 --> 02:08:45.166
[Brundle] <i>And somehow Sonny Hayes
has got his car back to the pit lane.</i>

2165
02:08:45.167 --> 02:08:47.418
- It's a miracle.
- I know! I know.

2166
02:08:47.419 --> 02:08:48.794
Never seen one until now.

2167
02:08:48.795 --> 02:08:52.299
Home free. Good girl. Let's go.

2168
02:08:53.008 --> 02:08:54.008
New softs. both cars.

2169
02:08:54.009 --> 02:08:56.552
Raise the tire pressure
for three quick laps.

2170
02:08:56.553 --> 02:08:58.721
- Team. time to build a car.
- [crew cheers. clamors]

2171
02:08:58.722 --> 02:09:00.181
[Croft] <i>Red flag rules then.</i>

2172
02:09:00.182 --> 02:09:03.559
The teams can make changes.
They can make repairs to their cars.

2173
02:09:03.560 --> 02:09:05.019
But only in that pit lane.

2174
02:09:05.020 --> 02:09:10.025
<i>And with only ten minutes to make repairs.
Apex GP has their work cut out.</i>

2175
02:09:10.525 --> 02:09:13.903
[Brundle] <i>And all cars
can fit a fresh set of tires</i>

2176
02:09:13.904 --> 02:09:15.947
<i>for what will be a three-lap sprint.</i>

2177
02:09:15.948 --> 02:09:18.951
- Dodge! Dodge. are we gonna make it?
- I don't know. I don't know.

2178
02:09:24.790 --> 02:09:27.375
That was clean.
That wasn't me. Not this time.

2179
02:09:27.376 --> 02:09:31.170
"Not this time"?
Tell that to the stewards.

2180
02:09:31.171 --> 02:09:32.506
Check the replay.

2181
02:09:33.549 --> 02:09:35.467
I got this. Lift that corner.

2182
02:09:43.850 --> 02:09:46.602
I'm good. I'm good. I'm good. I'm good.

2183
02:09:46.603 --> 02:09:48.229
[Brundle] <i>What the stewards
will be looking at</i>

2184
02:09:48.230 --> 02:09:50.147
<i>is whether Hayes went off completely</i>

2185
02:09:50.148 --> 02:09:54.193
<i>or kept at least one tire on track
during the contact with Russell.</i>

2186
02:09:54.194 --> 02:09:55.987
- Yo. you good?
- Yeah. good.

2187
02:09:55.988 --> 02:09:57.280
Listen. you were on track.

2188
02:09:57.281 --> 02:10:00.408
Yeah. it was your corner.
P3 and P4. Let's go!

2189
02:10:00.409 --> 02:10:04.453
[Croft] <i>Given Hayes's reputation. they'll
be looking at this really. really closely.</i>

2190
02:10:04.454 --> 02:10:06.205
<i>I'm not expecting a quick decision.</i>

2191
02:10:06.206 --> 02:10:07.790
Come on. that's clearly a penalty.

2192
02:10:07.791 --> 02:10:09.792
Like... I mean.
not that that's what we want.

2193
02:10:09.793 --> 02:10:13.504
but. like. objectively. that's the guy.

2194
02:10:13.505 --> 02:10:16.257
- Oh. man. It can't end this way.
- It's just a time-out.

2195
02:10:16.258 --> 02:10:20.344
Like the last 30 years.
It's in the hands of the racing gods now.

2196
02:10:20.345 --> 02:10:22.264
We gotta believe. Gotta believe.

2197
02:10:23.765 --> 02:10:25.850
[Croft] <i>Plenty going on here in the pit.</i>

2198
02:10:25.851 --> 02:10:29.103
<i>Oh. look. Here comes the new wing.
This is a massive job.</i>

2199
02:10:29.104 --> 02:10:33.150
<i>Yeah. but will the car hold together
for the remaining three laps?</i>

2200
02:10:36.361 --> 02:10:38.321
<i>Well. that barrier looks okay now.</i>

2201
02:10:38.322 --> 02:10:41.782
<i>The marshals just sweeping
the last few bits of debris off the track.</i>

2202
02:10:41.783 --> 02:10:43.951
<i>and the clock continues to tick down.</i>

2203
02:10:43.952 --> 02:10:47.956
[Brundle] <i>Yeah. it's just over two minutes
until this race gets underway again.</i>

2204
02:11:08.936 --> 02:11:10.395
JP. JP!

2205
02:11:11.688 --> 02:11:12.813
Three laps.

2206
02:11:12.814 --> 02:11:14.315
Three laps is a lifetime.

2207
02:11:14.316 --> 02:11:15.734
Go win this thing.

2208
02:11:27.663 --> 02:11:30.249
Hey. Sonny. Sonny. you got a minute?

2209
02:11:32.459 --> 02:11:33.502
We got you a car.

2210
02:11:34.169 --> 02:11:36.922
Ah. you rock. Thank you.

2211
02:11:39.508 --> 02:11:42.802
[Brundle] <i>Because Apex GP
didn't make the top 10 in qualifying.</i>

2212
02:11:42.803 --> 02:11:45.680
they have a new set
of soft tires available.

2213
02:11:45.681 --> 02:11:49.058
<i>which will give them extra speed
over the cars ahead of them</i>

2214
02:11:49.059 --> 02:11:51.394
<i>on the used soft tires.</i>

2215
02:11:51.395 --> 02:11:54.355
This red flag is a lifeline.

2216
02:11:54.356 --> 02:11:56.775
You'd almost wonder
if Sonny didn't engineer it.

2217
02:11:57.609 --> 02:12:00.403
But wait. we're the only cars
on fresh tires

2218
02:12:00.404 --> 02:12:02.238
because we sucked in qualifying yesterday?

2219
02:12:02.239 --> 02:12:03.990
Never got the chance to use them.

2220
02:12:03.991 --> 02:12:06.325
Sometimes when you lose. you win.

2221
02:12:06.326 --> 02:12:08.912
- That don't make no sense.
- It's a Sonny thing.

2222
02:12:09.788 --> 02:12:11.789
[Croft] <i>Light at the end of the pit lane
is green.</i>

2223
02:12:11.790 --> 02:12:15.042
<i>We're off on our second formation lap
of the evening.</i>

2224
02:12:15.043 --> 02:12:18.713
<i>and when this race resumes.
this is gonna be an epic sprint.</i>

2225
02:12:18.714 --> 02:12:21.800
<i>Hamilton. Leclerc. Pearce. Hayes.
That's the top four.</i>

2226
02:12:46.033 --> 02:12:47.992
[Hugh] <i>Sonny. we just heard
from the stewards.</i>

2227
02:12:47.993 --> 02:12:49.076
Goddamn it. Now?

2228
02:12:49.077 --> 02:12:50.786
[Hugh] <i>We're debating whether to tell you.</i>

2229
02:12:50.787 --> 02:12:53.039
Kaspar says. "Yes."
but Kate says. "Don't."

2230
02:12:53.040 --> 02:12:55.249
- <i>She says you're fast when you're angry.</i>
- [chuckles]

2231
02:12:55.250 --> 02:12:57.335
- Tell her. "Job well done."
- [laughs]

2232
02:12:57.336 --> 02:13:00.463
[Croft] <i>And here's news.
Stewards have made their decision.</i>

2233
02:13:00.464 --> 02:13:05.885
<i>That Lap 55 collision between Hayes
and Russell is ruled a racing incident.</i>

2234
02:13:05.886 --> 02:13:08.137
<i>- No further investigation.</i>
- [cheering]

2235
02:13:08.138 --> 02:13:10.265
Whoa! Sonny.

2236
02:13:13.143 --> 02:13:16.521
That was your line. Sonny.
Go finish your race.

2237
02:13:19.691 --> 02:13:22.401
Joshua. we still got two cars in the mix.

2238
02:13:22.402 --> 02:13:23.862
Then we've got a team.

2239
02:13:25.030 --> 02:13:26.531
[Brundle] <i>Once those red lights go out.</i>

2240
02:13:26.532 --> 02:13:29.535
<i>this will be an absolute sprint
to the finish.</i>

2241
02:13:30.410 --> 02:13:32.912
<i>Position advantage to Mercedes
and Ferrari.</i>

2242
02:13:32.913 --> 02:13:35.374
<i>Tire advantage to Apex GP.</i>

2243
02:14:01.900 --> 02:14:03.526
Tell JP to follow my lead.

2244
02:14:03.527 --> 02:14:05.403
[crew member]
<i>Joshua. Sonny says to follow him.</i>

2245
02:14:05.404 --> 02:14:07.072
Follow? He's behind me.

2246
02:14:09.324 --> 02:14:11.952
- Cheeky bastard.
- [Sonny] That's it. Stay with me.

2247
02:14:21.003 --> 02:14:22.503
[crew member] <i>He's giving you a tow.
Take it.</i>

2248
02:14:22.504 --> 02:14:23.714
All the way.

2249
02:14:51.200 --> 02:14:53.242
Come on. kid. Get it. Come on!

2250
02:14:53.243 --> 02:14:55.203
[Croft] <i>Hayes plays the decoy.</i>

2251
02:14:55.204 --> 02:14:59.665
<i>and Pearce rockets past Leclerc
and up into second.</i>

2252
02:14:59.666 --> 02:15:05.213
<i>And Leclerc's in danger from Sonny Hayes.
Round the outside. he's up into P3.</i>

2253
02:15:05.214 --> 02:15:06.672
[Brundle] <i>Perfect teamwork.</i>

2254
02:15:06.673 --> 02:15:10.469
<i>Hayes and Pearce working together.
it's like racing ballet.</i>

2255
02:15:11.053 --> 02:15:12.678
[Croft] <i>It's a beautiful sight.</i>

2256
02:15:12.679 --> 02:15:16.725
<i>but now their sights are set on
the race leader. Lewis Hamilton.</i>

2257
02:15:17.226 --> 02:15:18.685
Yeah! Remember me?

2258
02:15:28.278 --> 02:15:30.030
Come on. boys. Send it!

2259
02:15:57.224 --> 02:15:58.432
Why didn't they overtake?

2260
02:15:58.433 --> 02:16:00.101
Lewis will defend
whichever car attacks first.

2261
02:16:00.102 --> 02:16:03.522
- But they both can't wait.
- Someone has to sacrifice.

2262
02:16:08.819 --> 02:16:09.819
[Croft] <i>Two onto one.</i>

2263
02:16:09.820 --> 02:16:12.488
<i>and all the pressure is on Lewis Hamilton</i>

2264
02:16:12.489 --> 02:16:15.409
<i>as Apex work as a pack.</i>

2265
02:16:16.410 --> 02:16:17.451
Go win it. kid.

2266
02:16:17.452 --> 02:16:19.287
<i>Hayes makes the first move.</i>

2267
02:16:19.288 --> 02:16:22.290
- <i>Hamilton defends. Pearce attacks.</i>
- Yeah!

2268
02:16:22.291 --> 02:16:24.876
<i>- And Pearce has P1.
-</i> [crowd cheering]

2269
02:16:24.877 --> 02:16:26.253
- Yes!
- Yes. yes!

2270
02:16:28.130 --> 02:16:30.256
[Croft] <i>Toe-to-toe. wheel-to-wheel.</i>

2271
02:16:30.257 --> 02:16:33.926
<i>this is epic racing
to finish off the season.</i>

2272
02:16:33.927 --> 02:16:36.679
<i>And Sonny Hayes and Lewis Hamilton
aren't done yet.</i>

2273
02:16:36.680 --> 02:16:38.723
<i>Hamilton. on Sonny Hayes.</i>

2274
02:16:38.724 --> 02:16:40.182
<i>- There's contact!</i>
- [crowd clamors]

2275
02:16:40.183 --> 02:16:42.144
<i>And through goes Hamilton.</i>

2276
02:16:45.022 --> 02:16:47.273
- Yes. yes!
- Come on!

2277
02:16:47.274 --> 02:16:48.191
Yes!

2278
02:16:49.025 --> 02:16:51.485
Guys. talk to me.
Where's Sonny? Can he finish?

2279
02:16:51.486 --> 02:16:54.071
[crew member] <i>One more lap. JP.
Hamilton never backs down.</i>

2280
02:16:54.072 --> 02:16:56.032
Can Sonny finish the race. man?

2281
02:16:56.033 --> 02:16:58.408
[crew member] <i>Yes. he's on track.
Just watch Lewis when he fights.</i>

2282
02:16:58.409 --> 02:17:01.203
<i>You're P1. No more risks.</i>

2283
02:17:01.204 --> 02:17:02.372
No such thing.

2284
02:17:03.665 --> 02:17:07.376
[Croft] <i>The rookie holds his line.
He won't back down.</i>

2285
02:17:07.377 --> 02:17:11.048
<i>He's here to fight
the seven-time world champion.</i>

2286
02:17:14.801 --> 02:17:16.010
<i>That made contact.</i>

2287
02:17:16.011 --> 02:17:20.264
<i>The leader and Lewis Hamilton
are out of this race.</i>

2288
02:17:20.265 --> 02:17:24.393
[Brundle] <i>Despite yellow flags flying
at turn one. this race will continue.</i>

2289
02:17:24.394 --> 02:17:26.854
[Hugh] <i>Sonny. push. push. push.
You're P1! You're P1!</i>

2290
02:17:27.397 --> 02:17:29.898
[Brundle] <i>Apex GP has only one lap to go.</i>

2291
02:17:29.899 --> 02:17:33.069
<i>The question is do they have the car?</i>

2292
02:17:33.654 --> 02:17:34.988
We have the driver.

2293
02:17:38.825 --> 02:17:41.078
[muffled] Yeah! Go on. Sonny!

2294
02:17:50.504 --> 02:17:52.213
[breathing heavily]

2295
02:18:26.247 --> 02:18:27.165
What's happening?

2296
02:18:27.916 --> 02:18:29.251
He's flying.

2297
02:18:54.400 --> 02:18:56.318
[Hugh] <i>Sonny. you did it! We won! We won!</i>

2298
02:18:56.319 --> 02:18:57.403
[crew cheering]

2299
02:18:57.404 --> 02:18:59.072
Yeah!

2300
02:19:03.869 --> 02:19:05.578
Yes!

2301
02:19:10.334 --> 02:19:11.334
Yeah!

2302
02:19:11.335 --> 02:19:13.128
[cheers]

2303
02:19:15.923 --> 02:19:17.048
We won!

2304
02:19:17.049 --> 02:19:20.010
- Yeah!
- [cheering continues]

2305
02:19:22.930 --> 02:19:23.971
Yeah!

2306
02:19:25.515 --> 02:19:26.808
We won!

2307
